    color: #202122;background-color: 
#fafafa;
    " about="#mwt1023" id="mwB9E">
<div class="quotebox-title " style="
        color: #202122;background-color: 
#fafafa; 
        color: #202060;
        ">Asked: Are there limits on your global power?</div>
<blockquote class="quotebox-quote  left-aligned " style="
    ">
<p><span style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:16px;"><span class="nowrap"><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span><span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span></span> Yeah, there is one thing. My own morality. My own mind. It's the only thing that can stop me. I don't need international law. I'm not looking to hurt people.</span></p>
</blockquote>
<div style="padding-bottom: 0; padding-top: 0.5em"><cite class="right-aligned" style="">—<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Donald Trump, January 7, 2026<sup about="#mwt1027" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYTimes_20260108_292-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYTimes_20260108"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYTimes_20260108-292"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYTimes_20260108-292" id="mwB9I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9Q">[</span>291<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9U">]</span></span></a></sup>
<br/><br/><i>New York Times</i> White House correspondents wrote that "Mr. Trump's assessment... was the most blunt acknowledgment yet of his worldview. At its core is the concept that national strength, rather than laws, treaties and conventions, should be the deciding factor as powers collide."<sup about="#mwt1030" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYTimes_20260108_292-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYTimes_20260108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYTimes_20260108-292" id="mwB9Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9g">[</span>291<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB9k">]</span></span></a></sup></cite></div>
</div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1032" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB9o" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"multiple image\n","href":"./Template:Multiple_image"},"params":{"total_width":{"wt":"450"},"image1":{"wt":"2025 Foreign views of the US.svg"},"caption1":{"wt":"A 2025 [[Pew Research Center]] study found that more than half in 19 of 24 countries surveyed, said they lack confidence in Trump&apos;s leadership of world affairs, with views about Trump differing sharply along ideological and partisan lines.&lt;ref name=Pew_20250611>{{#invoke:cite | web |last1=Wike |first1=Richard |last2=Poushter |first2=Jacob |last3=Silver |first3=Laura |last4=Fetterolf |first4=Janell |title=U.S. Image Declines in Many Nations Amid Low Confidence in Trump |url=https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2025/06/11/us-image-declines-in-many-nations-amid-low-confidence-in-trump/ |page=1 |publisher=Pew Research Center |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250612025845/https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2025/06/11/us-image-declines-in-many-nations-amid-low-confidence-in-trump/ |archive-date=June 12, 2025 |date=June 11, 2025 |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>"},"image2":{"wt":"2025 Rating of Biden 2024 and Trump 2025 - survey results.svg"},"caption2":{"wt":"Among 24 surveyed countries, Trump&apos;s 2025 ratings trailed those of Joe Biden&apos;s 2024 ratings by an average of twelve percentage points in world affairs, though Trump fared better among right-wing populist parties in Europe.&lt;ref name=Pew_20250611p3>{{#invoke:cite | web |last1=Wike |first1=Richard |last2=Poushter |first2=Jacob |last3=Silver |first3=Laura |last4=Fetterolf |first4=Janell |title=Comparing confidence in Trump and Biden\n |url=https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2025/06/11/confidence-in-trump/ |page=3 |publisher=Pew Research Center |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250612030348/https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2025/06/11/confidence-in-trump/ |archive-date=June 12, 2025 |date=June 11, 2025 |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1349637415/mw-parser-output/.tmulti" about="#mwt1033" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Multiple image/styles.css","wrapper":".tmulti"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="thumb tmulti floatright" about="#mwt1032"><div class="thumbinner multiimageinner" style="width:442px;max-width:442px"><div class="trow"><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:130px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Foreign_views_of_the_US.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Foreign_views_of_the_US.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/2025_Foreign_views_of_the_US.svg/250px-2025_Foreign_views_of_the_US.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/2025_Foreign_views_of_the_US.svg/500px-2025_Foreign_views_of_the_US.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1250" data-file-height="750" data-file-type="drawing" height="130" width="217" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">A 2025 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pew_Research_Center" title="Pew Research Center">Pew Research Center</a> study found that more than half in 19 of 24 countries surveyed, said they lack confidence in Trump's leadership of world affairs, with views about Trump differing sharply along ideological and partisan lines.<sup about="#mwt1036" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pew_20250611_293-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pew_20250611"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pew_20250611-293"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pew_20250611-293" id="mwB9s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB90">[</span>292<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB94">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:130px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Rating_of_Biden_2024_and_Trump_2025_-_survey_results.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2025_Rating_of_Biden_2024_and_Trump_2025_-_survey_results.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2025_Rating_of_Biden_2024_and_Trump_2025_-_survey_results.svg/250px-2025_Rating_of_Biden_2024_and_Trump_2025_-_survey_results.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/2025_Rating_of_Biden_2024_and_Trump_2025_-_survey_results.svg/500px-2025_Rating_of_Biden_2024_and_Trump_2025_-_survey_results.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1250" data-file-height="750" data-file-type="drawing" height="130" width="217" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">Among 24 surveyed countries, Trump's 2025 ratings trailed those of Joe Biden's 2024 ratings by an average of twelve percentage points in world affairs, though Trump fared better among right-wing populist parties in Europe.<sup about="#mwt1041" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pew_20250611p3_294-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pew_20250611p3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pew_20250611p3-294"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pew_20250611p3-294" id="mwB98"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-E">[</span>293<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-I">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div></div></div></div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1032"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_using_multiple_image_with_auto_scaled_images"/></span>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB-M"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20260623_European_confidence_in_Trump_-_survey.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB-Q"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20260623_European_confidence_in_Trump_-_survey.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/20260623_European_confidence_in_Trump_-_survey.svg/250px-20260623_European_confidence_in_Trump_-_survey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/20260623_European_confidence_in_Trump_-_survey.svg/500px-20260623_European_confidence_in_Trump_-_survey.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwB-U"/></a><figcaption id="mwB-Y">A 2026 survey of European respondents showed net negative views of Trump concerning world affairs.<sup about="#mwt1046" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Pew_20260623_295-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Pew_20260623"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Pew_20260623-295"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Pew_20260623-295" id="mwB-c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB-g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-k">[</span>294<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB-o">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwB-s"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:List_of_international_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump_during_his_second_presidency.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwB-w"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:List_of_international_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump_during_his_second_presidency.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump_during_his_second_presidency.svg/500px-List_of_international_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump_during_his_second_presidency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump_during_his_second_presidency.svg/960px-List_of_international_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump_during_his_second_presidency.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2754" data-file-height="1398" data-file-type="drawing" height="178" width="350" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1.4" id="mwB-0"/></a><figcaption id="mwB-4">As of July 2026, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_international_presidential_trips_made_by_Donald_Trump" title="List of international presidential trips made by Donald Trump" id="mwB-8">Trump has made 12 international trips</a> to 17 different countries during his second presidency.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwB_A">Trump's second term foreign policy has been described as a mixture of both <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperialism" title="Imperialism" id="mwB_E">imperialist</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expansionism" title="Expansionism" id="mwB_I">expansionist</a> policies.<sup about="#mwt1049" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-296" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-296"}}'><a href="#cite_note-296" id="mwB_M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_U">[</span>295<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1052" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-297" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-297"}}'><a href="#cite_note-297" id="mwB_c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_k">[</span>296<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1055" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-298" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-298"}}'><a href="#cite_note-298" id="mwB_s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB_w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_0">[</span>297<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB_4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1058" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-299" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-299"}}'><a href="#cite_note-299" id="mwB_8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAE">[</span>298<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAI">]</span></span></a></sup> He engaged in a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Realism_(international_relations)" title="Realism (international relations)" id="mwCAM">realist</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isolationist" title="Isolationist" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCAQ">isolationist</a> "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/America_First_(policy)" title="America First (policy)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCAU">America First</a>" foreign policy agenda.<sup about="#mwt1061" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Basu_2282025_300-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Basu 2282025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Basu_2282025-300"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Basu_2282025-300" id="mwCAY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAg">[</span>299<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1062" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Blaxland_2182025_301-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Blaxland 2182025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Blaxland_2182025-301" id="mwCAo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCAs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCAw">[</span>300<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCA0">]</span></span></a></sup> His administration favored <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_power" title="Hard power" id="mwCA4">hard power</a> to achieve foreign policy goals,<sup about="#mwt1065" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Baker_02022025_302-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Baker 02022025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Baker_02022025-302"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Baker_02022025-302" id="mwCA8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBE">[</span>301<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBI">]</span></span></a></sup> and dismantled or withdrew support from domestic and international organizations dedicated to advancing American <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_power" title="Soft power" id="mwCBM">soft power</a>.<sup about="#mwt1068" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hvistendahl_07232025_303-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hvistendahl 07232025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hvistendahl_07232025-303"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hvistendahl_07232025-303" id="mwCBQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBY">[</span>302<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1071" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-304" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-304"}}'><a href="#cite_note-304" id="mwCBg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCBk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBo">[</span>303<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCBs">]</span></span></a></sup> The moves were described as ceding American global influence and creating a void filled by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia" title="Russia" id="mwCBw">Russia</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwCB0">China</a>.<sup about="#mwt1074" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Hsu_06242025_305-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Hsu 06242025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hsu_06242025-305"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Hsu_06242025-305" id="mwCB4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCB8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCA">[</span>304<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCCI">His relations with allies were transactional and ranged from indifference to hostility, and he threatened them with economic tariffs or annexation.<sup about="#mwt1075" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Erlanger_2272025_306-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Erlanger 2272025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Erlanger_2272025-306" id="mwCCM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCU">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1076" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Broadwater_2272025_307-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Broadwater 2272025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Broadwater_2272025-307" id="mwCCc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCCg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCk">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCCo">]</span></span></a></sup> He was described as taking the side of Russia in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine" id="mwCCs">Russian invasion of Ukraine</a>,<sup about="#mwt1079" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Erlanger_2272025_306-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Erlanger 2272025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Erlanger_2272025-306"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Erlanger_2272025-306" id="mwCCw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCC0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCC4">[</span>305<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCC8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1082" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Broadwater_2272025_307-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Broadwater 2272025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Broadwater_2272025-307"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Broadwater_2272025-307" id="mwCDA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDI">[</span>306<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1085" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-308" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-308"}}'><a href="#cite_note-308" id="mwCDQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDY">[</span>307<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDc">]</span></span></a></sup> and overseeing a rupture of the post-1945 rules-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberal_international_order" title="Liberal international order" id="mwCDg">liberal international order</a> and abandonment of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multilateralism" title="Multilateralism" id="mwCDk">multilateralism</a>.<sup about="#mwt1088" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-309" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-309"}}'><a href="#cite_note-309" id="mwCDo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCDs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCDw">[</span>308<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCD0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1089" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Basu_2282025_300-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Basu 2282025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Basu_2282025-300" id="mwCD4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCD8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEA">[</span>299<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1092" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Blaxland_2182025_301-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Blaxland 2182025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Blaxland_2182025-301"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Blaxland_2182025-301" id="mwCEI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEQ">[</span>300<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCEY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Michael_Klare" title="Michael Klare" id="mwCEc">Michael Klare</a> wrote that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China–United_States_relations" title="China–United States relations" id="mwCEg">containing the influence of China</a> and preventing the rise of any rival power is the central foreign policy objective of the administration.<sup about="#mwt1095" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-310" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-310"}}'><a href="#cite_note-310" id="mwCEk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCEo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEs">[</span>309<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCEw">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump has attempted to deepen the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India–United_States_relations" title="India–United States relations" id="mwCE0">U.S.-India partnership</a>.<sup about="#mwt1098" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-311" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-311"}}'><a href="#cite_note-311" id="mwCE4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCE8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFA">[</span>310<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCFI">Trump's administration saw large drops in global public opinion of the U.S.<sup about="#mwt1101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Henley_06112025_312-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Henley 06112025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Henley_06112025-312"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Henley_06112025-312" id="mwCFM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFU">[</span>311<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFY">]</span></span></a></sup> Countries like Canada, Germany, the U.K., Denmark, and Finland warned their citizens about traveling to the U.S.<sup about="#mwt1104" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-313" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-313"}}'><a href="#cite_note-313" id="mwCFc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFk">[</span>312<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCFo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-314" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-314"}}'><a href="#cite_note-314" id="mwCFs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCFw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF0">[</span>313<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCF4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1110" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-315" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-315"}}'><a href="#cite_note-315" id="mwCF8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGE">[</span>314<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1113" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-316" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-316"}}'><a href="#cite_note-316" id="mwCGM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGU">[</span>315<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1116" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-317" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-317"}}'><a href="#cite_note-317" id="mwCGc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCGg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGk">[</span>316<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCGo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="47" id="mwCGs" aria-labelledby="Americas"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Americas">Americas</h3></div>
<p id="mwCGw">Trump's second presidency has been characterized by a renewed American interference in the internal affairs of Latin American nations. These efforts have included both threats and promises made to influence the outcomes of elections in Honduras, Chile and Argentina, as well as tariff threats against Brazil and Mexico and military action against Venezuela.<sup about="#mwt1119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-318" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-318"}}'><a href="#cite_note-318" id="mwCG0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCG4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCG8">[</span>317<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="48" id="mwCHE" aria-labelledby="Argentina"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Argentina">Argentina</h4></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCHI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_J._Trump_and_President_of_Argentina_Javier_Milei_on_October_14,_2025_(1).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCHM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_J._Trump_and_President_of_Argentina_Javier_Milei_on_October_14,_2025_(1).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/President_Donald_J._Trump_and_President_of_Argentina_Javier_Milei_on_October_14%2C_2025_%281%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_J._Trump_and_President_of_Argentina_Javier_Milei_on_October_14%2C_2025_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/President_Donald_J._Trump_and_President_of_Argentina_Javier_Milei_on_October_14%2C_2025_%281%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_J._Trump_and_President_of_Argentina_Javier_Milei_on_October_14%2C_2025_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2000" data-file-height="3000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="375" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCHQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwCHU">Trump with Argentina president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Javier_Milei" title="Javier Milei" id="mwCHY">Javier Milei</a> on October 14, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCHc">On October 20, the United States and Argentina agreed to a currency swap for up to $20 billion. About President Javier Milei of Argentina and his upcoming October 26 mid-term elections, President Trump said, "If he loses, we are not going to be generous with Argentina."<sup about="#mwt1122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Guardian,_$20bn_currency_swap_deal,_Oct_20_319-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Guardian, $20bn currency swap deal, Oct 20"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Guardian,_$20bn_currency_swap_deal,_Oct_20-319"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Guardian,_$20bn_currency_swap_deal,_Oct_20-319" id="mwCHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCHk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHo">[</span>318<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCHs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCHw">The Trump administration also announced plans to increase beef imports from Argentina. The National Cattlemen's Beef Association objected to this plan with their leader saying, "If President Trump is truly an ally of America's cattle producers, we call on him to abandon this effort to manipulate markets." On October 22, Trump posted on social media that American ranchers need to help get beef prices down, and said that ranchers "don't understand that the only reason they are doing so well, for the first time in decades, is because I put Tariffs on cattle coming into the United States, including a 50% Tariff on Brazil".<sup about="#mwt1125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_News,_Cattlemen's_trade_group,_Oct_23_320-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC News, Cattlemen&apos;s trade group, Oct 23"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_News,_Cattlemen&apos;s_trade_group,_Oct_23-320"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_News,_Cattlemen's_trade_group,_Oct_23-320" id="mwCH0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCH4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCH8">[</span>319<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="49" id="mwCIE" aria-labelledby="Boat_strikes"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Boat_strikes">Boat strikes</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1126" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCII" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"United States strikes on alleged drug traffickers during Operation Southern Spear"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1127" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1126" id="mwCIM">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_strikes_on_alleged_drug_traffickers_during_Operation_Southern_Spear" title="United States strikes on alleged drug traffickers during Operation Southern Spear">United States strikes on alleged drug traffickers during Operation Southern Spear</a></div>
<p id="mwCIQ">At Trump's direction, the United States has executed a series of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Airstrike" title="Airstrike" id="mwCIU">airstrikes</a> in the Caribbean Sea on vessels alleged to be smuggling illegal drugs. As of January 4, 2026, a total of 35 strikes have been conducted, in which 115 individuals have been killed and 2 have been rescued after surviving the strikes.<sup about="#mwt1130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-321" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-321"}}'><a href="#cite_note-321" id="mwCIY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIg">[</span>320<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIk">]</span></span></a></sup> Since the first strike, which was conducted on September 2, 2025, and killed eleven people, the Trump Administration has invoked combatting "terrorism" conducted by drug cartels as a justification for the strikes.<sup about="#mwt1133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-322" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-322"}}'><a href="#cite_note-322" id="mwCIo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCIs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCIw">[</span>321<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCI0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCI4">Many legal experts have argued that the strikes constitute illegal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extrajudicial_killing" title="Extrajudicial killing" id="mwCI8">extrajudicial killings</a> under both U.S. and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_law" title="International law" id="mwCJA">international law</a>, noting that drug smuggling is generally considered to be a crime, not an act of war, and that the military is categorically prohibited from targeting civilians, even suspected criminals, unless facing a threat of imminent harm.<sup about="#mwt1136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-323" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-323"}}'><a href="#cite_note-323" id="mwCJE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJM">[</span>322<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conservatism_in_the_United_States" title="Conservatism in the United States" id="mwCJU">Conservative</a> lawyer and commentator <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_C._McCarthy" title="Andrew C. McCarthy" id="mwCJY">Andrew C. McCarthy</a>, writing in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Review" title="National Review" id="mwCJc">National Review</a>, called the strikes "lawless" and "not legitimate under the law".<sup about="#mwt1139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-324" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-324"}}'><a href="#cite_note-324" id="mwCJg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJo">[</span>323<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCJs">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_Justice" title="United States Department of Justice" id="mwCJw">U.S. Department of Justice</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_of_Legal_Counsel" title="Office of Legal Counsel" id="mwCJ0">Office of Legal Counsel</a> defended the strikes in a memo that has not been released to the public, endorsing President Trump's claim that the United States is an armed conflict with Latin American drug cartels and arguing that the destruction of drug boats eliminates a source of revenue that could be used to purchase weapons for attacks against the United States.<sup about="#mwt1142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-325" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-325"}}'><a href="#cite_note-325" id="mwCJ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCJ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKA">[</span>324<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCKI">On November 27, <i id="mwCKM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Washington_Post" title="The Washington Post" id="mwCKQ">The Washington Post</a></i> published an article alleging that Secretary of Defense <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Hegseth" title="Pete Hegseth" id="mwCKU">Pete Hegseth</a> had ordered the officers responsible for the first airstrike on September 2, 2025, to "kill everyone" on board, prompting Admiral <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_M._Bradley" title="Frank M. Bradley" id="mwCKY">Frank M. Bradley</a> to order a second strike to kill the two survivors of the initial strike, who were clinging to the wreckage of the boat that had been by the initial strike.<sup about="#mwt1146" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-326" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-326"}}'><a href="#cite_note-326" id="mwCKc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCKg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKk">[</span>325<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCKo">]</span></span></a></sup> As <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_quarter" title="No quarter" id="mwCKs">no quarter</a> orders are forbidden under the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_of_war" title="Law of war" id="mwCKw">Law of war</a>, the second September 2 strike was widely criticized as constituting a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/War_crime" title="War crime" id="mwCK0">war crime</a> even under the Trump Administration's justification for the boat strike campaign in general, with the chair of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Senate_Committee_on_Armed_Services" title="United States Senate Committee on Armed Services" id="mwCK4">United States Senate Committee on Armed Services</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Party_(United_States)" title="Republican Party (United States)" id="mwCK8">Republican</a> Senator <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Wicker" title="Roger Wicker" id="mwCLA">Roger Wicker</a>, along with ranking member <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Reed_(Rhode_Island_politician)" title="Jack Reed (Rhode Island politician)" id="mwCLE">Jack Reed</a>, promising "vigorous oversight to determine the facts related to these circumstances".<sup about="#mwt1149" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-327" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-327"}}'><a href="#cite_note-327" id="mwCLI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLQ">[</span>326<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLU">]</span></span></a></sup> According to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwCLY">The New York Times</a>, five U.S. officials stated that while Hegseth did, on September 2, order the killing of all individuals aboard the alleged drug boat, he did not specifically address what was to be done if any individuals survived the initial strike and was not present when Bradley carried out the second strike.<sup about="#mwt1152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-328" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-328"}}'><a href="#cite_note-328" id="mwCLc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCLg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLk">[</span>327<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCLo">]</span></span></a></sup> After Hegseth refused to release a video of the second strike to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Congress" title="United States Congress" id="mwCLs">Congress</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Senate" title="United States Senate" id="mwCLw">United States Senate</a> placed a provision in the 2026 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Defense_Authorization_Act" title="National Defense Authorization Act" id="mwCL0">National Defense Authorization Act</a> holding back a quarter of Hegseth's travel budget until he showed the video to lawmakers.<sup about="#mwt1155" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-329" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-329"}}'><a href="#cite_note-329" id="mwCL4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCL8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCMA">[</span>328<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCME">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="50" id="mwCMI" aria-labelledby="Venezuela"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Venezuela">Venezuela</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1156" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCMM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2026 United States intervention in Venezuela"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1157" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1156" id="mwCMQ">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_intervention_in_Venezuela" title="2026 United States intervention in Venezuela">2026 United States intervention in Venezuela</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCMU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20260103MR-0139_President_Donald_Trump,_CIA_Director_John_Ratcliffe_and_Secretary_of_State_Marco_Rubio_monitor_U.S._military_operations_in_Venezuela.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCMY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20260103MR-0139_President_Donald_Trump,_CIA_Director_John_Ratcliffe_and_Secretary_of_State_Marco_Rubio_monitor_U.S._military_operations_in_Venezuela.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/P20260103MR-0139_President_Donald_Trump%2C_CIA_Director_John_Ratcliffe_and_Secretary_of_State_Marco_Rubio_monitor_U.S._military_operations_in_Venezuela.jpg/250px-P20260103MR-0139_President_Donald_Trump%2C_CIA_Director_John_Ratcliffe_and_Secretary_of_State_Marco_Rubio_monitor_U.S._military_operations_in_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/P20260103MR-0139_President_Donald_Trump%2C_CIA_Director_John_Ratcliffe_and_Secretary_of_State_Marco_Rubio_monitor_U.S._military_operations_in_Venezuela.jpg/500px-P20260103MR-0139_President_Donald_Trump%2C_CIA_Director_John_Ratcliffe_and_Secretary_of_State_Marco_Rubio_monitor_U.S._military_operations_in_Venezuela.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCMc"/></a><figcaption id="mwCMg">US president Donald Trump with members of his cabinet at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mar-a-Lago" title="Mar-a-Lago" id="mwCMk">Mar-a-Lago</a> during Operation Absolute Resolve</figcaption></figure> 
<p id="mwCMo">On January 3, 2026, the United States launched <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_intervention_in_Venezuela" title="2026 United States intervention in Venezuela" id="mwCMs">airstrikes</a> in Venezuela, capturing Venezuelan president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicolás_Maduro" title="Nicolás Maduro" id="mwCMw">Nicolás Maduro</a> and his wife,<sup about="#mwt1160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-330" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-330"}}'><a href="#cite_note-330" id="mwCM0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCM4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCM8">[</span>329<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNA">]</span></span></a></sup> and resulting in an estimated 80 casualties, including Maduro's personal guard, military personnel, and civilians.<sup about="#mwt1163" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-331" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-331"}}'><a href="#cite_note-331" id="mwCNE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNM">[</span>330<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The airstrike was done without congressional awareness or authorization, resulting in criticism from media and a number of congressmen.<sup about="#mwt1166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-332" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-332"}}'><a href="#cite_note-332" id="mwCNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNc">[</span>331<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNg">]</span></span></a></sup> Maduro and his wife were arraigned in a Manhattan federal court on 5, January 2026. Both pleaded not guilty to a number of drug trafficking charges.<sup about="#mwt1169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-333" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-333"}}'><a href="#cite_note-333" id="mwCNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNs">[</span>332<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCNw">]</span></span></a></sup> Followed by a purge of Maduro-era loyalists from the Venezuelan government, which was taken over by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Delcy_Rodríguez" title="Delcy Rodríguez" id="mwCN0">Delcy Rodríguez</a>.<sup about="#mwt1172" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-334" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-334"}}'><a href="#cite_note-334" id="mwCN4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCN8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOA">[</span>333<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOE">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2026, Venezuela has been a <i id="mwCOI">de facto</i> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Puppet_state" title="Puppet state" id="mwCOM">puppet state</a> of the United States. The Trump administration, primarily through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Secretary_of_State" title="U.S. Secretary of State" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCOQ">U.S. Secretary of State</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Rubio" title="Marco Rubio" id="mwCOU">Marco Rubio</a>, maintains control over its domestic finances, foreign policy, government appointments, revenues, and oil reserves.<sup about="#mwt1175" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYT_07112026_335-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYT 07112026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYT_07112026-335"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYT_07112026-335" id="mwCOY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOg">[</span>334<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1178" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Callaghan_01042026_336-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Callaghan 01042026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Callaghan_01042026-336"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Callaghan_01042026-336" id="mwCOo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCOs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCOw">[</span>335<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCO0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="51" id="mwCO4" aria-labelledby="Europe"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Europe">Europe</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCO8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_and_President_Alexander_Stubb.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCPA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_and_President_Alexander_Stubb.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/President_Donald_Trump_and_President_Alexander_Stubb.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_and_President_Alexander_Stubb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/President_Donald_Trump_and_President_Alexander_Stubb.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_and_President_Alexander_Stubb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1366" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCPE"/></a><figcaption id="mwCPI">Trump has emphasized good relations with Finland, especially with the "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Icebreaker" title="Icebreaker" id="mwCPM">icebreaker</a> trade" in October 2025.<sup about="#mwt1181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-337" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-337"}}'><a href="#cite_note-337" id="mwCPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPY">[</span>336<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1184" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-338" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-338"}}'><a href="#cite_note-338" id="mwCPg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCPk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPo">[</span>337<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCPs">]</span></span></a></sup> He met with Finnish president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Stubb" title="Alexander Stubb" id="mwCPw">Alexander Stubb</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oval_Office" title="Oval Office" id="mwCP0">Oval Office</a>.</figcaption></figure>

<section data-mw-section-id="52" id="mwCP4" aria-labelledby="NATO_spending"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="NATO_spending">NATO spending</h4></div>
<p id="mwCP8">The Trump administration has argued that European nations should contribute more to their own defense while the U.S. focuses on China.<sup about="#mwt1187" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TheWashingtonPost2024_339-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TheWashingtonPost2024"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TheWashingtonPost2024-339"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TheWashingtonPost2024-339" id="mwCQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQI">[</span>338<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQM">]</span></span></a></sup> During his 2024 campaign, he said he would not defend <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NATO" title="NATO" id="mwCQQ">NATO</a> allies if they did not meet the alliance's spending target of 2% of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GDP" title="GDP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCQU">GDP</a> on defense, and that he would "encourage" Russia to "do whatever the hell they want".<sup about="#mwt1191" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-340" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-340"}}'><a href="#cite_note-340" id="mwCQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQg">[</span>339<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1194" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-341" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-341"}}'><a href="#cite_note-341" id="mwCQo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQw">[</span>340<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCQ0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1197" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-342" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-342"}}'><a href="#cite_note-342" id="mwCQ4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCQ8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRA">[</span>341<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRE">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump officials privately expressed contempt for European "freeloading";.<sup about="#mwt1200" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-343" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-343"}}'><a href="#cite_note-343" id="mwCRI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRQ">[</span>342<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1203" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Smialek/NYT_344-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Smialek/NYT"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Smialek/NYT-344"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Smialek/NYT-344" id="mwCRY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRg">[</span>343<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCRk">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's policies and rhetoric accelerated an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020s_European_rearmament" title="2020s European rearmament" id="mwCRo">ongoing European rearmament</a>.<sup about="#mwt1206" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-345" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-345"}}'><a href="#cite_note-345" id="mwCRs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCRw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCR0">[</span>344<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCR4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1209" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-346" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-346"}}'><a href="#cite_note-346" id="mwCR8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSE">[</span>345<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1212" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-347" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-347"}}'><a href="#cite_note-347" id="mwCSM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSU">[</span>346<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1215" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-348" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-348"}}'><a href="#cite_note-348" id="mwCSc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSk">[</span>347<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCSo">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump called Poland, which exceeds the NATO defense spending target, "one of the best groups of people I have ever met".<sup about="#mwt1218" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-349" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-349"}}'><a href="#cite_note-349" id="mwCSs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCS0">[</span>348<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCS4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="53" id="mwCS8" aria-labelledby="Vice_President_JD_Vance"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Vice_President_JD_Vance">Vice President JD Vance</h4></div>
<p id="mwCTA">Trump's administration has also expressed cultural disagreement with Europe and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Union" title="European Union" id="mwCTE">European Union</a>: in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_JD_Vance_speech_at_the_Munich_Security_Conference" title="2025 JD Vance speech at the Munich Security Conference" id="mwCTI">a speech</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/61st_Munich_Security_Conference" title="61st Munich Security Conference" id="mwCTM">61st Munich Security Conference</a>, Vice President Vance criticized European policies on free speech and democratic values, and accused European leaders of suppressing dissenting views on issues such as immigration.<sup about="#mwt1219" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TheWashingtonPost2024_339-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TheWashingtonPost2024"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TheWashingtonPost2024-339" id="mwCTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTY">[</span>338<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1222" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-350" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-350"}}'><a href="#cite_note-350" id="mwCTg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCTk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTo">[</span>349<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCTs">]</span></span></a></sup> Vance also expressed support for lifting restrictions on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alternative_for_Germany" title="Alternative for Germany" id="mwCTw">Alternative for Germany</a>, a far-right German political party.<sup about="#mwt1225" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-351" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-351"}}'><a href="#cite_note-351" id="mwCT0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCT4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCT8">[</span>350<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCUA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="54" id="mwCUE" aria-labelledby="United_Kingdom"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="United_Kingdom">United Kingdom</h4></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCUI"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_meets_US_President_Donald_Trump_(54687372410).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCUM"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_meets_US_President_Donald_Trump_(54687372410).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_meets_US_President_Donald_Trump_%2854687372410%29.jpg/250px-Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_meets_US_President_Donald_Trump_%2854687372410%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_meets_US_President_Donald_Trump_%2854687372410%29.jpg/500px-Prime_Minister_Keir_Starmer_meets_US_President_Donald_Trump_%2854687372410%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5123" data-file-height="3415" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCUQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwCUU">Trump with British prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keir_Starmer" title="Keir Starmer" id="mwCUY">Keir Starmer</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turnberry,_South_Ayrshire" title="Turnberry, South Ayrshire" id="mwCUc">Turnberry</a>, Scotland, July 28, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCUg">While meeting with British prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keir_Starmer" title="Keir Starmer" id="mwCUk">Keir Starmer</a> in February 2025, Trump accepted a request from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles_III" title="Charles III" id="mwCUo">King Charles III</a> for a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visit" title="State visit" id="mwCUs">state visit</a> in the U.K.;<sup about="#mwt1228" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBCNews2025b_352-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBCNews2025b"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBCNews2025b-352"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBCNews2025b-352" id="mwCUw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCU0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCU4">[</span>351<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCU8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1231" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-353" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-353"}}'><a href="#cite_note-353" id="mwCVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVI">[</span>352<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVM">]</span></span></a></sup> both Trump and Starmer praised the U.S.–U.K. "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special_Relationship" title="Special Relationship" id="mwCVQ">Special Relationship</a>".<sup about="#mwt1232" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBCNews2025b_352-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBCNews2025b"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBCNews2025b-352" id="mwCVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVc">[</span>351<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVg">]</span></span></a></sup> The state visit <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_state_visit_by_Donald_Trump_to_the_United_Kingdom" title="2025 state visit by Donald Trump to the United Kingdom" id="mwCVk">occurred between September 16–18</a>, 2025.<sup about="#mwt1235" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBC4Sep2025_354-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBC4Sep2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBC4Sep2025-354"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBC4Sep2025-354" id="mwCVo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCVs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCVw">[</span>353<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCV0">]</span></span></a></sup> Relations became strained in March 2026 due to Starmer's refusal to join the U.S.–Israeli strikes on Iran during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war" title="2026 Iran war" id="mwCV4">2026 Iran war</a> or support the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_naval_blockade_of_Iran" title="2026 United States naval blockade of Iran" id="mwCV8">U.S. naval blockade of Iran</a>, prompting Trump to repeatedly condemn the prime minister.<sup about="#mwt1238" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-355" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-355"}}'><a href="#cite_note-355" id="mwCWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCWE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWI">[</span>354<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWM">]</span></span></a></sup> King Charles III undertook a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visit_by_Charles_III_to_the_United_States" title="State visit by Charles III to the United States" id="mwCWQ">state visit to the United States</a> between April 27–30, 2026 and addressed Congress, aimed partly at alleviating these tensions.<sup about="#mwt1241" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-356" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-356"}}'><a href="#cite_note-356" id="mwCWU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCWY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWc">[</span>355<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCWg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="55" id="mwCWk" aria-labelledby="Ukraine"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Ukraine">Ukraine</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1242" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCWo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Peace negotiations in the Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present)#Developments under the second Trump presidency (since 2025)"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1243" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1242" id="mwCWs">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_negotiations_in_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022–present)#Developments_under_the_second_Trump_presidency_(since_2025)" title="Peace negotiations in the Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present)">Peace negotiations in the Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present) §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Developments under the second Trump presidency (since 2025)</a></div>
<p id="mwCWw">Trump began a push for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_negotiations_in_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022–present)" title="Peace negotiations in the Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present)" id="mwCW0">peace negotiations</a> to end the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="Russian invasion of Ukraine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCW4">Russia–Ukraine war</a>.<sup about="#mwt1246" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-357" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-357"}}'><a href="#cite_note-357" id="mwCW8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCXA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXE">[</span>356<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXI">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's first foreign visit as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President-elect_of_the_United_States" title="President-elect of the United States" id="mwCXM">president-elect</a> was to Paris for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reopening_of_Notre-Dame_de_Paris" title="Reopening of Notre-Dame de Paris" id="mwCXQ">the reopening</a> of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame_de_Paris" title="Notre-Dame de Paris" id="mwCXU">Notre-Dame de Paris</a>, during which he met with French president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmanuel_Macron" title="Emmanuel Macron" id="mwCXY">Emmanuel Macron</a> and Ukrainian president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volodymyr_Zelenskyy" title="Volodymyr Zelenskyy" id="mwCXc">Volodymyr Zelenskyy</a> to discuss the war,<sup about="#mwt1249" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-358" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-358"}}'><a href="#cite_note-358" id="mwCXg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCXk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXo">[</span>357<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCXs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1252" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-359" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-359"}}'><a href="#cite_note-359" id="mwCXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCX0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCX4">[</span>358<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCX8">]</span></span></a></sup> and met with other European officials.<sup about="#mwt1255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-360" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-360"}}'><a href="#cite_note-360" id="mwCYA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYI">[</span>359<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-361" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-361"}}'><a href="#cite_note-361" id="mwCYQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYY">[</span>360<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYc">]</span></span></a></sup> In February 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_2025_Putin–Trump_phone_call" title="February 2025 Putin–Trump phone call" id="mwCYg">Trump held phone calls</a> with Russian president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin" title="Vladimir Putin" id="mwCYk">Vladimir Putin</a> and with Zelenskyy that he said marked the beginning of negotiations.<sup about="#mwt1261" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-guardian-20250212b2_362-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"guardian-20250212b2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-guardian-20250212b2-362"}}'><a href="#cite_note-guardian-20250212b2-362" id="mwCYo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCYs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCYw">[</span>361<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCY0">]</span></span></a></sup> He threatened Ukraine with a suspension of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_and_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="United States and the Russian invasion of Ukraine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCY4">U.S. military aid</a><sup about="#mwt1264" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-363" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-363"}}'><a href="#cite_note-363" id="mwCY8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZE">[</span>362<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZI">]</span></span></a></sup> and Russia with sanctions and tariffs if he decided they were not negotiating in good faith.<sup about="#mwt1267" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MoscowTimesJan2025_364-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MoscowTimesJan2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MoscowTimesJan2025-364"}}'><a href="#cite_note-MoscowTimesJan2025-364" id="mwCZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZU">[</span>363<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1270" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-365" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-365"}}'><a href="#cite_note-365" id="mwCZc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZk">[</span>364<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZo">]</span></span></a></sup> The U.S. sought a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukraine–United_States_Mineral_Resources_Agreement" title="Ukraine–United States Mineral Resources Agreement" id="mwCZs">mineral resources agreement with Ukraine</a><sup about="#mwt1273" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NBC_minerals2_366-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NBC minerals2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NBC_minerals2-366"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NBC_minerals2-366" id="mwCZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCZ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZ4">[</span>365<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCZ8">]</span></span></a></sup> though was unwilling to offer postwar security guarantees for Ukraine in exchange.<sup about="#mwt1274" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NBC_minerals2_366-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NBC minerals2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NBC_minerals2-366" id="mwCaA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCaE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCaI">[</span>365<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCaM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1277" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-367" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-367"}}'><a href="#cite_note-367" id="mwCaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCaU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCaY">[</span>366<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCac">]</span></span></a></sup> Negotiators reached a deal on the agreement<sup about="#mwt1280" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Tarasova-Markina_20250226_368-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Tarasova-Markina_20250226"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Tarasova-Markina_20250226-368"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Tarasova-Markina_20250226-368" id="mwCag"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCak"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCao">[</span>367<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCas">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1283" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNN_fulltext_20250225_369-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNN_fulltext_20250225"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CNN_fulltext_20250225-369"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNN_fulltext_20250225-369" id="mwCaw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCa0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCa4">[</span>368<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCa8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1286" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Butenko_20250226_370-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Butenko_20250226"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Butenko_20250226-370"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Butenko_20250226-370" id="mwCbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCbE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbI">[</span>369<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbM">]</span></span></a></sup> but the agreement fell through after <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Trump–Zelenskyy_Oval_Office_meeting" title="2025 Trump–Zelenskyy Oval Office meeting" id="mwCbQ">a contentious meeting between Trump and Zelenskyy</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oval_Office" title="Oval Office" id="mwCbU">Oval Office</a> that ended when the Ukrainian delegation was abruptly asked to leave.<sup about="#mwt1287" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBCNews2025b_352-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBCNews2025b"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBCNews2025b-352" id="mwCbY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCbc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbg">[</span>351<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1290" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Bennett2025_371-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Bennett2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bennett2025-371"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Bennett2025-371" id="mwCbo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCbs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCbw">[</span>370<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCb0">]</span></span></a></sup> Afterwards, the U.K. and France developed a proposal in which a "<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coalition_of_the_willing_(Russo-Ukrainian_War)" title="Coalition of the willing (Russo-Ukrainian War)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCb4">coalition of the willing</a>" would provide security guarantees to Ukraine.<sup about="#mwt1293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-372" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-372"}}'><a href="#cite_note-372" id="mwCb8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcE">[</span>371<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1296" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Deutsche_Welle_20250302_373-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Deutsche_Welle_20250302"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Deutsche_Welle_20250302-373"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Deutsche_Welle_20250302-373" id="mwCcM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcU">[</span>372<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcY">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/February_2025_United_States–Russia_summit_in_Saudi_Arabia" title="February 2025 United States–Russia summit in Saudi Arabia" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCcc">U.S. and Russia held a summit</a> in Saudi Arabia for peace talks in February<sup about="#mwt1299" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-374" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-374"}}'><a href="#cite_note-374" id="mwCcg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCck"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCco">[</span>373<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCcs">]</span></span></a></sup> and U.S. held a summit with Ukraine the next month, during which Ukraine accepted a U.S.-proposed 30-day ceasefire.<sup about="#mwt1302" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ravid2025_375-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ravid2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ravid2025-375"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ravid2025-375" id="mwCcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCc0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCc4">[</span>374<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCc8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1305" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-376" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-376"}}'><a href="#cite_note-376" id="mwCdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdI">[</span>375<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdM">]</span></span></a></sup> Putin did not accept the ceasefire,<sup about="#mwt1308" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-377" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-377"}}'><a href="#cite_note-377" id="mwCdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdY">[</span>376<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdc">]</span></span></a></sup> though on March 18 Russia agreed to a 30-day ceasefire only for strikes on energy infrastructure and in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Sea" title="Black Sea" id="mwCdg">Black Sea</a>,<sup about="#mwt1311" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-378" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-378"}}'><a href="#cite_note-378" id="mwCdk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCdo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCds">[</span>377<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCdw">]</span></span></a></sup> which Ukraine agreed to.<sup about="#mwt1314" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-InstitutefortheStudyofWar2025_379-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"InstitutefortheStudyofWar2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-InstitutefortheStudyofWar2025-379"}}'><a href="#cite_note-InstitutefortheStudyofWar2025-379" id="mwCd0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCd4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCd8">[</span>378<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1317" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBCNewsРусскаяслужба2025_380-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBCNewsРусскаяслужба2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBCNewsРусскаяслужба2025-380"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBCNewsРусскаяслужба2025-380" id="mwCeE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCeI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeM">[</span>379<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCeQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCeU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_bilateral_meeting_with_Ukrainian_president_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_P20250625DT-0727.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCeY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_bilateral_meeting_with_Ukrainian_president_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_P20250625DT-0727.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_bilateral_meeting_with_Ukrainian_president_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_P20250625DT-0727.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_bilateral_meeting_with_Ukrainian_president_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_P20250625DT-0727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_bilateral_meeting_with_Ukrainian_president_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_P20250625DT-0727.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_bilateral_meeting_with_Ukrainian_president_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_P20250625DT-0727.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCec"/></a><figcaption id="mwCeg">Trump and Ukrainian president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volodymyr_Zelenskyy" title="Volodymyr Zelenskyy" id="mwCek">Volodymyr Zelenskyy</a> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_The_Hague_NATO_summit" title="2025 The Hague NATO summit" id="mwCeo">NATO summit</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hague" title="The Hague" id="mwCes">The Hague</a>, June 25, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCew">On July 9, Trump reversed a previously suspended military aid package to Ukraine following Russia's largest aerial assault on the country, involving hundreds of drones and missiles. The suspension, reportedly authorized by senior defense officials without Trump's prior knowledge. Trump expressed growing frustration with Russian president Vladimir Putin, accusing him of insincerity and relentless aggression, saying, "He wants to go all the way, just keep killing people, it's no good." The U.S. are discussing sending 10 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIM-104_Patriot" title="MIM-104 Patriot" id="mwCe0">Patriot missiles</a> to Ukraine, and Trump said he is reviewing a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sanctioning_Russia_Act" title="Sanctioning Russia Act" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCe4">proposed sanctions bill</a> by Senator <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lindsey_Graham" title="Lindsey Graham" id="mwCe8">Lindsey Graham</a> that would impose 500% <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tariffs_in_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Tariffs in the second Trump administration" id="mwCfA">tariffs</a> on countries trading with Russia. Although Trump has previously mentioned <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secondary_sanctions" title="Secondary sanctions" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCfE">secondary sanctions</a>, none have been implemented so far, with the president citing their cost and waiting to see if a peace deal would emerge.<sup about="#mwt1320" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-381" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-381"}}'><a href="#cite_note-381" id="mwCfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfQ">[</span>380<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfU">]</span></span></a></sup> On July 14, 2025, Trump threatened to impose 100% tariffs and secondary sanctions on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Russian_oil_products_sanctions_and_price_cap" title="2023 Russian oil products sanctions and price cap" id="mwCfY">countries purchasing Russian oil</a> if Russia did not agree to a ceasefire within 50 days.<sup about="#mwt1323" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-382" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-382"}}'><a href="#cite_note-382" id="mwCfc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfk">[</span>381<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCfo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1326" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-383" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-383"}}'><a href="#cite_note-383" id="mwCfs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCf0">[</span>382<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCf4">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump confirmed a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Russia–United_States_Summit" title="2025 Russia–United States Summit" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCf8">summit meeting</a> between him and Putin to be held on August 15, 2025, in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alaska" title="Alaska" id="mwCgA">Alaska</a><sup about="#mwt1329" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-384" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-384"}}'><a href="#cite_note-384" id="mwCgE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgM">[</span>383<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The high-level summit at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joint_Base_Elmendorf–Richardson" title="Joint Base Elmendorf–Richardson" id="mwCgU">Joint Base Elmendorf–Richardson</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anchorage,_Alaska" title="Anchorage, Alaska" id="mwCgY">Anchorage</a> concluded without progress toward a ceasefire. Following the talks, Trump suggested the United States could assist Ukraine with surveillance flights or air defense support, while ruling out the deployment of ground troops.<sup about="#mwt1333" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-385" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-385"}}'><a href="#cite_note-385" id="mwCgc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgk">[</span>384<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCgo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1336" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-386" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-386"}}'><a href="#cite_note-386" id="mwCgs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCgw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCg0">[</span>385<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCg4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCg8"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250818DT-1089.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwChA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250818DT-1089.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/President_Donald_Trump_hosts_a_multilateral_meeting_with_President_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_of_Ukraine_and_European_leaders_%2854731808486%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_hosts_a_multilateral_meeting_with_President_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_of_Ukraine_and_European_leaders_%2854731808486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/President_Donald_Trump_hosts_a_multilateral_meeting_with_President_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_of_Ukraine_and_European_leaders_%2854731808486%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_hosts_a_multilateral_meeting_with_President_Volodymyr_Zelenskyy_of_Ukraine_and_European_leaders_%2854731808486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwChE"/></a><figcaption id="mwChI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/August_2025_White_House_multilateral_meeting_on_Ukraine" title="August 2025 White House multilateral meeting on Ukraine" id="mwChM">EU, NATO members and Zelenskyy in Washington, D.C.</a>, August 18, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwChQ">Trump emphasized that European nations should shoulder the primary burden of assistance and pressed Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelenskyy to take greater responsibility in securing peace. He further hinted that Ukraine may eventually face difficult choices, including potential territorial concessions, to bring the conflict to an end.<sup about="#mwt1339" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-387" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-387"}}'><a href="#cite_note-387" id="mwChU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwChY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChc">[</span>386<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwChg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwChk">In September 2025, Trump urged Europe to stop buying <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia_in_the_European_energy_sector" title="Russia in the European energy sector" id="mwCho">Russian oil</a> and start putting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China–European_Union_relations" title="China–European Union relations" id="mwChs">economic pressure on China</a> for funding Russia's war effort.<sup about="#mwt1342" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-388" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-388"}}'><a href="#cite_note-388" id="mwChw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCh0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCh4">[</span>387<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCh8">]</span></span></a></sup> Treasury Secretary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Bessent" title="Scott Bessent" id="mwCiA">Scott Bessent</a> said the Trump administration is "prepared to increase pressure on Russia, but we need our European partners to follow us".<sup about="#mwt1345" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-389" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-389"}}'><a href="#cite_note-389" id="mwCiE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCiI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiM">[</span>388<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCiQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCiU">In September 2025, the Trump administration approved the delivery of the first two packages of weapons to Ukraine from US stockpiles totalling approximately $1 billion, which would be paid for by NATO allies, under the new mechanism called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prioritized_Ukraine_Requirements_List" title="Prioritized Ukraine Requirements List" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCiY">Prioritized Ukraine Requirements List</a> (PURL). The mechanism aims to deliver aid worth up to $10 billion.<sup about="#mwt1348" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-390" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-390"}}'><a href="#cite_note-390" id="mwCic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCik">[</span>389<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCio">]</span></span></a></sup> On September 27, 2025, President Zelenskyy announced a $90 billion arms agreement with the United States in works.<sup about="#mwt1351" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-391" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-391"}}'><a href="#cite_note-391" id="mwCis"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCiw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCi0">[</span>390<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCi4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCi8">On October 22, 2025, the United States imposed sanctions on Russian energy companies <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosneft" title="Rosneft" id="mwCjA">Rosneft</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukoil" title="Lukoil" id="mwCjE">Lukoil</a>,<sup about="#mwt1354" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-392" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-392"}}'><a href="#cite_note-392" id="mwCjI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjQ">[</span>391<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjU">]</span></span></a></sup> affecting their customers in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_and_the_Russo-Ukrainian_War" title="China and the Russo-Ukrainian War" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCjY">China</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India_and_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="India and the Russian invasion of Ukraine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCjc">India</a>.<sup about="#mwt1357" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-393" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-393"}}'><a href="#cite_note-393" id="mwCjg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCjk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjo">[</span>392<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCjs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCjw">In November 2025, Trump proposed a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_negotiations_in_the_Russo-Ukrainian_war_(2022–present)#US_28-point_plan" title="Peace negotiations in the Russo-Ukrainian war (2022–present)" id="mwCj0">peace plan</a> that would require Ukraine to cede territory in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donbas" title="Donbas" id="mwCj4">Donbas</a>, including Ukrainian-controlled parts of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donetsk_Oblast" title="Donetsk Oblast" id="mwCj8">Donetsk Oblast</a>. The plan would also freeze the front lines in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kherson_Oblast" title="Kherson Oblast" id="mwCkA">Kherson Oblast</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaporizhzhia_Oblast" title="Zaporizhzhia Oblast" id="mwCkE">Zaporizhzhia Oblast</a>.<sup about="#mwt1360" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-394" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-394"}}'><a href="#cite_note-394" id="mwCkI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCkM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkQ">[</span>393<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCkU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="56" id="mwCkY" aria-labelledby="Africa"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Africa">Africa</h3></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="57" id="mwCkc" aria-labelledby="South_Africa"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="South_Africa">South Africa</h4></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCkg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_greets_President_of_South_Africa_Cyril_Ramaphosa_(54537936065).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCkk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_greets_President_of_South_Africa_Cyril_Ramaphosa_(54537936065).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/President_Donald_Trump_greets_President_of_South_Africa_Cyril_Ramaphosa_%2854537936065%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_President_of_South_Africa_Cyril_Ramaphosa_%2854537936065%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/President_Donald_Trump_greets_President_of_South_Africa_Cyril_Ramaphosa_%2854537936065%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_President_of_South_Africa_Cyril_Ramaphosa_%2854537936065%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCko"/></a><figcaption id="mwCks">Trump with South African president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyril_Ramaphosa" title="Cyril Ramaphosa" id="mwCkw">Cyril Ramaphosa</a> in May 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCk0">Trump's administration strained <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Africa–United_States_relations" title="South Africa–United States relations" id="mwCk4">relations with South Africa</a>. Trump suspended all aid to South Africa, saying the country's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expropriation_Act,_2024" title="Expropriation Act, 2024" id="mwCk8">land expropriation law</a> discriminated against <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afrikaners" title="Afrikaners" id="mwClA">Afrikaners</a>;<sup about="#mwt1363" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TheWhiteHouse2025_395-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TheWhiteHouse2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-TheWhiteHouse2025-395"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TheWhiteHouse2025-395" id="mwClE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClM">[</span>394<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClQ">]</span></span></a></sup> he also offered Afrikaners refugee status in the U.S.<sup about="#mwt1364" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TheWashingtonPost2024_339-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TheWashingtonPost2024"}}'><a href="#cite_note-TheWashingtonPost2024-339" id="mwClU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClc">[</span>338<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1367" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-guard-12may2025_396-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"guard-12may2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-guard-12may2025-396"}}'><a href="#cite_note-guard-12may2025-396" id="mwClk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwClo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCls">[</span>395<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwClw">]</span></span></a></sup> Rubio refused to attend the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_G20_Johannesburg_Summit" title="2025 G20 Johannesburg Summit" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCl0">G20 foreign ministers' meeting in Johannesburg</a><sup about="#mwt1370" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AlJazeeraEnglish2025_397-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AlJazeeraEnglish2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AlJazeeraEnglish2025-397"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AlJazeeraEnglish2025-397" id="mwCl4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCl8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmA">[</span>396<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmE">]</span></span></a></sup> and he declared the South African ambassador <i id="mwCmI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persona_non_grata" title="Persona non grata" id="mwCmM">persona non grata</a></i> for his criticism of U.S. policies.<sup about="#mwt1373" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Politico2025_398-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Politico2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Politico2025-398"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Politico2025-398" id="mwCmQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCmU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmY">[</span>397<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCmc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="58" id="mwCmg" aria-labelledby="Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo_and_Rwanda"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo_and_Rwanda">Democratic Republic of the Congo and Rwanda</h4></div>
<p id="mwCmk">Rubio condemned the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rwanda" title="Rwanda" id="mwCmo">Rwandan</a>-backed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Goma_offensive" title="2025 Goma offensive" id="mwCms">Goma offensive</a> in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo" title="Democratic Republic of the Congo" id="mwCmw">Democratic Republic of the Congo</a> and called for an immediate ceasefire and respect for territorial integrity.<sup about="#mwt1376" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-399" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-399"}}'><a href="#cite_note-399" id="mwCm0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCm4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCm8">[</span>398<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCnA">]</span></span></a></sup> In April, U.S. officials entered into talks with the DRC on a minerals deal after a proposal from Congolese president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Félix_Tshisekedi" title="Félix Tshisekedi" id="mwCnE">Félix Tshisekedi</a>.<sup about="#mwt1379" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-400" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-400"}}'><a href="#cite_note-400" id="mwCnI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCnM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCnQ">[</span>399<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCnU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCnY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Secretary_Rubio_Hosts_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo-Rwanda_Peace_Agreement_(54618044678).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCnc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Secretary_Rubio_Hosts_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo-Rwanda_Peace_Agreement_(54618044678).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Secretary_Rubio_Hosts_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo-Rwanda_Peace_Agreement_%2854618044678%29.jpg/250px-Secretary_Rubio_Hosts_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo-Rwanda_Peace_Agreement_%2854618044678%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Secretary_Rubio_Hosts_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo-Rwanda_Peace_Agreement_%2854618044678%29.jpg/500px-Secretary_Rubio_Hosts_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo-Rwanda_Peace_Agreement_%2854618044678%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2810" data-file-height="1878" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCng"/></a><figcaption id="mwCnk">Signing ceremony for the peace agreement, Washington, D.C., June 27, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCno">In June 2025, President Trump brokered a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Democratic_Republic_of_the_Congo–Rwanda_peace_agreement" title="2025 Democratic Republic of the Congo–Rwanda peace agreement" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCns">peace deal between the Democratic Republic of Congo and Rwanda</a>, with the U.S. getting "a lot of mineral rights". This potentially brings to an end a 30+ year conflict dating back to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rwandan_genocide" title="Rwandan genocide" id="mwCnw">1994 Rwanda genocide</a>. Each country had accused the other of financing and supporting rebel groups. On June 27, in a deal signed in the White House, each country pledged to end such support, allow the return of refugees, and create a joint security coordination mechanism aimed at resolving disputes.<sup about="#mwt1380" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC,_Trump_heralds_US-brokered_peace_deal,_June_27,_2025_401-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC, Trump heralds US-brokered peace deal, June 27, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC,_Trump_heralds_US-brokered_peace_deal,_June_27,_2025-401" id="mwCn0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCn4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCn8">[</span>400<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCoA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCoE">An estimated 6 million persons have died in this conflict, and Trump said that this deal ends "one of the worst wars anyone's ever seen". A critic said, "It risks reducing peace to a transactional exchange. Minerals are only one driver of conflict." Secretary of State Marco Rubio said, "This is an important moment after 30 years of war. President Trump is a president of peace. He really does want peace. He prioritizes it above all else."<sup about="#mwt1383" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC,_Trump_heralds_US-brokered_peace_deal,_June_27,_2025_401-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC, Trump heralds US-brokered peace deal, June 27, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC,_Trump_heralds_US-brokered_peace_deal,_June_27,_2025-401"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC,_Trump_heralds_US-brokered_peace_deal,_June_27,_2025-401" id="mwCoI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCoM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCoQ">[</span>400<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCoU">]</span></span></a></sup> A former prime minister of the DR Congo, Joseph Kabila, expressed skepticism of the peace deal, saying that it was "nothing more than a trade agreement".<sup about="#mwt1386" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBC,_DR_Congo-Rwanda_peace_deal,_June_28,_2025_402-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBC, DR Congo-Rwanda peace deal, June 28, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBC,_DR_Congo-Rwanda_peace_deal,_June_28,_2025-402"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBC,_DR_Congo-Rwanda_peace_deal,_June_28,_2025-402" id="mwCoY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCoc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCog">[</span>401<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCok">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="59" id="mwCoo" aria-labelledby="South_Sudan"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="South_Sudan">South Sudan</h4></div>
<p id="mwCos">In April 2025, the U.S. revoked all visas of and barred entry to citizens of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Sudan" title="South Sudan" id="mwCow">South Sudan</a> after a dispute over the deportation of a South Sudanese citizen.<sup about="#mwt1389" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Guardian_Apr_6,_20252_403-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Guardian Apr 6, 20252"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Guardian_Apr_6,_20252-403"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Guardian_Apr_6,_20252-403" id="mwCo0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCo4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCo8">[</span>402<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCpA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="60" id="mwCpE" aria-labelledby="Asia"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Asia">Asia</h3></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="61" id="mwCpI" aria-labelledby="Middle_East_2"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Middle_East_2">Middle East</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1390" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCpM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025–2026 Iran–United States negotiations"},"2":{"wt":"March–May 2025 United States attacks in Yemen"},"3":{"wt":"Twelve-Day War"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1391" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1390" id="mwCpQ">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025–2026_Iran–United_States_negotiations" title="2025–2026 Iran–United States negotiations">2025–2026 Iran–United States negotiations</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March–May_2025_United_States_attacks_in_Yemen" title="March–May 2025 United States attacks in Yemen">March–May 2025 United States attacks in Yemen</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twelve-Day_War" title="Twelve-Day War">Twelve-Day War</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCpU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_multilateral_meeting_with_Arab_and_Muslim_leaders_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_(54822741907).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCpY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_multilateral_meeting_with_Arab_and_Muslim_leaders_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_(54822741907).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_multilateral_meeting_with_Arab_and_Muslim_leaders_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_%2854822741907%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_multilateral_meeting_with_Arab_and_Muslim_leaders_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_%2854822741907%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_multilateral_meeting_with_Arab_and_Muslim_leaders_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_%2854822741907%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_participates_in_a_multilateral_meeting_with_Arab_and_Muslim_leaders_at_the_United_Nations_Headquarters_%2854822741907%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="1926" data-file-type="bitmap" height="161" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCpc"/></a><figcaption id="mwCpg">Trump with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recep_Tayyip_Erdoğan" title="Recep Tayyip Erdoğan" id="mwCpk">Recep Tayyip Erdoğan</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prabowo_Subianto" title="Prabowo Subianto" id="mwCpo">Prabowo Subianto</a>, and other Muslim leaders at a multilateral meeting at the United Nations, September 23, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<section data-mw-section-id="62" id="mwCps" aria-labelledby="Houthis"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading5"><h5 id="Houthis">Houthis</h5></div>
<p id="mwCpw">In March 2025, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March–May_2025_United_States_attacks_in_Yemen" title="March–May 2025 United States attacks in Yemen" id="mwCp0">U.S. began a series of airstrikes</a> on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Houthis" title="Houthis" id="mwCp4">Houthi</a> targets in Yemen to counter <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Sea_crisis" title="Red Sea crisis" id="mwCp8">attacks on Red Sea shipping</a>, with the goal of restoring freedom of navigation and deterring further aggression.<sup about="#mwt1394" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-404" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-404"}}'><a href="#cite_note-404" id="mwCqA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCqE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCqI">[</span>403<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCqM">]</span></span></a></sup> U.S. officials accidentally included <i id="mwCqQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atlantic" title="The Atlantic" id="mwCqU">The Atlantic</a></i> editor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeffrey_Goldberg" title="Jeffrey Goldberg" id="mwCqY">Jeffrey Goldberg</a> in a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Signal_(software)" title="Signal (software)" id="mwCqc">Signal</a> group chat discussing the military plans, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_government_group_chat_leak" title="United States government group chat leak" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCqg">sparking a political scandal</a> and accusations of risking national security and violating records-preservation laws.<sup about="#mwt1397" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-405" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-405"}}'><a href="#cite_note-405" id="mwCqk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCqo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCqs">[</span>404<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCqw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1400" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-406" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-406"}}'><a href="#cite_note-406" id="mwCq0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCq4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCq8">[</span>405<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1403" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-407" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-407"}}'><a href="#cite_note-407" id="mwCrE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCrI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrM">[</span>406<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCrU">In May 2025, Trump announced that his administration had reached a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ceasefire" title="Ceasefire" id="mwCrY">ceasefire</a> deal with the Houthis.<sup about="#mwt1406" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-408" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-408"}}'><a href="#cite_note-408" id="mwCrc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCrg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCrk">[</span>407<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCro">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="63" id="mwCrs" aria-labelledby="Iran"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading5"><h5 id="Iran">Iran</h5></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1407" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCrw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Iran–United States relations during the second Trump administration"},"2":{"wt":"2026 Iran war"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1408" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1407" id="mwCr0">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran–United_States_relations_during_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Iran–United States relations during the second Trump administration">Iran–United States relations during the second Trump administration</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war" title="2026 Iran war">2026 Iran war</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCr4"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Trump_situation_room_6-21-25.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCr8"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Trump_situation_room_6-21-25.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/President_Donald_Trump_and_his_national_security_team_meet_in_the_Situation_Room_of_the_White_House_%2854607926187%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_and_his_national_security_team_meet_in_the_Situation_Room_of_the_White_House_%2854607926187%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/President_Donald_Trump_and_his_national_security_team_meet_in_the_Situation_Room_of_the_White_House_%2854607926187%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_and_his_national_security_team_meet_in_the_Situation_Room_of_the_White_House_%2854607926187%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCsA"/></a><figcaption id="mwCsE">Trump and Vance in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Situation_Room" title="Situation Room" id="mwCsI">Situation Room</a> during <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States_strikes_on_Iranian_nuclear_sites" title="2025 United States strikes on Iranian nuclear sites" id="mwCsM">strikes on Iran</a></figcaption></figure>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1409" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwCsQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"multiple image ","href":"./Template:Multiple_image"},"params":{"total_width":{"wt":"450"},"image1":{"wt":"2021- Retail price of gasoline (US).svg"},"caption1":{"wt":"The retail price of gasoline in the US increased at the outbreak of war in Iran.&lt;ref name=EIAgasPrices>Data from {{#invoke:cite | web |title=Petroleum &amp; Other Liquids / Data / Weekly U.S. All Grades All Formulations Retail Gasoline Prices |url=https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/LeafHandler.ashx?n=pet&amp;s=emm_epm0_pte_nus_dpg&amp;f=w |publisher=U.S. Energy Information Administration |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260508185722/https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/LeafHandler.ashx?n=pet&amp;s=emm_epm0_pte_nus_dpg&amp;f=w |archive-date=8 May 2026 |date=2026 |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref name=NYTimes_20260420>{{#invoke:cite | news |last1=DePillis |first1=Lydia |title=Why Gas Prices Go Up Fast and Take So Long to Fall |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/20/business/economy/gas-stations-pricing.html |newspaper=The New York Times |date=April 20, 2026 |quote=Source: AAA for national average unleaded retail gasoline prices.}}&lt;/ref> In late April 2026, Trump said Americans should expect higher gas prices for \"a little while\".&lt;ref>{{#invoke:cite | news |last1=Breuninger |first1=Kevin |title=Trump says Americans should expect higher gas prices for &apos;a little while&apos; |url=https://www.cnbc.com/2026/04/23/trump-iran-war-gas-prices-strait-of-hormuz.html |agency=CNBC |date=April 23, 2026}}&lt;/ref>"},"image2":{"wt":"2021- Retail price of diesel fuel (US).svg"},"caption2":{"wt":"The retail price of diesel fuel in the US increased at the outbreak of war in Ukraine and Iran.&lt;ref name=EIA_diesel>{{cite web |title=Petroleum &amp; Other Liquids / Browse Data / Weekly U.S. No 2 Diesel Retail Prices (Dollars per Gallon) |url=https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/LeafHandler.ashx?n=PET&amp;s=EMD_EPD2D_PTE_NUS_DPG&amp;f=W |publisher=U.S. Energy Information Administration (EIA) |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260916163538/https://www.eia.gov/dnav/pet/hist/LeafHandler.ashx?n=PET&amp;s=EMD_EPD2D_PTE_NUS_DPG&amp;f=W |archive-date=16 September 2026 |date=2026 |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1349637415/mw-parser-output/.tmulti" about="#mwt1410" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Multiple image/styles.css","wrapper":".tmulti"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="thumb tmulti floatright" about="#mwt1409"><div class="thumbinner multiimageinner" style="width:442px;max-width:442px"><div class="trow"><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:122px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2021-_Retail_price_of_gasoline_(US).svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2021-_Retail_price_of_gasoline_(US).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/2021-_Retail_price_of_gasoline_%28US%29.svg/250px-2021-_Retail_price_of_gasoline_%28US%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/2021-_Retail_price_of_gasoline_%28US%29.svg/500px-2021-_Retail_price_of_gasoline_%28US%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="122" width="217" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">The retail price of gasoline in the US increased at the outbreak of war in Iran.<sup about="#mwt1413" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EIAgasPrices_409-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EIAgasPrices"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-EIAgasPrices-409"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EIAgasPrices-409" id="mwCsU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCsY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsc">[</span>408<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1418" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYTimes_20260420_410-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYTimes_20260420"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYTimes_20260420-410"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYTimes_20260420-410" id="mwCsk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCso"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCss">[</span>409<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCsw">]</span></span></a></sup> In late April 2026, Trump said Americans should expect higher gas prices for "a little while".<sup about="#mwt1423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-411" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-411"}}'><a href="#cite_note-411" id="mwCs0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCs4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCs8">[</span>410<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtA">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:122px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2021-_Retail_price_of_diesel_fuel_(US).svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2021-_Retail_price_of_diesel_fuel_(US).svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/2021-_Retail_price_of_diesel_fuel_%28US%29.svg/250px-2021-_Retail_price_of_diesel_fuel_%28US%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/2021-_Retail_price_of_diesel_fuel_%28US%29.svg/500px-2021-_Retail_price_of_diesel_fuel_%28US%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="122" width="217" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">The retail price of diesel fuel in the US increased at the outbreak of war in Ukraine and Iran.<sup about="#mwt1428" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-EIA_diesel_412-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"EIA_diesel"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-EIA_diesel-412"}}'><a href="#cite_note-EIA_diesel-412" id="mwCtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtM">[</span>411<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtQ">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div></div></div></div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1409"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_using_multiple_image_with_auto_scaled_images"/></span>
<p id="mwCtU">Trump reinstated his <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maximum_pressure_campaign" title="Maximum pressure campaign" id="mwCtY">"maximum pressure" campaign</a> against Iran and sought <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025–2026_Iran–United_States_negotiations" title="2025–2026 Iran–United States negotiations" id="mwCtc">a new set of negotiations</a> to limit <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_program_of_Iran" title="Nuclear program of Iran" id="mwCtg">Iran's nuclear program</a>.<sup about="#mwt1433" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-413" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-413"}}'><a href="#cite_note-413" id="mwCtk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCto"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCts">[</span>412<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCtw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1436" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-414" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-414"}}'><a href="#cite_note-414" id="mwCt0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCt4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCt8">[</span>413<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuA">]</span></span></a></sup> In March 2025, Trump sent a letter to Iranian supreme leader <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei" title="Ali Khamenei" id="mwCuE">Ali Khamenei</a> urging new negotiations and warning of military action if talks fail.<sup about="#mwt1439" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-415" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-415"}}'><a href="#cite_note-415" id="mwCuI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuQ">[</span>414<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1442" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-416" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-416"}}'><a href="#cite_note-416" id="mwCuY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCuc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCug">[</span>415<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1445" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-417" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-417"}}'><a href="#cite_note-417" id="mwCuo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCus"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCuw">[</span>416<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCu0">]</span></span></a></sup> On June 13, 2025, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twelve-Day_War" title="Twelve-Day War" id="mwCu4">Israeli planes bombed sites in Iran</a> associated with Iran's nuclear program. President Trump stated he was not involved, although Iranian leaders have said they do not believe this. There have been reports that Trump vetoed a plan to kill Iran's Ayatollah Khamenei, and that the United States communicated to Israel that Iran has not killed an American and discussions of killing political leaders should not be on the table.<sup about="#mwt1448" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_News,_Israel-Iran_live_updates,_June_15,_2025_418-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC News, Israel-Iran live updates, June 15, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_News,_Israel-Iran_live_updates,_June_15,_2025-418"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_News,_Israel-Iran_live_updates,_June_15,_2025-418" id="mwCu8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvE">[</span>417<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCvM">On June 21, 2025, the U.S. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States_strikes_on_Iranian_nuclear_sites" title="2025 United States strikes on Iranian nuclear sites" id="mwCvQ">attacked three nuclear sites</a>: the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fordow_Fuel_Enrichment_Plant" title="Fordow Fuel Enrichment Plant" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCvU">Fordow</a> uranium enrichment facility, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natanz_Nuclear_Facility" title="Natanz Nuclear Facility" id="mwCvY">Natanz</a> nuclear facility, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isfahan" title="Isfahan" id="mwCvc">Isfahan</a> nuclear technology center.<sup about="#mwt1451" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-419" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-419"}}'><a href="#cite_note-419" id="mwCvg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCvk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvo">[</span>418<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCvs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1454" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-420" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-420"}}'><a href="#cite_note-420" id="mwCvw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCv0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCv4">[</span>419<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCv8">]</span></span></a></sup> B-2 airplanes took off from the state of Missouri and made the 18-hour flight to Iran, being refueled multiple times en route. Entering Iranian airspace, fighter jets cleared space ahead of them, and a Navy sub fired more than 24 Tomahawk missiles. The leading B-2 dropped two Massive Ordnance Penetrators bombs (MOPs, or "bunker-busters") at the Fordo site. A total of 14 MOPs were dropped at two target sites. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Hegseth" title="Pete Hegseth" id="mwCwA">Secretary of Defense Pete Hegseth</a> said, "We devastated the Iranian nuclear program, but it's worth noting that the operation did not target Iranian troops or the Iranian people."<sup about="#mwt1457" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-421" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-421"}}'><a href="#cite_note-421" id="mwCwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwM">[</span>420<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On June 22, Trump said that since the Islamic regime in control of Iran has failed to make Iran great, it should be replaced to "Make Iran Great Again".<sup about="#mwt1460" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Guzman2025_422-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Guzman2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Guzman2025-422"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Guzman2025-422" id="mwCwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwc">[</span>421<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCwg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1463" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-423" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-423"}}'><a href="#cite_note-423" id="mwCwk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCwo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCws">[</span>422<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCww">]</span></span></a></sup> Later, he posted on social media that their constant anger, hostility, and despair have only led them to ruin. The path they're on offers no hope, only more hardship, "I wish the leadership of Iran would realize that you often get more with honey than you do with vinegar".<sup about="#mwt1466" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-424" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-424"}}'><a href="#cite_note-424" id="mwCw0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCw8">[</span>423<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwCxE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_(3).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwCxI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_(3).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_%283%29.jpg/250px-Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_%283%29.jpg/500px-Shajareh_Tayyebeh_school_in_Minab_photos_from_Mehr_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="5504" data-file-height="3680" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwCxM"/></a><figcaption id="mwCxQ">Rescuers and residents at the site of the Shajareh Tayyebeh girls' school in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minab" title="Minab" id="mwCxU">Minab</a>, Iran, which was destroyed by a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Minab_school_attack" title="2026 Minab school attack" id="mwCxY">U.S. military strike</a> on February 28, 2026</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwCxc">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025–2026_Iranian_protests" title="2025–2026 Iranian protests" id="mwCxg">2025–2026 Iranian protests</a>, Trump repeatedly warned the Iranian authorities that the U.S. would "intervene" if the regime did not halt its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_massacres" title="2026 Iran massacres" class="mw-redirect" id="mwCxk">crackdown on protesters</a>.<sup about="#mwt1469" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-425" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-425"}}'><a href="#cite_note-425" id="mwCxo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCxs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCxw">[</span>424<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCx0">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 16, 2026, Trump announced that the Iranian leadership had reportedly canceled over 800 planned executions.<sup about="#mwt1472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-426" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-426"}}'><a href="#cite_note-426" id="mwCx4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCx8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyA">[</span>425<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyE">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 28, 2026, Trump launched a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war" title="2026 Iran war" id="mwCyI">major attack on Iran</a> with Israel with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regime_change_efforts_in_the_2026_Iran_war" title="Regime change efforts in the 2026 Iran war" id="mwCyM">stated goal of regime change</a>.<sup about="#mwt1475" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-427" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-427"}}'><a href="#cite_note-427" id="mwCyQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCyU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyY">[</span>426<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyc">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 21, 2026, Trump announced a 48-hour ultimatum on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truth_Social" title="Truth Social" id="mwCyg">Truth Social</a> calling for Iran to open the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strait_of_Hormuz" title="Strait of Hormuz" id="mwCyk">Strait of Hormuz</a>, threatening the destruction of Iranian power infrastructure.<sup about="#mwt1478" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-428" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-428"}}'><a href="#cite_note-428" id="mwCyo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCys"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCyw">[</span>427<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCy0">]</span></span></a></sup> Over the following week, specifically on March 23 and 26, Trump announced two different extensions to the ultimatum. On March 26, an official pause on "the period of Energy Plant destruction" until April 2, 2026, was announced on social media,<sup about="#mwt1481" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-429" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-429"}}'><a href="#cite_note-429" id="mwCy4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCy8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzA">[</span>428<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzE">]</span></span></a></sup> an extension he later stated was a result of Iran allowing oil-carrying ships to safely pass through the Strait of Hormuz.<sup about="#mwt1484" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABCNews2026_430-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABCNews2026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABCNews2026-430"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABCNews2026-430" id="mwCzI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzQ">[</span>429<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwCzY">On April 4 and 5, 2026, Trump resumed posting threats of US attack on Iranian infrastructure, stating April 7, 2026, as the deadline for the Strait of Hormuz to be opened.<sup about="#mwt1485" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABCNews2026_430-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABCNews2026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABCNews2026-430" id="mwCzc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzk">[</span>429<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCzo">]</span></span></a></sup> On April 7, Trump posted to Truth Social that "a whole civilization will die tonight, never to be brought back again",<sup about="#mwt1488" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-431" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-431"}}'><a href="#cite_note-431" id="mwCzs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCzw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCz0">[</span>430<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwCz4">]</span></span></a></sup> causing domestic concern that Trump would use nuclear weapons, and resulting in a number of bipartisan calls for the 25th Amendment to be invoked.<sup about="#mwt1491" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-432" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-432"}}'><a href="#cite_note-432" id="mwCz8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0E">[</span>431<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0I">]</span></span></a></sup> The White House confirmed in an official statement that there is currently no consideration of usage of nuclear weaponry.<sup about="#mwt1495" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-433" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-433"}}'><a href="#cite_note-433" id="mwC0M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0U">[</span>432<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0Y">]</span></span></a></sup> Following the failure of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamabad_Talks" title="Islamabad Talks" id="mwC0c">Islamabad Talks</a> to end the war, Trump imposed a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_United_States_naval_blockade_of_Iran" title="2026 United States naval blockade of Iran" id="mwC0g">naval blockade on Iran</a> on April 13.<sup about="#mwt1498" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-434" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-434"}}'><a href="#cite_note-434" id="mwC0k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC0o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0s">[</span>433<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC0w">]</span></span></a></sup> In June 2026, after concluding that continued hostilities would risk economic calamity,<sup about="#mwt1501" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-graunr_435-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"graunr"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-graunr-435"}}'><a href="#cite_note-graunr-435" id="mwC00"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC04"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC08">[</span>434<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1A">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump signed a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamabad_Memorandum" title="Islamabad Memorandum" id="mwC1E">Memorandum of Understanding</a> (MOU) on behalf of the United States during a ceremony at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palace_of_Versailles" title="Palace of Versailles" id="mwC1I">Palace of Versailles</a> on 17 June 2026.<sup about="#mwt1502" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-graunr_435-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"graunr"}}'><a href="#cite_note-graunr-435" id="mwC1M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1U">[</span>434<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1Y">]</span></span></a></sup> According to a report by the <i id="mwC1c">Wall Street Journal</i>, Trump was initially pleased how the Iran war was going, notably after the killing of Ali Khamenei. However, with increase in fuel prices and a stalemate in the war, leaders from Saudi Arabia and Qatar pushed the US government for a diplomatic solution, while nearly 80% of Americans, according to polls, favored an agreement to end the war, prompting Trump to pursue the June truce.<sup about="#mwt1505" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-436" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-436"}}'><a href="#cite_note-436" id="mwC1g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC1k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1o">[</span>435<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC1s">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC1w">In September 2026, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UN" title="UN" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC10">UN</a>-commissioned fact-finding mission panel found "reasonable grounds" to believe that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mwC14">United States</a> had committed war crimes during military strikes in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran" title="Iran" id="mwC18">Iran</a> during the 2026 Iran war. The report highlighted two February 28 strikes that killed at least 178 civilians.<sup about="#mwt1508" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-437" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-437"}}'><a href="#cite_note-437" id="mwC2A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2I">[</span>436<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1511" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-438" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-438"}}'><a href="#cite_note-438" id="mwC2Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2Y">[</span>437<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1514" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ds-un_439-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ds-un"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ds-un-439"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ds-un-439" id="mwC2g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC2k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2o">[</span>438<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC2s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1517" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-440" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-440"}}'><a href="#cite_note-440" id="mwC2w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC20"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC24">[</span>439<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC28">]</span></span></a></sup> U.S. President <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump" title="Donald Trump" id="mwC3A">Donald Trump</a>'s threats to completely destroy <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran" title="Iran" id="mwC3E">Iranian</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Power_plant" title="Power plant" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC3I">power plants</a> and other essential infrastructure during the 2026 Iran war have been widely condemned by human rights organizations, legal experts, and lawmakers as potential war crimes.<sup about="#mwt1520" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-441" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-441"}}'><a href="#cite_note-441" id="mwC3M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3U">[</span>440<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1523" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-442" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-442"}}'><a href="#cite_note-442" id="mwC3c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3k">[</span>441<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC3o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1526" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-443" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-443"}}'><a href="#cite_note-443" id="mwC3s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC3w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC30">[</span>442<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC34">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1529" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-444" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-444"}}'><a href="#cite_note-444" id="mwC38"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4E">[</span>443<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4I">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1532" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-445" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-445"}}'><a href="#cite_note-445" id="mwC4M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4U">[</span>444<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4Y">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1535" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-446" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-446"}}'><a href="#cite_note-446" id="mwC4c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4k">[</span>445<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC4o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1538" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-447" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-447"}}'><a href="#cite_note-447" id="mwC4s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC4w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC40">[</span>446<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC44">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="64" id="mwC48" aria-labelledby="Israel_and_Gaza"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading5"><h5 id="Israel_and_Gaza">Israel and Gaza</h5></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1539" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwC5A" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"United States support for Israel in the Gaza war"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1540" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1539" id="mwC5E">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_support_for_Israel_in_the_Gaza_war" title="United States support for Israel in the Gaza war">United States support for Israel in the Gaza war</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwC5I"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_J._Trump_Welcomes_Israeli_Prime_Minister_Benjamin_Netanyahu_to_the_White_House_(cropped_b).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwC5M"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_J._Trump_Welcomes_Israeli_Prime_Minister_Benjamin_Netanyahu_to_the_White_House_(cropped_b).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/President_Donald_J._Trump_Welcomes_Israeli_Prime_Minister_Benjamin_Netanyahu_to_the_White_House_%28cropped_b%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_J._Trump_Welcomes_Israeli_Prime_Minister_Benjamin_Netanyahu_to_the_White_House_%28cropped_b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/President_Donald_J._Trump_Welcomes_Israeli_Prime_Minister_Benjamin_Netanyahu_to_the_White_House_%28cropped_b%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_J._Trump_Welcomes_Israeli_Prime_Minister_Benjamin_Netanyahu_to_the_White_House_%28cropped_b%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2099" data-file-height="1477" data-file-type="bitmap" height="176" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwC5Q"/></a><figcaption id="mwC5U">President Trump hosting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Netanyahu" title="Benjamin Netanyahu" id="mwC5Y">Benjamin Netanyahu</a> at the White House on July 7, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwC5c"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:250709-D-PM193-1255_SecDef_Pete_Hegseth_Hosts_Israeli_PM_Netanyahu_at_the_Pentagon.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwC5g"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:250709-D-PM193-1255_SecDef_Pete_Hegseth_Hosts_Israeli_PM_Netanyahu_at_the_Pentagon.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/250709-D-PM193-1255_SecDef_Pete_Hegseth_Hosts_Israeli_PM_Netanyahu_at_the_Pentagon.jpg/250px-250709-D-PM193-1255_SecDef_Pete_Hegseth_Hosts_Israeli_PM_Netanyahu_at_the_Pentagon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/250709-D-PM193-1255_SecDef_Pete_Hegseth_Hosts_Israeli_PM_Netanyahu_at_the_Pentagon.jpg/500px-250709-D-PM193-1255_SecDef_Pete_Hegseth_Hosts_Israeli_PM_Netanyahu_at_the_Pentagon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="7788" data-file-height="5192" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwC5k"/></a><figcaption id="mwC5o">Secretary of Defense <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pete_Hegseth" title="Pete Hegseth" id="mwC5s">Pete Hegseth</a> hosting Netanyahu at the Pentagon on July 9, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwC5w">After being elected in November 2024, Trump said he wished to end the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_war" title="Gaza war" id="mwC50">Gaza war</a>,<sup about="#mwt1543" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abces2024_448-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abces2024"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-abces2024-448"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abces2024-448" id="mwC54"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC58"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6A">[</span>447<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1546" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-449" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-449"}}'><a href="#cite_note-449" id="mwC6I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC6M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6Q">[</span>448<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6U">]</span></span></a></sup> telling Israeli prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Netanyahu" title="Benjamin Netanyahu" id="mwC6Y">Benjamin Netanyahu</a> to end <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israeli_invasion_of_the_Gaza_Strip" title="Israeli invasion of the Gaza Strip" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC6c">Israel's invasion</a> within two months<sup about="#mwt1547" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-abces2024_448-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"abces2024"}}'><a href="#cite_note-abces2024-448" id="mwC6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC6k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6o">[</span>447<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC6s">]</span></span></a></sup> and warning Hamas that they would have "all hell to pay" if they did not agree to a ceasefire and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_war_hostage_crisis" title="Gaza war hostage crisis" id="mwC6w">release all hostages</a> by Trump's inauguration.<sup about="#mwt1550" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-450" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-450"}}'><a href="#cite_note-450" id="mwC60"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC64"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC68">[</span>449<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7A">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's incoming administration joined the Biden administration in pressuring negotiations,<sup about="#mwt1553" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-washingtonpost202501152_451-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"washingtonpost202501152"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-washingtonpost202501152-451"}}'><a href="#cite_note-washingtonpost202501152-451" id="mwC7E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7M">[</span>450<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7Q">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1556" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-haaretz202501132_452-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"haaretz202501132"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-haaretz202501132-452"}}'><a href="#cite_note-haaretz202501132-452" id="mwC7U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7c">[</span>451<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1559" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nytimes20250115a2_453-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nytimes20250115a2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nytimes20250115a2-453"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nytimes20250115a2-453" id="mwC7k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC7o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7s">[</span>452<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC7w">]</span></span></a></sup> and Israel and Hamas <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_2025_Gaza_war_ceasefire" title="January 2025 Gaza war ceasefire" id="mwC70">agreed to a phased ceasefire</a> on January 15, 2025.<sup about="#mwt1562" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-454" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-454"}}'><a href="#cite_note-454" id="mwC74"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC78"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8A">[</span>453<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1565" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-agreementconfirmed_455-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"agreementconfirmed"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-agreementconfirmed-455"}}'><a href="#cite_note-agreementconfirmed-455" id="mwC8I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8Q">[</span>454<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8U">]</span></span></a></sup> In February 2025, Trump <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Donald_Trump_Gaza_Strip_takeover_proposal" title="2025 Donald Trump Gaza Strip takeover proposal" id="mwC8Y">proposed an American takeover of Gaza</a> in which the territory's Palestinian population would be relocated to allow for its redevelopment, which was criticized by Egypt and Jordan.<sup about="#mwt1568" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-456" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-456"}}'><a href="#cite_note-456" id="mwC8c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8k">[</span>455<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC8o">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1571" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Trump_plan_457-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Trump plan"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Trump_plan-457"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Trump_plan-457" id="mwC8s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC8w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC80">[</span>456<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC84">]</span></span></a></sup> The ceasefire lasted until March 18, when <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_2025_Israeli_attacks_on_the_Gaza_Strip" title="March 2025 Israeli attacks on the Gaza Strip" id="mwC88">Israel launched attacks on Gaza</a>.<sup about="#mwt1578" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-breaking_ceasefire_458-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"breaking ceasefire"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-breaking_ceasefire-458"}}'><a href="#cite_note-breaking_ceasefire-458" id="mwC9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC9E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9I">[</span>457<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9M">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's special envoy <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Witkoff" title="Steve Witkoff" id="mwC9Q">Steve Witkoff</a> blamed Hamas for renewed fighting in Gaza.<sup about="#mwt1581" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-459" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-459"}}'><a href="#cite_note-459" id="mwC9U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC9Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9c">[</span>458<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC9g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC9k">On May 16, while in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abu_Dhabi" title="Abu Dhabi" id="mwC9o">Abu Dhabi</a>, United Arab Emirates, Trump said, "We're looking at Gaza. And we're going to get that taken care of. A lot of people are starving." This is an area of tension between President Trump and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Netanyahu" title="Benjamin Netanyahu" id="mwC9s">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu</a>. Israel claims that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas" title="Hamas" id="mwC9w">Hamas</a> systemically raids food aid in order to support its operations, and Israel has put forward a plan of food distributed through a system of hubs run by private contractors and protected by Israeli soldiers. The U.S.-backed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_Humanitarian_Foundation" title="Gaza Humanitarian Foundation" id="mwC90">Gaza Humanitarian Foundation</a> has been set up to carry out this plan and announced it would be ready to begin operations by the end of May.<sup about="#mwt1584" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-The_Guardian,_Trump_acknowledges_starvation_in_Gaza,_May_16,_2025_460-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"The Guardian, Trump acknowledges starvation in Gaza, May 16, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-The_Guardian,_Trump_acknowledges_starvation_in_Gaza,_May_16,_2025-460"}}'><a href="#cite_note-The_Guardian,_Trump_acknowledges_starvation_in_Gaza,_May_16,_2025-460" id="mwC94"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC98"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-A">[</span>459<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1587" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_Trump_says_461-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, Trump says"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_Trump_says-461"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_Trump_says-461" id="mwC-I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-Q">[</span>460<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-U">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC-Y">On July 28, while in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scotland" title="Scotland" id="mwC-c">Scotland</a>, President Trump said he believed there was <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_Strip_famine" title="Gaza Strip famine" id="mwC-g">starvation occurring in Gaza</a>. He further added, "Nobody's done anything great over there. The whole place is a mess... I told Israel maybe they have to do it a different way." Israeli Prime Minister said, "And what has interdicted the supply of humanitarian aid is one force, Hamas. Again, the reversal of truth."<sup about="#mwt1590" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BBC,_'real_starvation,'_Trump_says,_July_28,_2025_462-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BBC, &apos;real starvation,&apos; Trump says, July 28, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BBC,_&apos;real_starvation,&apos;_Trump_says,_July_28,_2025-462"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BBC,_'real_starvation,'_Trump_says,_July_28,_2025-462" id="mwC-k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-s">[</span>461<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-w">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1593" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Guardian,_does_not_endorse_Netanyahu's_claim_there_is_no_starvation,_July_28,_2025_463-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Guardian, does not endorse Netanyahu&apos;s claim there is no starvation, July 28, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Guardian,_does_not_endorse_Netanyahu&apos;s_claim_there_is_no_starvation,_July_28,_2025-463"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Guardian,_does_not_endorse_Netanyahu's_claim_there_is_no_starvation,_July_28,_2025-463" id="mwC-0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC-4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC-8">[</span>462<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwC_E">Asked about an Israeli <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Nasser_Hospital_strikes" title="2025 Nasser Hospital strikes" id="mwC_I">double-strike on a hospital</a> on August 25, 2025, Trump said he was "not happy about it", adding, "We have to end this whole nightmare."<sup about="#mwt1596" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NBC,_Israel_faces_new_pressure_over_hospital_strikes,_August_27,_2025_464-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NBC, Israel faces new pressure over hospital strikes, August 27, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NBC,_Israel_faces_new_pressure_over_hospital_strikes,_August_27,_2025-464"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NBC,_Israel_faces_new_pressure_over_hospital_strikes,_August_27,_2025-464" id="mwC_M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwC_Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_U">[</span>463<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwC_Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwC_c"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:US_President_Donald_Trump_speaks_at_the_2025_Sharm_El-Sheikh_Peace_Summit_02.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwC_g"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:US_President_Donald_Trump_speaks_at_the_2025_Sharm_El-Sheikh_Peace_Summit_02.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/US_President_Donald_Trump_speaks_at_the_2025_Sharm_El-Sheikh_Peace_Summit_02.jpg/250px-US_President_Donald_Trump_speaks_at_the_2025_Sharm_El-Sheikh_Peace_Summit_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/US_President_Donald_Trump_speaks_at_the_2025_Sharm_El-Sheikh_Peace_Summit_02.jpg/500px-US_President_Donald_Trump_speaks_at_the_2025_Sharm_El-Sheikh_Peace_Summit_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3758" data-file-height="2507" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwC_k"/></a><figcaption id="mwC_o">Trump at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Gaza_peace_summit" title="2025 Gaza peace summit" class="mw-redirect" id="mwC_s">Gaza peace summit</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharm_El_Sheikh" title="Sharm El Sheikh" id="mwC_w">Sharm El Sheikh</a>, Egypt, on October 13, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwC_0">On September 29, 2025, President Trump announced, alongside Prime Minister Netanyahu, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_peace_plan" title="Gaza peace plan" id="mwC_4">20-Point Gaza Peace Plan</a> from the White House which consisted of 20 specific points aimed at achieving a ceasefire, the return of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_war_hostage_crisis" title="Gaza war hostage crisis" id="mwC_8">Israeli hostages</a>, dismantling <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas" title="Hamas" id="mwDAA">Hamas</a>'s military capabilities, and establishing a transitional governance structure in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_Strip" title="Gaza Strip" id="mwDAE">Gaza Strip</a>.<sup about="#mwt1599" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-465" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-465"}}'><a href="#cite_note-465" id="mwDAI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAQ">[</span>464<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDAY">In October 2025, President Trump announced his deal for a ceasefire between Israel and Hamas had been reached and that the remaining hostages would be released.<sup about="#mwt1602" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-466" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-466"}}'><a href="#cite_note-466" id="mwDAc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAk">[</span>465<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDAo">]</span></span></a></sup> In exchange, Israel will release 250 Palestinian prisoners serving longterm sentences and another 1,700 other prisoners. The Israeli military will withdraw from a "blue line" to a "yellow line" further away from the Gaza coast.<sup about="#mwt1605" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_News,_Israel-Hamas_ceasefire,_Oct_9,_2025_467-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC News, Israel-Hamas ceasefire, Oct 9, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_News,_Israel-Hamas_ceasefire,_Oct_9,_2025-467"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_News,_Israel-Hamas_ceasefire,_Oct_9,_2025-467" id="mwDAs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDAw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA0">[</span>466<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA4">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump was widely praised for negotiating this settlement, including by former presidents Bill Clinton and Barack Obama and former Secretary of State and 2016 presidential candidate Hillary Clinton.<sup about="#mwt1608" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-468" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-468"}}'><a href="#cite_note-468" id="mwDA8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDBA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBE">[</span>467<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1611" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-469" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-469"}}'><a href="#cite_note-469" id="mwDBM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDBQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBU">[</span>468<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDBY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="65" id="mwDBc" aria-labelledby="Qatar"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading5"><h5 id="Qatar">Qatar</h5></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDBg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Donald_Trump_state_visit_to_Qatar,_2025-05-14_P20250514DT-2130.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDBk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Donald_Trump_state_visit_to_Qatar,_2025-05-14_P20250514DT-2130.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Donald_Trump_state_visit_to_Qatar%2C_2025-05-14_P20250514DT-2130.jpg/250px-Donald_Trump_state_visit_to_Qatar%2C_2025-05-14_P20250514DT-2130.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Donald_Trump_state_visit_to_Qatar%2C_2025-05-14_P20250514DT-2130.jpg/500px-Donald_Trump_state_visit_to_Qatar%2C_2025-05-14_P20250514DT-2130.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDBo"/></a><figcaption id="mwDBs">Trump and Qatar's emir <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamim_bin_Hamad_Al_Thani" title="Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani" id="mwDBw">Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lusail" title="Lusail" id="mwDB0">Lusail</a>, Qatar during <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/May_2025_visit_by_Donald_Trump_to_the_Middle_East" title="May 2025 visit by Donald Trump to the Middle East" id="mwDB4">Donald Trump's visit to the Middle East</a>, May 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDB8">In September 2025, following an Israeli strike against suspected Hamas terrorists in Qatar's capital city of Doha, President Trump signed an executive order which stated, "The United States shall regard any armed attack on the territory, sovereignty, or critical infrastructure of the State of Qatar as a threat to the peace and security of the United States."<sup about="#mwt1614" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_U.S._base_in_Idaho,_Oct_10,_2025_470-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, U.S. base in Idaho, Oct 10, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_U.S._base_in_Idaho,_Oct_10,_2025-470"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_U.S._base_in_Idaho,_Oct_10,_2025-470" id="mwDCA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDCE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCI">[</span>469<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCM">]</span></span></a></sup> President Biden had begun a closer relationship with Qatar following their help with the 2001 American withdrawal from Afghanistan. In January 2022, Biden named Qatar a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_non-NATO_ally" title="Major non-NATO ally" id="mwDCQ">major non-NATO ally</a>.<sup about="#mwt1615" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_News,_executive_order_vowing_to_defend_Qatar,_Oct_1,_2025_471-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC News, executive order vowing to defend Qatar, Oct 1, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_News,_executive_order_vowing_to_defend_Qatar,_Oct_1,_2025-471"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_News,_executive_order_vowing_to_defend_Qatar,_Oct_1,_2025-471" id="mwDCU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDCY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCc">[</span>470<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDCg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDCk">The editorial board of <i id="mwDCo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wall_Street_Journal" title="The Wall Street Journal" id="mwDCs">The Wall Street Journal</a></i> wrote, "This is a decision that can be and should have been debated. Instead it comes out of the blue — an executive order following no public debate."<sup about="#mwt1616" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_News,_executive_order_vowing_to_defend_Qatar,_Oct_1,_2025_471-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC News, executive order vowing to defend Qatar, Oct 1, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_News,_executive_order_vowing_to_defend_Qatar,_Oct_1,_2025-471" id="mwDCw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDC0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDC4">[</span>470<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDC8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDDA">In October, Defense Secretary Hegseth announced a training agreement that the Qatar Air Force will build a facility at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Home_Air_Force_Base" title="Mountain Home Air Force Base" id="mwDDE">Mountain Home Air Force Base</a> in Idaho. The United States has a similar arrangement with Singapore, at the same base. Hegseth emphasized that the U.S. will remain in charge of the facility "like we do with all partners".<sup about="#mwt1617" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_U.S._base_in_Idaho,_Oct_10,_2025_470-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, U.S. base in Idaho, Oct 10, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_U.S._base_in_Idaho,_Oct_10,_2025-470" id="mwDDI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDDM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDQ">[</span>469<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDDU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="66" id="mwDDY" aria-labelledby="Syria"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading5"><h5 id="Syria">Syria</h5></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDDc"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_with_Saudi_Crown_Prince_Mohammed_Bin_Salman_and_President_of_Syria_Ahmed_al-Sharaa_(2025).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDDg"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_with_Saudi_Crown_Prince_Mohammed_Bin_Salman_and_President_of_Syria_Ahmed_al-Sharaa_(2025).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/President_Donald_Trump_with_Saudi_Crown_Prince_Mohammed_Bin_Salman_and_President_of_Syria_Ahmed_al-Sharaa_%282025%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_with_Saudi_Crown_Prince_Mohammed_Bin_Salman_and_President_of_Syria_Ahmed_al-Sharaa_%282025%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/President_Donald_Trump_with_Saudi_Crown_Prince_Mohammed_Bin_Salman_and_President_of_Syria_Ahmed_al-Sharaa_%282025%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_with_Saudi_Crown_Prince_Mohammed_Bin_Salman_and_President_of_Syria_Ahmed_al-Sharaa_%282025%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1536" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDDk"/></a><figcaption id="mwDDo">Trump with Syrian president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahmed_al-Sharaa" title="Ahmed al-Sharaa" id="mwDDs">Ahmed al-Sharaa</a> and Crown Prince of Saudi Arabia <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_bin_Salman" title="Mohammed bin Salman" id="mwDDw">Mohammed bin Salman</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riyadh" title="Riyadh" id="mwDD0">Riyadh</a>, Saudi Arabia, May 14, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDD4">During the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Syrian_opposition_offensives" title="2024 Syrian opposition offensives" id="mwDD8">2024 Syrian opposition offensives</a> that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fall_of_the_Assad_regime" title="Fall of the Assad regime" id="mwDEA">toppled the Assad regime</a> in Syria, Trump said that the U.S. should stay out of the conflict.<sup about="#mwt1620" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-472" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-472"}}'><a href="#cite_note-472" id="mwDEE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEM">[</span>471<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In March 2025, Rubio condemned the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_massacres_of_Syrian_Alawites" title="2025 massacres of Syrian Alawites" id="mwDEU">massacres of Syrian Alawites</a>.<sup about="#mwt1623" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-473" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-473"}}'><a href="#cite_note-473" id="mwDEY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDEc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEg">[</span>472<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDEk">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump agreed to lift sanctions on Syria after discussing the situation with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_bin_Salman" title="Mohammed bin Salman" id="mwDEo">Mohammed bin Salman</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recep_Tayyip_Erdoğan" title="Recep Tayyip Erdoğan" id="mwDEs">Erdoğan</a> in May 2025.<sup about="#mwt1626" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Ghinwa_Obeid_474-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Ghinwa Obeid"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Ghinwa_Obeid-474"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Ghinwa_Obeid-474" id="mwDEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDE0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDE4">[</span>473<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDE8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1629" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Gram_Slattery_et_al._475-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Gram Slattery et al."},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Gram_Slattery_et_al.-475"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Gram_Slattery_et_al.-475" id="mwDFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDFE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFI">[</span>474<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDFM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="67" id="mwDFQ" aria-labelledby="Indian_subcontinent"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Indian_subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1630" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDFU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"2025 United States–India diplomatic and trade crisis"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1631" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1630" id="mwDFY">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States–India_diplomatic_and_trade_crisis" title="2025 United States–India diplomatic and trade crisis" class="mw-redirect">2025 United States–India diplomatic and trade crisis</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDFc"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250213MR-1471.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDFg"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250213MR-1471.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/P20250213MR-1471.jpg/250px-P20250213MR-1471.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/P20250213MR-1471.jpg/500px-P20250213MR-1471.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDFk"/></a><figcaption id="mwDFo">Trump with Indian prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narendra_Modi" title="Narendra Modi" id="mwDFs">Narendra Modi</a>, February 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDFw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India" title="India" id="mwDF0">India</a> rejected Trump's offer to mediate <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China–India_relations" title="China–India relations" id="mwDF4">India–China tensions</a>.<sup about="#mwt1634" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-476" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-476"}}'><a href="#cite_note-476" id="mwDF8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGE">[</span>475<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGI">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 13, 2025, Indian prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narendra_Modi" title="Narendra Modi" id="mwDGM">Narendra Modi</a> became the fourth world leader to visit Donald Trump at the White House.<sup about="#mwt1637" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-477" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-477"}}'><a href="#cite_note-477" id="mwDGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGY">[</span>476<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDGc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDGg">In early 2025, deportations to Bhutan of Nepali-speaking <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bhutanese_refugees" title="Bhutanese refugees" id="mwDGk">Bhutanese refugees</a> who had been settled in the US for nearly two decades resulted in statelessness of the deportees following their interrogation and expulsion from Bhutan upon arrival. Some of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-refoulement" title="Non-refoulement" id="mwDGo">refouled refugees</a>, who had encountered largely minor legal issues in the US, were then arrested for illegal entry to Nepal upon seeking to re-enter the refugee camps they had previously inhabited before US resettlement.<sup about="#mwt1640" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-478" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-478"}}'><a href="#cite_note-478" id="mwDGs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDGw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDG0">[</span>477<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDG4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1643" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-479" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-479"}}'><a href="#cite_note-479" id="mwDG8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDHA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHE">[</span>478<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDHI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDHM"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250925DT-0757_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Prime_Minister_Shehbaz_Sharif_and_Field_Marshal_Asim_Munir_of_Pakistan.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDHQ"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250925DT-0757_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Prime_Minister_Shehbaz_Sharif_and_Field_Marshal_Asim_Munir_of_Pakistan.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/P20250925DT-0757_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Prime_Minister_Shehbaz_Sharif_and_Field_Marshal_Asim_Munir_of_Pakistan.jpg/250px-P20250925DT-0757_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Prime_Minister_Shehbaz_Sharif_and_Field_Marshal_Asim_Munir_of_Pakistan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/P20250925DT-0757_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Prime_Minister_Shehbaz_Sharif_and_Field_Marshal_Asim_Munir_of_Pakistan.jpg/500px-P20250925DT-0757_President_Donald_Trump_meets_with_Prime_Minister_Shehbaz_Sharif_and_Field_Marshal_Asim_Munir_of_Pakistan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDHU"/></a><figcaption id="mwDHY">Trump with Pakistani prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shehbaz_Sharif" title="Shehbaz Sharif" id="mwDHc">Shehbaz Sharif</a> (left) and Pakistani chief of Army staff <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asim_Munir" title="Asim Munir" id="mwDHg">Asim Munir</a> (right)</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDHk">In response to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_India–Pakistan_strikes" title="2025 India–Pakistan strikes" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDHo">2025 India–Pakistan conflict</a>, Vice President Vance said that, a potential war between India and Pakistan is "none of our business".<sup about="#mwt1646" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-480" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-480"}}'><a href="#cite_note-480" id="mwDHs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDHw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDH0">[</span>479<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDH4">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump claimed to have negotiated a ceasefire, a claim that Pakistan corroborated and India denied.<sup about="#mwt1649" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-481" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-481"}}'><a href="#cite_note-481" id="mwDH8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIE">[</span>480<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDII">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1652" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-482" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-482"}}'><a href="#cite_note-482" id="mwDIM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIU">[</span>481<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1655" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-483" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-483"}}'><a href="#cite_note-483" id="mwDIc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDIg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIk">[</span>482<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDIo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDIs">In July 2025, Trump criticized India over its continued oil trade with Russia, despite ongoing Western sanctions.<sup about="#mwt1658" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NDTV2025_484-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NDTV2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NDTV2025-484"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NDTV2025-484" id="mwDIw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDI0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDI4">[</span>483<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDI8">]</span></span></a></sup> On July 30, 2025, Trump announced that Indian products would be subject to 25% reciprocal <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tariffs_in_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Tariffs in the second Trump administration" id="mwDJA">tariffs</a> upon arrival in the United States starting August 1, and that a "penalty" would be added for the purchase of Russian oil.<sup about="#mwt1661" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-485" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-485"}}'><a href="#cite_note-485" id="mwDJE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJM">[</span>484<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On August 6, 2025, Trump raised the tariff to 50%, a 25% increase, over India's purchase of Russian oil.<sup about="#mwt1664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-486" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-486"}}'><a href="#cite_note-486" id="mwDJU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJc">[</span>485<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDJk">In July 2025, Trump's administration reached a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan–United_States_trade_deal" title="Pakistan–United States trade deal" id="mwDJo">trade agreement</a> with Pakistan, in which Trump announced that the United States would help Pakistan develop its large and untapped <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_reserves" title="Oil reserves" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDJs">oil reserves</a>.<sup about="#mwt1667" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-APNews2025a_487-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"APNews2025a"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-APNews2025a-487"}}'><a href="#cite_note-APNews2025a-487" id="mwDJw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDJ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJ4">[</span>486<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDJ8">]</span></span></a></sup> The agreement also reduced American reciprocal tariffs on Pakistan to 19%, the lowest of any country in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Asia" title="South Asia" id="mwDKA">South Asia</a>.<sup about="#mwt1668" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-APNews2025a_487-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"APNews2025a"}}'><a href="#cite_note-APNews2025a-487" id="mwDKE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDKI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKM">[</span>486<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDKQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="68" id="mwDKU" aria-labelledby="Caucasus"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Caucasus">Caucasus</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1669" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDKY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Armenia–Azerbaijan peace agreement"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1670" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1669" id="mwDKc">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenia–Azerbaijan_peace_agreement" title="Armenia–Azerbaijan peace agreement">Armenia–Azerbaijan peace agreement</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDKg"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250808DT-1377_President_Donald_Trump_signs_a_trilateral_joint_declaration_with_President_Ilham_Aliyev_of_Azerbaijan_and_Prime_Minister_Nikol_Pashinyan_of_Armenia.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDKk"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250808DT-1377_President_Donald_Trump_signs_a_trilateral_joint_declaration_with_President_Ilham_Aliyev_of_Azerbaijan_and_Prime_Minister_Nikol_Pashinyan_of_Armenia.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/P20250808DT-1377_President_Donald_Trump_signs_a_trilateral_joint_declaration_with_President_Ilham_Aliyev_of_Azerbaijan_and_Prime_Minister_Nikol_Pashinyan_of_Armenia.jpg/250px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/P20250808DT-1377_President_Donald_Trump_signs_a_trilateral_joint_declaration_with_President_Ilham_Aliyev_of_Azerbaijan_and_Prime_Minister_Nikol_Pashinyan_of_Armenia.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDKo"/></a><figcaption id="mwDKs">Azerbaijani president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilham_Aliyev" title="Ilham Aliyev" id="mwDKw">Ilham Aliyev</a>, President Trump and Armenian prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikol_Pashinyan" title="Nikol Pashinyan" id="mwDK0">Nikol Pashinyan</a> signing a trilateral joint declaration in Washington, D.C., on August 8, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDK4">On April 24, 2025, during the first <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenian_Genocide_Remembrance_Day" title="Armenian Genocide Remembrance Day" id="mwDK8">Armenian Genocide Remembrance Day</a> of Trump's second term, the White House issued a statement commemorating the day that did not use the term "genocide".<sup about="#mwt1673" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-488" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-488"}}'><a href="#cite_note-488" id="mwDLA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLI">[</span>487<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLM">]</span></span></a></sup> This was seen as a reversal after Joe Biden formally <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_recognition_of_the_Armenian_genocide" title="United States recognition of the Armenian genocide" id="mwDLQ">recognized</a> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenian_genocide" title="Armenian genocide" id="mwDLU">Armenian genocide</a> in 2021.<sup about="#mwt1676" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-489" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-489"}}'><a href="#cite_note-489" id="mwDLY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDLc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLg">[</span>488<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDLk">]</span></span></a></sup> The second Trump administration continues to avoid using the term "genocide", instead continuing to refer to the events as the <i id="mwDLo"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terminology_of_the_Armenian_genocide#Armenian" title="Terminology of the Armenian genocide" id="mwDLs">Medz Yeghern</a></i> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenian_language" title="Armenian language" id="mwDLw">Armenian</a> for 'Great Catastrophe') and labeling April 24 as only "Armenian Remembrance Day".<sup about="#mwt1679" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-490" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-490"}}'><a href="#cite_note-490" id="mwDL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDL8">[</span>489<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDME">On August 8, 2025, Armenian prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nikol_Pashinyan" title="Nikol Pashinyan" id="mwDMI">Nikol Pashinyan</a> and Azerbaijani president <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilham_Aliyev" title="Ilham Aliyev" id="mwDMM">Ilham Aliyev</a> signed a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armenia–Azerbaijan_peace_agreement" title="Armenia–Azerbaijan peace agreement" id="mwDMQ">peace agreement</a> in a ceremony hosted by President Donald Trump in the White House,<sup about="#mwt1682" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-491" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-491"}}'><a href="#cite_note-491" id="mwDMU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMc">[</span>490<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMg">]</span></span></a></sup> aiming to end the more than <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagorno-Karabakh_conflict" title="Nagorno-Karabakh conflict" id="mwDMk">35-year conflict</a> between Armenia and Azerbaijan.<sup about="#mwt1685" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-492" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-492"}}'><a href="#cite_note-492" id="mwDMo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDMs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDMw">[</span>491<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDM0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="69" id="mwDM4" aria-labelledby="Southeast_Asia"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Southeast_Asia">Southeast Asia</h4></div>
<p id="mwDM8">In 2025, Trump attempted to negotiate a ceasefire in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Cambodia–Thailand_border_conflict" title="2025 Cambodia–Thailand border conflict" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDNA">border conflict between Cambodia and Thailand</a>.<sup about="#mwt1688" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-493" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-493"}}'><a href="#cite_note-493" id="mwDNE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNM">[</span>492<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1691" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-494" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-494"}}'><a href="#cite_note-494" id="mwDNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNc">[</span>493<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDNg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="70" id="mwDNk" aria-labelledby="China_2"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="China_2">China</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1692" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDNo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"China–United States trade war"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1693" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1692" id="mwDNs">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China–United_States_trade_war" title="China–United States trade war">China–United States trade war</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDNw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_(54890669668).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDN0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_(54890669668).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_%2854890669668%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_%2854890669668%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_%2854890669668%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_%2854890669668%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDN4"/></a><figcaption id="mwDN8">Trump meets with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount_leader" title="Paramount leader" id="mwDOA">Chinese leader</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping" title="Xi Jinping" id="mwDOE">Xi Jinping</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Busan_Summit" title="Busan Summit" id="mwDOI">summit meeting</a> in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Busan" title="Busan" id="mwDOM">Busan</a> on October 30, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDOQ">In February 2025, Trump signed an executive order that directed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Committee_on_Foreign_Investment_in_the_United_States" title="Committee on Foreign Investment in the United States" id="mwDOU">Committee on Foreign Investment in the United States</a> (CFIUS) to restrict Chinese investment in strategic economic areas.<sup about="#mwt1696" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-495" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-495"}}'><a href="#cite_note-495" id="mwDOY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDOc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOg">[</span>494<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDOk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDOo">Trump blamed China for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opioid_epidemic_in_the_United_States" title="Opioid epidemic in the United States" id="mwDOs">opioid crisis in the United States</a>.<sup about="#mwt1699" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-496" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-496"}}'><a href="#cite_note-496" id="mwDOw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDO0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDO4">[</span>495<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDO8">]</span></span></a></sup> He said the tariffs are intended to pressure China to do more to stop the flow of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fentanyl" title="Fentanyl" id="mwDPA">fentanyl</a> into the US.<sup about="#mwt1702" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-497" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-497"}}'><a href="#cite_note-497" id="mwDPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPM">[</span>496<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opioid" title="Opioid" id="mwDPU">Opioids</a>, predominantly fentanyl, have killed over 500,000 Americans since 2012.<sup about="#mwt1705" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-498" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-498"}}'><a href="#cite_note-498" id="mwDPY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDPc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPg">[</span>497<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDPk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDPo">In September 2025, Trump asked the EU to impose 100% tariffs on China to punish it for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_and_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine" title="China and the Russian invasion of Ukraine" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDPs">buying Russian oil</a> and de facto financing Russia's invasion of Ukraine.<sup about="#mwt1708" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-499" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-499"}}'><a href="#cite_note-499" id="mwDPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDP0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDP4">[</span>498<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDP8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1711" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-500" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-500"}}'><a href="#cite_note-500" id="mwDQA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDQE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQI">[</span>499<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="71" id="mwDQQ" aria-labelledby="Oceania"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Oceania">Oceania</h3></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="72" id="mwDQU" aria-labelledby="Australia"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Australia">Australia</h4></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDQY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_greets_Australian_Prime_Minister_Anthony_Albanese_at_the_West_Wing_Lobby_entrance_of_the_White_House_(54874273357).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDQc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_greets_Australian_Prime_Minister_Anthony_Albanese_at_the_West_Wing_Lobby_entrance_of_the_White_House_(54874273357).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/President_Donald_Trump_greets_Australian_Prime_Minister_Anthony_Albanese_at_the_West_Wing_Lobby_entrance_of_the_White_House_%2854874273357%29.jpg/250px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_Australian_Prime_Minister_Anthony_Albanese_at_the_West_Wing_Lobby_entrance_of_the_White_House_%2854874273357%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/President_Donald_Trump_greets_Australian_Prime_Minister_Anthony_Albanese_at_the_West_Wing_Lobby_entrance_of_the_White_House_%2854874273357%29.jpg/500px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_Australian_Prime_Minister_Anthony_Albanese_at_the_West_Wing_Lobby_entrance_of_the_White_House_%2854874273357%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDQg"/></a><figcaption id="mwDQk">Trump greets Australian Prime Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Albanese" title="Anthony Albanese" id="mwDQo">Anthony Albanese</a> at the White House, October 20, 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDQs">On October 21, 2025, partly as a consequence of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China–United_States_trade_war" title="China–United States trade war" id="mwDQw">China–U.S. trade war</a> that included China imposing restrictions on its sale of processed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rare-earth_element" title="Rare-earth element" id="mwDQ0">rare-earth elements</a>, Trump signed a deal with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Albanese" title="Anthony Albanese" id="mwDQ4">Anthony Albanese</a>, Prime Minister of Australia,<sup about="#mwt1724" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-sherman2025_501-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"sherman2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-sherman2025-501"}}'><a href="#cite_note-sherman2025-501" id="mwDQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRE">[</span>500<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRI">]</span></span></a></sup> over rare-earths and other <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Critical_minerals" title="Critical minerals" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDRM">critical minerals</a><sup about="#mwt1712" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-503" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-503"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Rare-earth elements or minerals are distinct from minerals or materials described as [[critical minerals]] or raw materials, which refers to materials that are considered to be of strategic or economic importance to a country. There is no single list, but individual governments compile lists of materials that are critical for their own economies.&lt;ref>{{#invoke:cite | web | title=What are &apos;critical minerals&apos; and what is their significance for climate change action? | website=[[Grantham Research Institute]] | date=May 30, 2023| url=https://www.lse.ac.uk/granthaminstitute/explainers/what-are-critical-minerals-and-what-is-their-significance-for-climate-change-action/ | access-date=September 25, 2025}}&lt;/ref> However the two terms are often used interchangeably, especially in the U.S."}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-503" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDRQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRY">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRc">]</span></span></a></sup> that are needed for commercial <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clean_energy" title="Clean energy" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDRg">clean energy</a> production and technologically advanced <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_hardware" title="Military hardware" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDRk">military hardware</a>. They each committed to provide at least US$1bn (A$1.54bn) towards a number of projects worth $US8.5bn (A$13bn) in both countries over six months.<sup about="#mwt1728" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-barrett_504-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"barrett"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-barrett-504"}}'><a href="#cite_note-barrett-504" id="mwDRo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDRs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDRw">[</span>502<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDR0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1731" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-govtannounce_505-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"govtannounce"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-govtannounce-505"}}'><a href="#cite_note-govtannounce-505" id="mwDR4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDR8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSA">[</span>503<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSE">]</span></span></a></sup> The deal has been well received by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_rare-earths_industry" title="Australian rare-earths industry" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDSI">Australian rare-earths industry</a><sup about="#mwt1734" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-li2025_506-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"li2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-li2025-506"}}'><a href="#cite_note-li2025-506" id="mwDSM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSU">[</span>504<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1737" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wood2025_507-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wood2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wood2025-507"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wood2025-507" id="mwDSc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSk">[</span>505<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDSo">]</span></span></a></sup> and the markets,<sup about="#mwt1740" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-capolingua_508-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"capolingua"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-capolingua-508"}}'><a href="#cite_note-capolingua-508" id="mwDSs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDSw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDS0">[</span>506<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDS4">]</span></span></a></sup> and is important to the U.S. because rare earths are used in many technologies, including components of the Defense Force such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F-35" title="F-35" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDS8">F-35</a> fighter jets and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomahawk_missile" title="Tomahawk missile" id="mwDTA">Tomahawk missiles</a>.<sup about="#mwt1743" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-509" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-509"}}'><a href="#cite_note-509" id="mwDTE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTM">[</span>507<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The deal is also seen as a major shift in economic alliances.<sup about="#mwt1744" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-capolingua_508-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"capolingua"}}'><a href="#cite_note-capolingua-508" id="mwDTU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDTY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTc">[</span>506<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDTg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="73" id="mwDTk" aria-labelledby="Foreign_aid"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Foreign_aid">Foreign aid</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1745" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDTo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"United States Agency for International Development"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1746" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1745" id="mwDTs">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Agency_for_International_Development" title="United States Agency for International Development">United States Agency for International Development</a></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="74" id="mwDTw" aria-labelledby="Freezing_most_programs_for_90_days"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Freezing_most_programs_for_90_days">Freezing most programs for 90 days</h4></div>
<p id="mwDT0">DOGE dismantled most of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USAID" title="USAID" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDT4">USAID</a>,<sup about="#mwt1749" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Knickmeyer2025_510-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Knickmeyer2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Knickmeyer2025-510"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Knickmeyer2025-510" id="mwDT8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUE">[</span>508<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUI">]</span></span></a></sup> which had been a 10,000-person agency originally tasked to carry-out humanitarian projects.<sup about="#mwt1752" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-511" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-511"}}'><a href="#cite_note-511" id="mwDUM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUU">[</span>509<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUY">]</span></span></a></sup> USAID's critics maintained that many of the projects were in fact not all that humanitarian and/or much of the money was not well spent.<sup about="#mwt1755" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-512" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-512"}}'><a href="#cite_note-512" id="mwDUc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUk">[</span>510<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDUo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDUs">In January 2025, the administration issued a 90-day stop-work order worldwide,<sup about="#mwt1758" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AP_News,_State_Department_freezes_new_funding,_January_24,_2025_513-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AP News, State Department freezes new funding, January 24, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AP_News,_State_Department_freezes_new_funding,_January_24,_2025-513"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AP_News,_State_Department_freezes_new_funding,_January_24,_2025-513" id="mwDUw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDU0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDU4">[</span>511<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDU8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1761" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ProPublica-Jan_514-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ProPublica-Jan"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ProPublica-Jan-514"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ProPublica-Jan-514" id="mwDVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVI">[</span>512<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVM">]</span></span></a></sup> Stop work interrupted about 30 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinical_trial" title="Clinical trial" id="mwDVQ">clinical trials</a>,<sup about="#mwt1764" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-515" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-515"}}'><a href="#cite_note-515" id="mwDVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVc">[</span>513<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVg">]</span></span></a></sup> and interrupted projects such as emergency medical care for displaced Palestinians and Yemenis, aid for war refugees on the Sudan-Chad border, and electricity for Ukrainian refugees.<sup about="#mwt1765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ProPublica-Jan_514-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ProPublica-Jan"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ProPublica-Jan-514" id="mwDVk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDVo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVs">[</span>512<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDVw">]</span></span></a></sup> The HIV Modeling Consortium estimated the death toll from HIV in sub-Saharan Africa at approximately 15,000 adults and 1,600 children in the one month after Trump's January 2025 funding freeze.<sup about="#mwt1768" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-516" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-516"}}'><a href="#cite_note-516" id="mwDV0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDV4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDV8">[</span>514<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1771" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-517" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-517"}}'><a href="#cite_note-517" id="mwDWE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWM">[</span>515<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWQ">]</span></span></a></sup> A key controversy is whether or not waivers are being made and money actually starting to flow again for the most essential programs.<sup about="#mwt1772" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ProPublica-Jan_514-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ProPublica-Jan"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ProPublica-Jan-514" id="mwDWU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDWY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWc">[</span>512<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDWg">]</span></span></a></sup> For example, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associated_Press" title="Associated Press" id="mwDWk">Associated Press</a> reported on February 19, that waivers for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PEPFAR" title="PEPFAR" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDWo">PEPFAR</a>, the program that has saved 26<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDWs"> </span>million lives from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AIDS" title="AIDS" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDWw">AIDS</a>, were not in force, despite a federal judge having lifted the funding freeze.<sup about="#mwt1775" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-518" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-518"}}'><a href="#cite_note-518" id="mwDW0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDW4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDW8">[</span>516<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDXE"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:US_Army_and_Air_Force_in_Europe_join_USAID_to_provide_support_to_Lebanon_(6303783).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDXI"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:US_Army_and_Air_Force_in_Europe_join_USAID_to_provide_support_to_Lebanon_(6303783).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/US_Army_and_Air_Force_in_Europe_join_USAID_to_provide_support_to_Lebanon_%286303783%29.jpg/250px-US_Army_and_Air_Force_in_Europe_join_USAID_to_provide_support_to_Lebanon_%286303783%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/US_Army_and_Air_Force_in_Europe_join_USAID_to_provide_support_to_Lebanon_%286303783%29.jpg/500px-US_Army_and_Air_Force_in_Europe_join_USAID_to_provide_support_to_Lebanon_%286303783%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="6720" data-file-height="4480" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDXM"/></a><figcaption id="mwDXQ">U.S. Army and Air Force service members assisted USAID with the transportation of nearly 12,000 pounds of medical kits from the Netherlands, through Germany and on to Lebanon in August 2020.</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDXU">In early February 2025, it was reported that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USAID" title="USAID" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDXY">USAID</a> director of security and a deputy were put on administrative leave after they "blocked efforts by DOGE members to physically access restricted areas" in order to obtain sensitive information. The DOGE members eventually gained access to the information, which reportedly included email as well as classified information for which they did not have security clearance. And they obtained the ability to lock USAID staff out. Musk had earlier tweeted "USAID is a criminal organization" and that it is "time for it to die".<sup about="#mwt1778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-519" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-519"}}'><a href="#cite_note-519" id="mwDXc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDXg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXk">[</span>517<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDXo">]</span></span></a></sup> Estimates do vary. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxfam" title="Oxfam" id="mwDXs">Oxfam</a> criticized Musk's policies and actions as the world's richest individual deciding "to shutter the world's largest provider of lifesaving humanitarian aid".<sup about="#mwt1781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-520" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-520"}}'><a href="#cite_note-520" id="mwDXw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDX0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDX4">[</span>518<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDX8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDYA">USAID staff were instructed to keep away from USAID headquarters while hundreds of USAID staff lost access to USAID computer systems.<sup about="#mwt1782" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Knickmeyer2025_510-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Knickmeyer2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Knickmeyer2025-510" id="mwDYE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYM">[</span>508<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDYU">There have been reports that China has offered to take over development projects if the United States permanently leaves.<sup about="#mwt1785" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNN,_Trump_says_dismantling,_Feb_7,_2025_521-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNN, Trump says dismantling, Feb 7, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CNN,_Trump_says_dismantling,_Feb_7,_2025-521"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNN,_Trump_says_dismantling,_Feb_7,_2025-521" id="mwDYY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYg">[</span>519<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1788" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Politico,_As_USAID,_Feb_10,_2025_522-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Politico, As USAID, Feb 10, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Politico,_As_USAID,_Feb_10,_2025-522"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Politico,_As_USAID,_Feb_10,_2025-522" id="mwDYo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDYs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDYw">[</span>520<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDY0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1791" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NBC_News,_Cambodian_mine-clearing,_Feb_14,_2025_523-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NBC News, Cambodian mine-clearing, Feb 14, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NBC_News,_Cambodian_mine-clearing,_Feb_14,_2025-523"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NBC_News,_Cambodian_mine-clearing,_Feb_14,_2025-523" id="mwDY4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDY8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZA">[</span>521<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDZI">During a February 6 press conference, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Rubio" title="Marco Rubio" id="mwDZM">Secretary of State Marco Rubio</a> stated, "If it's providing food or medicine or anything that is saving lives and is immediate and urgent, you're not included in the freeze."<sup about="#mwt1792" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNN,_State_Department_says_humanitarian,_February_8,_2025_524-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNN, State Department says humanitarian, February 8, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNN,_State_Department_says_humanitarian,_February_8,_2025-524" id="mwDZQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZY">[</span>522<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZc">]</span></span></a></sup> However, a February 8 CNN article reported that many waivers were not being acted upon because of staff placed on leave, plus payment systems had been taken over.<sup about="#mwt1795" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNN,_State_Department_says_humanitarian,_February_8,_2025_524-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNN, State Department says humanitarian, February 8, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CNN,_State_Department_says_humanitarian,_February_8,_2025-524"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNN,_State_Department_says_humanitarian,_February_8,_2025-524" id="mwDZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZo">[</span>522<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZs">]</span></span></a></sup> In an interview before the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl_LIX" title="Super Bowl LIX" id="mwDZw">February 9 Super Bowl</a>, Trump said, "Let him take care of the few good ones", referring to Rubio.<sup about="#mwt1798" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AP_News,_Unspent_aid_worth_billions,_Feb_11,_2035_525-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AP News, Unspent aid worth billions, Feb 11, 2035"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AP_News,_Unspent_aid_worth_billions,_Feb_11,_2035-525"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AP_News,_Unspent_aid_worth_billions,_Feb_11,_2035-525" id="mwDZ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDZ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDZ8">[</span>523<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1801" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-526" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-526"}}'><a href="#cite_note-526" id="mwDaE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDaI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaM">[</span>524<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDaQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDaU">On February 13, federal judge <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amir_Ali_(judge)" title="Amir Ali (judge)" id="mwDaY">Amir Ali</a> ordered the Trump administration to continue contracts and grants which were in effect January 19.<sup about="#mwt1804" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_Judge_orders_Trump_administration_to_temporarily_restore_funding,_Feb_13,_2025_527-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, Judge orders Trump administration to temporarily restore funding, Feb 13, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_Judge_orders_Trump_administration_to_temporarily_restore_funding,_Feb_13,_2025-527"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_Judge_orders_Trump_administration_to_temporarily_restore_funding,_Feb_13,_2025-527" id="mwDac"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDak">[</span>525<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDao">]</span></span></a></sup> Chief Justice John Roberts, overseeing cases for the District of Columbia, paused this order.<sup about="#mwt1807" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_Chief_Justice_halts,_Feb_27,_2025_528-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, Chief Justice halts, Feb 27, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_Chief_Justice_halts,_Feb_27,_2025-528"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_Chief_Justice_halts,_Feb_27,_2025-528" id="mwDas"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDaw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDa0">[</span>526<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDa4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1810" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reuters,_Foreign_aid_groups_ask,_Feb_28,_2025_529-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reuters, Foreign aid groups ask, Feb 28, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Reuters,_Foreign_aid_groups_ask,_Feb_28,_2025-529"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reuters,_Foreign_aid_groups_ask,_Feb_28,_2025-529" id="mwDa8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbE">[</span>527<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbI">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 5, the Supreme Court ruled 5–4 that the Trump administration must comply with Judge Ali's order.<sup about="#mwt1811" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_Supreme_Court_won't_lift_lower_court_order,_March_5,_2025_530-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, Supreme Court won&apos;t lift lower court order, March 5, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_Supreme_Court_won't_lift_lower_court_order,_March_5,_2025-530" id="mwDbM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbU">[</span>528<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1814" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-531" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-531"}}'><a href="#cite_note-531" id="mwDbc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbk">[</span>529<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDbo">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the Supreme Court stated that Judge Ali must clarify the payment obligations with "due regard for the feasibility of any compliance timelines".<sup about="#mwt1817" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_Supreme_Court_won't_lift_lower_court_order,_March_5,_2025_530-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, Supreme Court won&apos;t lift lower court order, March 5, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_Supreme_Court_won&apos;t_lift_lower_court_order,_March_5,_2025-530"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_Supreme_Court_won't_lift_lower_court_order,_March_5,_2025-530" id="mwDbs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDbw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDb0">[</span>528<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDb4">]</span></span></a></sup> On March 10, Judge Ali ruled that the Trump administration must pay for completed projects at the rate of 300 back payments a day, meaning four days for all 1,200 back payments, and this being for projects completed by February 13.<sup about="#mwt1820" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Axios,_Judge_holds_Congress_has_power,_March_11,_2025_532-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Axios, Judge holds Congress has power, March 11, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Axios,_Judge_holds_Congress_has_power,_March_11,_2025-532"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Axios,_Judge_holds_Congress_has_power,_March_11,_2025-532" id="mwDb8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcE">[</span>530<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1823" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_&amp;_Associated_Press,_Trump_overstepped,_March_11,_2025_533-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC &amp; Associated Press, Trump overstepped, March 11, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_&amp;_Associated_Press,_Trump_overstepped,_March_11,_2025-533"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_&amp;_Associated_Press,_Trump_overstepped,_March_11,_2025-533" id="mwDcM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDcQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcU">[</span>531<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcY">]</span></span></a></sup> A March 11 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ABC_News_(United_States)" title="ABC News (United States)" id="mwDcc">ABC News</a> article reported that, until recently, no payments were being made because DOGE had disabled the payment system.<sup about="#mwt1824" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_&amp;_Associated_Press,_Trump_overstepped,_March_11,_2025_533-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC &amp; Associated Press, Trump overstepped, March 11, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_&amp;_Associated_Press,_Trump_overstepped,_March_11,_2025-533" id="mwDcg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDck"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDco">[</span>531<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDcs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="75" id="mwDcw" aria-labelledby="Keeping_17%_of_programs"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Keeping_17%_of_programs"><span id="Keeping_17.25_of_programs" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Keeping 17% of programs</h4></div>
<p id="mwDc0">On March 10, Secretary of State <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Rubio" title="Marco Rubio" id="mwDc4">Marco Rubio</a> announced that he was cancelling 83% of USAID programs, or approximately 5,200 out of 6,200 programs. The remaining 1,000 programs (approximately) would be moved to the Department of State.<sup about="#mwt1827" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-534" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-534"}}'><a href="#cite_note-534" id="mwDc8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdE">[</span>532<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1830" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_Secretary_of_state_says_83%,_March_10,_2025_535-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, Secretary of state says 83%, March 10, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_Secretary_of_state_says_83%,_March_10,_2025-535"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_Secretary_of_state_says_83%,_March_10,_2025-535" id="mwDdM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdU">[</span>533<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdY">]</span></span></a></sup> As of late March, DOGE no longer lists the details of canceled USAID contracts on its "Wall of Receipts".<sup about="#mwt1833" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_DOGE_removes_details,_Mar_26,_2025_536-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, DOGE removes details, Mar 26, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS_News,_DOGE_removes_details,_Mar_26,_2025-536"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_DOGE_removes_details,_Mar_26,_2025-536" id="mwDdc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdk">[</span>534<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDdo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDds">DOGE lists approximately $12 billion saved, although a former USAID analyst estimates the actual amount is closer to $6 or $7 billion.<sup about="#mwt1834" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS_News,_DOGE_removes_details,_Mar_26,_2025_536-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS News, DOGE removes details, Mar 26, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS_News,_DOGE_removes_details,_Mar_26,_2025-536" id="mwDdw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDd0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDd4">[</span>534<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDd8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDeA">In early April, USAID announced it was adding back 14 nations to grants under the UN's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Food_Programme" title="World Food Programme" id="mwDeE">World Food Programme</a>. These nations include Lebanon, Syria, Somalia, Jordan, Iraq and Ecuador, plus the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Organization_for_Migration" title="International Organization for Migration" id="mwDeI">International Organization for Migration</a> in the Pacific region.<sup about="#mwt1837" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reuters,_Trump_administration_moves,_April_8,_2025_537-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reuters, Trump administration moves, April 8, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Reuters,_Trump_administration_moves,_April_8,_2025-537"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reuters,_Trump_administration_moves,_April_8,_2025-537" id="mwDeM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDeQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeU">[</span>535<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeY">]</span></span></a></sup> However, food aid was not restored to either Yemen or Afghanistan, with a State Department spokesperson saying this was "based on concern that the funding was benefiting terrorist groups, including the Houthis and the Taliban".<sup about="#mwt1840" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNN,_USAID_reverses_course,_April_9,_2025_538-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNN, USAID reverses course, April 9, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CNN,_USAID_reverses_course,_April_9,_2025-538"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNN,_USAID_reverses_course,_April_9,_2025-538" id="mwDec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDek">[</span>536<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDeo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="76" id="mwDes" aria-labelledby='July_2025_rescissions_("claw_backs"),_but_not_for_PEPFAR'><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id='July_2025_rescissions_("claw_backs"),_but_not_for_PEPFAR'><span id="July_2025_rescissions_.28.22claw_backs.22.29.2C_but_not_for_PEPFAR" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>July 2025 rescissions ("claw backs"), but not for PEPFAR</h4></div>
<p id="mwDew">In June 2025, the White House requested that Congress pass a package of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rescission_bill" title="Rescission bill" id="mwDe0">rescissions</a>, or "claw backs", of approximately $8 billion in foreign aid and $1 billion for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corporation_for_Public_Broadcasting" title="Corporation for Public Broadcasting" id="mwDe4">Corporation for Public Broadcasting</a> including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPR" title="NPR" id="mwDe8">NPR</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PBS" title="PBS" id="mwDfA">PBS</a>.<sup about="#mwt1841" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025_539-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS, Trump&apos;s request to cancel billions, July 15, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025-539" id="mwDfE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfM">[</span>537<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDfU">The House of Representatives passed the cuts as requested. The Senate excluded the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PEPFAR" title="PEPFAR" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDfY">PEPFAR</a> cuts, which is the program started in 2003 during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Presidency_of_George_W._Bush" title="Presidency of George W. Bush" id="mwDfc">presidency of George W Bush</a> to help provide HIV medicines to lower-income countries. The Senate passed two preliminary votes in close 51-50 fashion with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JD_Vance" title="JD Vance" id="mwDfg">Vice President JD Vance</a> casting the tie-breaking votes. A rescission is one of the exceptions to the Senate's 60-vote <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filibuster_in_the_United_States_Senate" title="Filibuster in the United States Senate" id="mwDfk">filibuster</a> rule.<sup about="#mwt1844" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025_539-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CBS, Trump&apos;s request to cancel billions, July 15, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS,_Trump&apos;s_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025-539"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025-539" id="mwDfo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDfs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDfw">[</span>537<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDf0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDf4">President Trump focused on the public broadcasting aspect, criticizing CNN and also "MSDNC" which is a mix of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MSNBC" title="MSNBC" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDf8">MSNBC</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_National_Committee" title="Democratic National Committee" id="mwDgA">DNC</a> (Democratic National Committee). In a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truth_Social" title="Truth Social" id="mwDgE">Truth Social</a> post, he wrote, "It is very important that all Republicans adhere to my Recissions Bill and, in particular, DEFUND THE CORPORATION FOR PUBLIC BROADCASTING (PBS and NPR), which is worse than CNN &amp; MSDNC put together."<sup about="#mwt1845" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025_540-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC, Senate to vote to formalize, July 14, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025-540" id="mwDgI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgQ">[</span>538<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDgY">In a late night session at 2:00 AM on July 17, the Senate voted 51–48 in favor of the cuts. Later that same day, the House of Representatives voted 216 - 213 for the Senate version, meaning PEPFAR was protected in the amount of $400 million.<sup about="#mwt1846" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025_540-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC, Senate to vote to formalize, July 14, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025-540"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025-540" id="mwDgc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgk">[</span>538<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDgo">]</span></span></a></sup> Regarding the cuts to public broadcasting, service to rural areas became one of the political issues.<sup about="#mwt1849" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NBC,_Trump's_cuts_clear_Congress,_July_17,_2025_541-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NBC, Trump&apos;s cuts clear Congress, July 17, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NBC,_Trump&apos;s_cuts_clear_Congress,_July_17,_2025-541"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NBC,_Trump's_cuts_clear_Congress,_July_17,_2025-541" id="mwDgs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDgw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg0">[</span>539<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDg4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="77" id="mwDg8" aria-labelledby="Disaster_response"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Disaster_response">Disaster response</h3></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="78" id="mwDhA" aria-labelledby="Myanmar_earthquake,_March_2025"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Myanmar_earthquake,_March_2025"><span id="Myanmar_earthquake.2C_March_2025" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Myanmar earthquake, March 2025</h4></div>
<p id="mwDhE">President Trump stated the United States would help in response to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Myanmar_earthquake" title="2025 Myanmar earthquake" id="mwDhI">March 28 earthquake in Myanmar</a>, although the question was asked by a former USAID executive of whether or not the United States will beat other countries in getting there with a relief team(s).<sup about="#mwt1852" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-542" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-542"}}'><a href="#cite_note-542" id="mwDhM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDhQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhU">[</span>540<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDhY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="79" id="mwDhc" aria-labelledby="Hurricane_Melissa,_October_2025"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Hurricane_Melissa,_October_2025"><span id="Hurricane_Melissa.2C_October_2025" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Hurricane Melissa, October 2025</h4></div>
<p id="mwDhg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane_Melissa" title="Hurricane Melissa" id="mwDhk">Hurricane Melissa</a> was a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saffir–Simpson_scale" title="Saffir–Simpson scale" id="mwDho">Category 5</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurricane" title="Hurricane" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDhs">hurricane</a> which first made landfall at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jamaica" title="Jamaica" id="mwDhw">Jamaica</a> on October 28, 2025, and then hit other <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean" title="Caribbean" id="mwDh0">Caribbean islands</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Rubio" title="Marco Rubio" id="mwDh4">Secretary of State Rubio</a> activated a disaster assistance response team. By October 31, three U.S. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing_CH-47_Chinook" title="Boeing CH-47 Chinook" id="mwDh8">CH-47 Chinook helicopters</a> were deployed to Jamaica to help with relief efforts, with five more on the way.<sup about="#mwt1855" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-543" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-543"}}'><a href="#cite_note-543" id="mwDiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDiE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiI">[</span>541<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDiM">]</span></span></a></sup> In early November, the State Department promised $12 million in aid to Jamaica, $8 million to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haiti" title="Haiti" id="mwDiQ">Haiti</a>, $3 million to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba" title="Cuba" id="mwDiU">Cuba</a>, and $500,000 to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bahamas" title="The Bahamas" id="mwDiY">The Bahamas</a>.<sup about="#mwt1858" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-544" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-544"}}'><a href="#cite_note-544" id="mwDic"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDik">[</span>542<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDio">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="80" id="mwDis" aria-labelledby="Refugees"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Refugees">Refugees</h3></div>
<p id="mwDiw">On January 20, 2025, Trump signed the executive order named "Securing Our Borders". This order suspends <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parole_(United_States_immigration)#Uniting_for_Ukraine" title="Parole (United States immigration)" id="mwDi0">the Uniting for Ukraine parole program</a>, and no new applications from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukrainian_refugee_crisis" title="Ukrainian refugee crisis" id="mwDi4">Ukrainian refugees</a> with relatives in the United States are being accepted.<sup about="#mwt1861" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-545" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-545"}}'><a href="#cite_note-545" id="mwDi8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjE">[</span>543<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1864" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-546" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-546"}}'><a href="#cite_note-546" id="mwDjM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjU">[</span>544<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDjc">On May 12, 59 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_South_African_refugee_program" title="White South African refugee program" id="mwDjg">white South African refugees arrived</a> from South Africa. The Trump administration has been criticized for fast-tracking their applications while pausing other refugee programs.<sup about="#mwt1867" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ABC_News,_First_group_of_49_white_South_Africans,_May_11,_2025_547-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ABC News, First group of 49 white South Africans, May 11, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_News,_First_group_of_49_white_South_Africans,_May_11,_2025-547"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ABC_News,_First_group_of_49_white_South_Africans,_May_11,_2025-547" id="mwDjk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDjo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjs">[</span>545<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDjw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDj0">The Trump administration slowed the entry of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afghan_refugees" title="Afghan refugees" id="mwDj4">Afghan refugees</a> into the U.S., including persons who had fought on the U.S. side against the Taliban. A leader of an American veterans group said, "these pilots risked everything for America. Their lives are now on the line because of our failure to follow through on our promises."<sup about="#mwt1870" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CNN_News,_Afghan_pilots_who_fought_in_20-year_war_against_Taliban_in_limbo,_March_28,_2025_548-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CNN News, Afghan pilots who fought in 20-year war against Taliban in limbo, March 28, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CNN_News,_Afghan_pilots_who_fought_in_20-year_war_against_Taliban_in_limbo,_March_28,_2025-548"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CNN_News,_Afghan_pilots_who_fought_in_20-year_war_against_Taliban_in_limbo,_March_28,_2025-548" id="mwDj8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkE">[</span>546<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDkI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDkM">On May 12, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_Homeland_Security" title="United States Department of Homeland Security" id="mwDkQ">Department of Homeland Security</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kristi_Noem" title="Kristi Noem" id="mwDkU">Secretary Noem</a> announced that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temporary_protected_status" title="Temporary protected status" id="mwDkY">TPS</a>, or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temporary_Protected_Status" title="Temporary Protected Status" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDkc">temporary protected status</a>, for Afghan refugees would be ended in 60 days, which is the shortest time period permitted by United States law. This decision cited improved conditions in Afghanistan.<sup about="#mwt1871" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-The_Hill,_Trump_administration_ends_protections_from_deportation_for_Afghans,_May_12,_2025_549-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"The Hill, Trump administration ends protections from deportation for Afghans, May 12, 2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-The_Hill,_Trump_administration_ends_protections_from_deportation_for_Afghans,_May_12,_2025-549" id="mwDkg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDkk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDko">[</span>547<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDks">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDkw"><i id="mwDk0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Hill_(newspaper)" title="The Hill (newspaper)" id="mwDk4">The Hill</a></i> reports that the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_High_Commissioner_for_Refugees" title="United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees" id="mwDk8">UN high commissioner for refugees</a> has stated that the situation in Afghanistan has not improved, with a report stating "The large-scale returns are putting even greater pressure on already stretched humanitarian resources." On the other hand, Secretary Noem has pointed to an increase in tourists from China and a drop in the number of Afghans needing assistance from 29 million to 24 million.
<sup about="#mwt1874" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-The_Hill,_Trump_administration_ends_protections_from_deportation_for_Afghans,_May_12,_2025_549-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"The Hill, Trump administration ends protections from deportation for Afghans, May 12, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-The_Hill,_Trump_administration_ends_protections_from_deportation_for_Afghans,_May_12,_2025-549"}}'><a href="#cite_note-The_Hill,_Trump_administration_ends_protections_from_deportation_for_Afghans,_May_12,_2025-549" id="mwDlA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlI">[</span>547<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDlQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox_News" title="Fox News" id="mwDlU">Fox News</a> reported that the leader of "Afghans for Trump", which formed in the aftermath of President Biden's chaotic 2021 withdrawal from Afghanistan, claimed that conditions have not significantly improved and urged President Trump to reconsider.<sup about="#mwt1877" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Fox_News,_'Afghans_for_Trump'_group_feels_abandoned,_May_16,_2025_550-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Fox News, &apos;Afghans for Trump&apos; group feels abandoned, May 16, 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Fox_News,_&apos;Afghans_for_Trump&apos;_group_feels_abandoned,_May_16,_2025-550"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Fox_News,_'Afghans_for_Trump'_group_feels_abandoned,_May_16,_2025-550" id="mwDlY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDlc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlg">[</span>548<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDlk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="81" id="mwDlo" aria-labelledby="Expansionism_and_revanchism"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Expansionism_and_revanchism">Expansionism and revanchism</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1878" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDls" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"American expansionism under Donald Trump"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1879" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1878" id="mwDlw">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_expansionism_under_Donald_Trump" title="American expansionism under Donald Trump">American expansionism under Donald Trump</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDl0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:OTAN_Summit_2025_-_June_25,_2025_(54611827592).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDl4"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:OTAN_Summit_2025_-_June_25,_2025_(54611827592).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/OTAN_Summit_2025_-_June_25%2C_2025_%2854611827592%29.jpg/250px-OTAN_Summit_2025_-_June_25%2C_2025_%2854611827592%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/OTAN_Summit_2025_-_June_25%2C_2025_%2854611827592%29.jpg/500px-OTAN_Summit_2025_-_June_25%2C_2025_%2854611827592%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="6000" data-file-height="4000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDl8"/></a><figcaption id="mwDmA">Trump with NATO general secretary <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Rutte" title="Mark Rutte" id="mwDmE">Mark Rutte</a> at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_The_Hague_NATO_summit" title="2025 The Hague NATO summit" id="mwDmI">2025 The Hague NATO summit</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDmM">In the lead-up to his second inauguration, Trump proposed plans and ideas that would expand the United States' political influence and territory.<sup about="#mwt1882" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-551" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-551"}}'><a href="#cite_note-551" id="mwDmQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDmU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmY">[</span>549<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmc">]</span></span></a></sup> It has been characterized as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donroe_Doctrine" title="Donroe Doctrine" id="mwDmg">a revival of</a> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monroe_Doctrine" title="Monroe Doctrine" id="mwDmk">Monroe Doctrine</a>.<sup about="#mwt1885" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-552" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-552"}}'><a href="#cite_note-552" id="mwDmo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDms"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDmw">[</span>550<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDm0">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_territorial_acquisitions_table" title="United States territorial acquisitions table" id="mwDm4">last territory acquired by the United States was in 1947</a> when the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mariana_Islands" title="Mariana Islands" id="mwDm8">Mariana</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caroline_Islands" title="Caroline Islands" id="mwDnA">Caroline</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marshall_Islands" title="Marshall Islands" id="mwDnE">Marshall Islands</a> were acquired.</p>

<section data-mw-section-id="82" id="mwDnI" aria-labelledby="Canada"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Canada">Canada</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1886" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDnM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Movements for the annexation of Canada to the United States#Proposals to annex Canada by Donald Trump"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1887" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1886" id="mwDnQ">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movements_for_the_annexation_of_Canada_to_the_United_States#Proposals_to_annex_Canada_by_Donald_Trump" title="Movements for the annexation of Canada to the United States" class="mw-redirect">Movements for the annexation of Canada to the United States §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Proposals to annex Canada by Donald Trump</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDnU"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250616DT-0088_President_Donald_Trump_attends_the_G7_Summit_in_Canada.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDnY"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:P20250616DT-0088_President_Donald_Trump_attends_the_G7_Summit_in_Canada.jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/P20250616DT-0088_President_Donald_Trump_attends_the_G7_Summit_in_Canada.jpg/250px-P20250616DT-0088_President_Donald_Trump_attends_the_G7_Summit_in_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/P20250616DT-0088_President_Donald_Trump_attends_the_G7_Summit_in_Canada.jpg/500px-P20250616DT-0088_President_Donald_Trump_attends_the_G7_Summit_in_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="3000" data-file-height="2000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDnc"/></a><figcaption id="mwDng">Trump with Canadian prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Carney" title="Mark Carney" id="mwDnk">Mark Carney</a>, June 2025</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDno">The Trump administration has imposed 25% tariffs on Canadian goods imports that do not fall under <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canada–United_States–Mexico_Agreement" title="Canada–United States–Mexico Agreement" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDns">Canada–United States–Mexico Agreement</a>, with exceptions for steel, aluminum, and Canadian-made passenger vehicle content.<sup about="#mwt1890" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-553" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-553"}}'><a href="#cite_note-553" id="mwDnw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDn0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDn4">[</span>551<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDn8">]</span></span></a></sup> Canadian officials responded with retaliatory 25% tariffs,<sup about="#mwt1893" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-554" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-554"}}'><a href="#cite_note-554" id="mwDoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoI">[</span>552<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1896" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-555" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-555"}}'><a href="#cite_note-555" id="mwDoQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDoU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoY">[</span>553<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDoc">]</span></span></a></sup> and have even proposed cutting off the supply of Canadian energy into the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_United_States" title="Northern United States" id="mwDog">Northern United States</a>.<sup about="#mwt1899" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-556" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-556"}}'><a href="#cite_note-556" id="mwDok"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDoo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDos">[</span>554<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDow">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manitoba" title="Manitoba" id="mwDo0">Manitoba</a> has diverted energy to Canada that it previously supplied to the USA.<sup about="#mwt1902" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-557" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-557"}}'><a href="#cite_note-557" id="mwDo4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDo8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpA">[</span>555<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpE">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Navarro" title="Peter Navarro" id="mwDpI">Peter Navarro</a>, a trade envoy and high-ranking Trump official, has suggested expelling Canada from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Eyes" title="Five Eyes" id="mwDpM">Five Eyes</a> intelligence alliance to increase pressure in the trade war.<sup about="#mwt1905" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-p983_558-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"p983"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-p983-558"}}'><a href="#cite_note-p983-558" id="mwDpQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpY">[</span>556<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDpg">Trump has repeatedly stated his desire for the United States to annex Canada and calling for it to become the 51st state,<sup about="#mwt1908" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-d293_559-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"d293"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-d293-559"}}'><a href="#cite_note-d293-559" id="mwDpk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDpo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDps">[</span>557<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDpw">]</span></span></a></sup> calling former Canadian prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justin_Trudeau" title="Justin Trudeau" id="mwDp0">Justin Trudeau</a> "Governor of the Great State of Canada".<sup about="#mwt1911" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-560" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-560"}}'><a href="#cite_note-560" id="mwDp4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDp8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqA">[</span>558<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqE">]</span></span></a></sup> Trudeau stated to business leaders in Canada that he believes the annexation threats are a "real thing".<sup about="#mwt1914" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-s944_561-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"s944"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-s944-561"}}'><a href="#cite_note-s944-561" id="mwDqI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqQ">[</span>559<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqU">]</span></span></a></sup> The strained relations have led to a "Buy Canadian" movement to boycott American goods and services,<sup about="#mwt1917" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-u378_562-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"u378"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-u378-562"}}'><a href="#cite_note-u378-562" id="mwDqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqg">[</span>560<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqk">]</span></span></a></sup> and booing the American national anthem during international hockey games.<sup about="#mwt1920" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-t749_563-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"t749"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-t749-563"}}'><a href="#cite_note-t749-563" id="mwDqo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDqs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDqw">[</span>561<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDq0">]</span></span></a></sup> When tariffs were implemented on March 4, Trudeau stated that Trump's goal in the trade war was to weaken Canada in order to annex it.<sup about="#mwt1923" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-g713_564-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"g713"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-g713-564"}}'><a href="#cite_note-g713-564" id="mwDq4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDq8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrA">[</span>562<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDrI">On February 8, 2026, Trump threatened to block the opening of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordie_Howe_International_Bridge" title="Gordie Howe International Bridge" id="mwDrM">Gordie Howe International Bridge</a>, citing Canada's recent trade developments with China and the alleged one-sided nature of the contract (wherein Canada gains all revenue from bridge tolls to pay back construction costs). Trump said the bridge's opening will be delayed until multiple trade and bridge related grievances were resolved. Trump's announcement was criticised by politicians, business leaders and industry groups.<sup about="#mwt1926" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-565" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-565"}}'><a href="#cite_note-565" id="mwDrQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrY">[</span>563<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1929" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-566" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-566"}}'><a href="#cite_note-566" id="mwDrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDrk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDro">[</span>564<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDrs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1933" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-567" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-567"}}'><a href="#cite_note-567" id="mwDrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDr0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDr4">[</span>565<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDr8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDsA">On February 12, 2026, the United States House of Representatives voted to repeal the tariffs that had been imposed on Canadian goods during Donald Trump's administration. The resolution passed by a 219–211 vote, with a small number of Republican lawmakers joining nearly all Democrats in support. The tariffs had originally been enacted under a national emergency declaration in February 2025, and their repeal represented a rare bipartisan rebuke of Trump's trade policy. Following the vote, President Trump reportedly threatened political consequences for Republicans who voted against the measure. While passage in the House reflects congressional concern over the tariffs, actual repeal would still require Senate approval and presidential assent, and was expected to face a potential veto.<sup about="#mwt1936" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-568" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-568"}}'><a href="#cite_note-568" id="mwDsE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDsI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsM">[</span>566<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1939" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-569" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-569"}}'><a href="#cite_note-569" id="mwDsU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDsY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsc">[</span>567<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1942" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-570" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-570"}}'><a href="#cite_note-570" id="mwDsk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDso"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDss">[</span>568<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDsw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="83" id="mwDs0" aria-labelledby="Greenland"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Greenland">Greenland</h4></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1943" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDs4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"See also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Greenland crisis"},"2":{"wt":"Proposals for the United States to purchase Greenland"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt1944" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt1943" id="mwDs8">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland_crisis" title="Greenland crisis">Greenland crisis</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proposals_for_the_United_States_to_purchase_Greenland" title="Proposals for the United States to purchase Greenland" class="mw-redirect">Proposals for the United States to purchase Greenland</a></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwDtA"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jens-Frederik_Nielsen_&amp;_Mette_Frederiksen_by_Christian_Ursilva_(3).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwDtE"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Jens-Frederik_Nielsen_&amp;_Mette_Frederiksen_by_Christian_Ursilva_(3).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Jens-Frederik_Nielsen_%26_Mette_Frederiksen_by_Christian_Ursilva_%283%29.jpg/250px-Jens-Frederik_Nielsen_%26_Mette_Frederiksen_by_Christian_Ursilva_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Jens-Frederik_Nielsen_%26_Mette_Frederiksen_by_Christian_Ursilva_%283%29.jpg/500px-Jens-Frederik_Nielsen_%26_Mette_Frederiksen_by_Christian_Ursilva_%283%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="6000" data-file-height="4000" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwDtI"/></a><figcaption id="mwDtM">Greenlandic leader <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jens-Frederik_Nielsen" title="Jens-Frederik Nielsen" id="mwDtQ">Jens Frederik-Nielsen</a> announcing "We choose Denmark" at a January 2026 press conference with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mette_Frederiksen" title="Mette Frederiksen" id="mwDtU">Mette Frederiksen</a> in response to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenland_crisis" title="Greenland crisis" id="mwDtY">Trump's threats to invade or annex</a> the country<sup about="#mwt1947" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-571" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-571"}}'><a href="#cite_note-571" id="mwDtc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDtg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDtk">[</span>569<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDto">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1950" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-572" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-572"}}'><a href="#cite_note-572" id="mwDts"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDtw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDt0">[</span>570<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDt4">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwDt8">In December 2024, Trump stated a further <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proposals_for_the_United_States_to_purchase_Greenland" title="Proposals for the United States to purchase Greenland" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDuA">proposal for the United States to purchase Greenland from Denmark</a>, describing "ownership" and control of the island as "an absolute necessity" for national security purposes. This builds upon a prior offer from Trump to buy Greenland during his first term, which the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_Realm" title="Danish Realm" id="mwDuE">Danish Realm</a> refused, causing him to cancel his August 2019 visit to Denmark.<sup about="#mwt1954" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-573" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-573"}}'><a href="#cite_note-573" id="mwDuI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDuM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuQ">[</span>571<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuU">]</span></span></a></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_lacking_reliable_references" about="#mwt1951" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDuY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Better source needed","href":"./Template:Better_source_needed"},"params":{"reason":{"wt":"See [[WP:NYPOST]]"},"date":{"wt":"February 2025"}},"i":0}}]}'/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_lacking_reliable_references_from_February_2025" about="#mwt1951"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template noprint noexcerpt Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" about="#mwt1951" id="mwDuc"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span><i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Verifiability#Questionable_sources" title="Wikipedia:Verifiability"><span title="See WP:NYPOST (February 2025)">better<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>source<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></sup> On January 7, 2025, Trump's son <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump_Jr." title="Donald Trump Jr." id="mwDug">Donald Trump Jr.</a> visited Greenland's capital city <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuuk" title="Nuuk" id="mwDuk">Nuuk</a> alongside <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charlie_Kirk" title="Charlie Kirk" id="mwDuo">Charlie Kirk</a> to hand out <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MAGA_hat" title="MAGA hat" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDus">MAGA hats</a>.<sup about="#mwt1957" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-574" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-574"}}'><a href="#cite_note-574" id="mwDuw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDu0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDu4">[</span>572<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDu8">]</span></span></a></sup> At a press conference the following day, Trump refused to rule out military or economic force to take over Greenland or the Panama Canal.<sup about="#mwt1960" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Davies-2025_575-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Davies-2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Davies-2025-575"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Davies-2025-575" id="mwDvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvI">[</span>573<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvM">]</span></span></a></sup> However, he did rule out military force in taking over Canada.<sup about="#mwt1961" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Davies-2025_575-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Davies-2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Davies-2025-575" id="mwDvQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvY">[</span>573<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvc">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 14, the Trump-affiliated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nelk" title="Nelk" id="mwDvg">Nelk Boys</a> also visited Nuuk, handing out <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Reserve_Note" title="Federal Reserve Note" id="mwDvk">dollar bills</a> to locals.<sup about="#mwt1964" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-576" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-576"}}'><a href="#cite_note-576" id="mwDvo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDvs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDvw">[</span>574<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDv0">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 16, the CEOs of major Danish companies Novo Nordisk, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vestas" title="Vestas" id="mwDv4">Vestas</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlsberg_Group" title="Carlsberg Group" id="mwDv8">Carlsberg</a> among others were assembled for a crisis meeting in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_State_(Denmark)" title="Ministry of State (Denmark)" id="mwDwA">Ministry of State</a> to discuss the situation.<sup about="#mwt1967" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-577" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-577"}}'><a href="#cite_note-577" id="mwDwE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDwI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwM">[</span>575<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1970" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-578" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-578"}}'><a href="#cite_note-578" id="mwDwU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDwY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwc">[</span>576<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwDwk">On the subsequent day, former chief executive <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friis_Arne_Petersen" title="Friis Arne Petersen" id="mwDwo">Friis Arne Petersen</a> in the Danish <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Foreign_Affairs_(Denmark)" title="Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Denmark)" id="mwDws">Ministry of Foreign Affairs</a> described the situation as "historically unheard of", while <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noa_Redington" title="Noa Redington" id="mwDww">Noa Redington</a>, special adviser to former prime minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helle_Thorning-Schmidt" title="Helle Thorning-Schmidt" id="mwDw0">Helle Thorning-Schmidt</a>, compared the international pressure on Denmark that during the 2005 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jyllands-Posten_Muhammad_cartoons_controversy" title="Jyllands-Posten Muhammad cartoons controversy" id="mwDw4"><i id="mwDw8">Jyllands-Posten</i> Muhammad cartoons controversy</a>.<sup about="#mwt1973" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-579" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-579"}}'><a href="#cite_note-579" id="mwDxA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxI">[</span>577<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxM">]</span></span></a></sup> On February 12, 2025, a bill was introduced in Congress to advance efforts to acquire Greenland and rename it Red, White, and Blueland.<sup about="#mwt1976" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-580" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-580"}}'><a href="#cite_note-580" id="mwDxQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxY">[</span>578<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxc">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's actions against Greenland have been described as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hybrid_warfare" title="Hybrid warfare" id="mwDxg">hybrid warfare</a> by academics and analysts.<sup about="#mwt1979" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-dab_581-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"dab"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-dab-581"}}'><a href="#cite_note-dab-581" id="mwDxk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxs">[</span>579<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxw">]</span></span></a></sup> Prime Minister <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mette_Frederiksen" title="Mette Frederiksen" id="mwDx0">Mette Frederiksen</a> said that "the Kingdom of Denmark—and thus Greenland—is a member of NATO and is therefore covered by the Alliance's <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Atlantic_Treaty#Article_5" title="North Atlantic Treaty" id="mwDx4">collective security guarantee</a> ... I ... strongly urge the United States to cease its threats against a historically close ally."<sup about="#mwt1982" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-mefr_582-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"mefr"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-mefr-582"}}'><a href="#cite_note-mefr-582" id="mwDx8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyE">[</span>580<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyI">]</span></span></a></sup> The official Danish threat assessment published by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Danish_Defence_Intelligence_Service" title="Danish Defence Intelligence Service" id="mwDyM">Danish Defence Intelligence Service</a> in 2025 for the first time mentioned the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mwDyQ">United States</a> as a threat to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_security" title="National security" id="mwDyU">national security</a>, alongside <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia" title="Russia" id="mwDyY">Russia</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China" title="China" id="mwDyc">China</a>.<sup about="#mwt1985" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-politico_583-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"politico"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-politico-583"}}'><a href="#cite_note-politico-583" id="mwDyg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDyk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyo">[</span>581<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDys">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1988" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-584" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-584"}}'><a href="#cite_note-584" id="mwDyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDy0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDy4">[</span>582<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDy8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1991" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-585" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-585"}}'><a href="#cite_note-585" id="mwDzA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDzE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzI">[</span>583<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzM">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2026 Greenland and Denmark saw massive <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-Trump_protests" title="Anti-Trump protests" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDzQ">anti-Trump protests</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hands_off_Greenland" title="Hands off Greenland" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDzU">Hands off Greenland</a> protests, where protesters chanted "Greenland is not for sale".<sup about="#mwt1994" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-586" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-586"}}'><a href="#cite_note-586" id="mwDzY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDzc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzg">[</span>584<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1997" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-587" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-587"}}'><a href="#cite_note-587" id="mwDzo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDzs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDzw">[</span>585<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDz0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2000" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-588" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-588"}}'><a href="#cite_note-588" id="mwDz4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDz8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0A">[</span>586<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="84" id="mwD0I" aria-labelledby="Panama_Canal"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="Panama_Canal">Panama Canal</h4></div>
<p id="mwD0M">In 2024, Trump demanded that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panama" title="Panama" id="mwD0Q">Panama</a> return control of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panama_Canal" title="Panama Canal" id="mwD0U">Panama Canal</a> to the United States because "excessive rates" were being charged for American passage.<sup about="#mwt2003" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-589" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-589"}}'><a href="#cite_note-589" id="mwD0Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD0c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0g">[</span>587<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD0k">]</span></span></a></sup> The United States previously was in control of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Panama_Canal_Zone" title="Panama Canal Zone" id="mwD0o">Panama Canal Zone</a> from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hay–Bunau-Varilla_Treaty" title="Hay–Bunau-Varilla Treaty" id="mwD0s">1903</a> until <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torrijos–Carter_Treaties" title="Torrijos–Carter Treaties" id="mwD0w">1999</a>, and has <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_invasion_of_Panama" title="United States invasion of Panama" id="mwD00">invaded Panama before in 1989</a>.<sup about="#mwt2006" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-590" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-590"}}'><a href="#cite_note-590" id="mwD04"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD08"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1A">[</span>588<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1E">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2009" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-591" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-591"}}'><a href="#cite_note-591" id="mwD1I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1Q">[</span>589<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1U">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump told Congress in March 2025 that his administration "will be reclaiming the Panama Canal".<sup about="#mwt2012" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-592" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-592"}}'><a href="#cite_note-592" id="mwD1Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1g">[</span>590<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1k">]</span></span></a></sup> Also that month, Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth instructed the Trump administration to "immediately" present "credible military options to ensure fair and unfettered US military and commercial access to the Panama Canal".<sup about="#mwt2015" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-593" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-593"}}'><a href="#cite_note-593" id="mwD1o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD1s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD1w">[</span>591<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD10">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="85" id="mwD14" aria-labelledby="United_Nations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="United_Nations">United Nations</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwD18"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Trump_and_Vice_President_Vance_at_the_Board_of_Peace_meeting_(HBnh7p0XgAI3n-C).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwD2A"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Trump_and_Vice_President_Vance_at_the_Board_of_Peace_meeting_(HBnh7p0XgAI3n-C).jpg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/President_Trump_and_Vice_President_Vance_at_the_Board_of_Peace_meeting_%28HBnh7p0XgAI3n-C%29.jpg/250px-President_Trump_and_Vice_President_Vance_at_the_Board_of_Peace_meeting_%28HBnh7p0XgAI3n-C%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/President_Trump_and_Vice_President_Vance_at_the_Board_of_Peace_meeting_%28HBnh7p0XgAI3n-C%29.jpg/500px-President_Trump_and_Vice_President_Vance_at_the_Board_of_Peace_meeting_%28HBnh7p0XgAI3n-C%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="2048" data-file-height="1365" data-file-type="bitmap" height="167" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwD2E"/></a><figcaption id="mwD2I">Trump and other leaders during the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Board_of_Peace" title="Board of Peace" id="mwD2M">Board of Peace</a> meeting in Davos, Switzerland, February 2026</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwD2Q">On July 22, 2025, the United States informed of its decision to withdraw from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNESCO" title="UNESCO" id="mwD2U">UNESCO</a>, effective December 31, 2026.<sup about="#mwt2018" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-594" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-594"}}'><a href="#cite_note-594" id="mwD2Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD2c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2g">[</span>592<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2k">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2021" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-us_withdrawal_595-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"us withdrawal"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-us_withdrawal-595"}}'><a href="#cite_note-us_withdrawal-595" id="mwD2o"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD2s"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD2w">[</span>593<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD20">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2024" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-596" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-596"}}'><a href="#cite_note-596" id="mwD24"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD28"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3A">[</span>594<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3E">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwD3I">In a presidential memorandum issued on January 7, 2026, Donald Trump directed to start the process of withdrawal of the US from the 66 organizations, agencies and commissions of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations" title="United Nations" id="mwD3M">United Nations</a>, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UN_Framework_Convention_on_Climate_Change" title="UN Framework Convention on Climate Change" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD3Q">UN Framework Convention on Climate Change</a> (UNFCCC), calling them "contrary to the interests of the United States".<sup about="#mwt2027" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-WH_597-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"WH"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WH-597"}}'><a href="#cite_note-WH-597" id="mwD3U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD3Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3c">[</span>595<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3g">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2030" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-598" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-598"}}'><a href="#cite_note-598" id="mwD3k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD3o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3s">[</span>596<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD3w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<section data-mw-section-id="86" id="mwD30" aria-labelledby="World_Health_Organization"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading4"><h4 id="World_Health_Organization">World Health Organization</h4></div>
<p id="mwD34">On January 22, 2026, President Donald Trump completed the withdrawal of the United States from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Health_Organization" title="World Health Organization" id="mwD38">World Health Organization</a> (WHO), a specialized agency of the United Nations, a year after he signed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Executive_Order_14155" title="Executive Order 14155" id="mwD4A">Executive Order 14155</a> on January 20, 2025. As announced by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_Health_and_Human_Services" title="United States Department of Health and Human Services" id="mwD4E">Department of Health and Human Services</a>, the United States officially exited the organization, ending its 78-year membership and halting all U.S. funding and participation in the WHO's governance and activities.<sup about="#mwt2033" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HHS_599-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HHS"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HHS-599"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HHS-599" id="mwD4I"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD4M"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4Q">[</span>597<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4U">]</span></span></a></sup> Although the organization hoped for a reconsideration the day after Trump's executive order,<sup about="#mwt2036" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-600" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-600"}}'><a href="#cite_note-600" id="mwD4Y"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD4c"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4g">[</span>598<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD4k">]</span></span></a></sup> the administration continued with the decision.</p>

<p id="mwD4o">The administration justified the withdrawal by citing concerns about the WHO's handling of global health emergencies, including the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwD4s">COVID-19 pandemic</a>, its resistance to reforms, and its failure to operate independently from inappropriate political influence of other WHO member states.<sup about="#mwt2037" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HHS_599-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HHS"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HHS-599" id="mwD4w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD40"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD44">[</span>597<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD48">]</span></span></a></sup> In a joint statement by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secretary_of_state_(U.S._state_government)" title="Secretary of state (U.S. state government)" id="mwD5A">Secretary of State</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marco_Rubio" title="Marco Rubio" id="mwD5E">Marco Rubio</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secretary_of_Health_and_Human_Services" title="Secretary of Health and Human Services" class="mw-redirect" id="mwD5I">Secretary of Health and Human Services</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_F._Kennedy_Jr." title="Robert F. Kennedy Jr." id="mwD5M">Robert F. Kennedy Jr.</a>, they said that the WHO "tarnished and trashed everything that America has done for it" and it "abandoned its core mission and acted repeatedly against the interests of the United States", including the failure to "hand over the American flag that hung in front of it".<sup about="#mwt2040" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-601" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-601"}}'><a href="#cite_note-601" id="mwD5Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD5U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5Y">[</span>599<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5c">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwD5g">The United States still owes outstanding dues to the WHO from 2024 to 2025, raising questions about the legality and financial implications of the exit.<sup about="#mwt2043" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-602" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-602"}}'><a href="#cite_note-602" id="mwD5k"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD5o"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5s">[</span>600<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD5w">]</span></span></a></sup> Being one of the biggest donors to the WHO, the country's unpaid fees of estimated $260 million has already caused massive job losses at the organization. However, as a response, Washington said they saw no reason to comply.<sup about="#mwt2046" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-603" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-603"}}'><a href="#cite_note-603" id="mwD50"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD54"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD58">[</span>601<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwD6E">Ronald G. Nahass, president of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infectious_Diseases_Society_of_America" title="Infectious Diseases Society of America" id="mwD6I">Infectious Diseases Society of America</a> (IDSA), criticized the withdrawal, calling it "a shortsighted and misguided abandonment of our global health commitments" and "scientifically reckless". He emphasized that "It fails to acknowledge the fundamental natural history of infectious diseases" and that "Global cooperation and communication are critical to keep our own citizens protected because germs do not respect borders," adding that global cooperation is "not a luxury" but a "biological necessity".<sup about="#mwt2049" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-604" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-604"}}'><a href="#cite_note-604" id="mwD6M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD6Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6U">[</span>602<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD6Y">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id="87" id="mwD6c" aria-labelledby="Ethics"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Ethics">Ethics</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2050" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD6g" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"see also","href":"./Template:See_also"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"First presidency of Donald Trump#Ethics"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2051" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2050" id="mwD6k">See also: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_presidency_of_Donald_Trump#Ethics" title="First presidency of Donald Trump">First presidency of Donald Trump §<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>Ethics</a></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="88" id="mwD6o" aria-labelledby="Corruption_allegations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Corruption_allegations">Corruption allegations</h3></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt2052" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwD6s" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:Excerpt","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"main"},"2":{"wt":"only=paragraphs"},"3":{"wt":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-empty-elt"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1353838603" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt2053" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Excerpt/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output .excerpt-hat .mw-editsection-like{font-style:normal}</style><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2054" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency" title="Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency">Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p>Trump's second presidency has faced unprecedented conflicts of interest, self-enrichment, and allegations of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corruption" title="Corruption">corruption</a> unrivaled in American history from historians, legal experts, and federal judges.<sup about="#mwt2176" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-626" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":""},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-626"}}'><a href="#cite_note-626" id="mwD6w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD60"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD64">[</span>624<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD68">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>His administration has faced widespread <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insider_trading_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Insider trading allegations during the second Trump administration">allegations of insider trading</a> and raised conflict of interest concerns due to business dealings by Trump's son-in-law <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jared_Kushner" title="Jared Kushner">Jared Kushner</a> and his cabinet.<sup about="#mwt2230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_theguardian.com_627-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency theguardian.com"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_theguardian.com-627"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_theguardian.com-627" id="mwD7A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7I">[</span>625<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2235" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_nytimes.com_628-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency nytimes.com"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_nytimes.com-628"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_nytimes.com-628" id="mwD7Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7Y">[</span>626<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7c">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2240" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_212025_629-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Lipton 212025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_212025-629"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_212025-629" id="mwD7g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD7k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7o">[</span>627<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD7s">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's grants of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_people_granted_executive_clemency_in_the_second_Trump_presidency" title="List of people granted executive clemency in the second Trump presidency">pardons and clemency</a> have favored political allies and loyalists, with several given after millions in donations or fees.<sup about="#mwt2245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-630" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-630"}}'><a href="#cite_note-630" id="mwD7w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD70"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD74">[</span>628<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD78">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2250" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_axios.com_631-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency axios.com"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_axios.com-631"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_axios.com-631" id="mwD8A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD8E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8I">[</span>629<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2255" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Thrush_May292025_632-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Thrush May292025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Thrush_May292025-632"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Thrush_May292025-632" id="mwD8Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD8U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8Y">[</span>630<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8c">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump has proactively solicited donations from companies and individuals following which favorable regulatory actions and decisions have occurred.<sup about="#mwt2258" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Dawsey 08102026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" id="mwD8g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD8k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8o">[</span>607<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD8s">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump has maintained an active stock market account with thousands of trades totaling hundreds of millions of dollars.<sup about="#mwt2262" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_nbcnews.com_633-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency nbcnews.com"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_nbcnews.com-633"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_nbcnews.com-633" id="mwD8w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD80"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD84">[</span>631<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD88">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump has directly benefited by soliciting his own memecoin <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/$TRUMP" title="$TRUMP" class="mw-redirect">$TRUMP</a> and benefitted from his family's cryptocurrency company <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Liberty_Financial" title="World Liberty Financial">World Liberty Financial</a> which has received investments by anonymous individuals and foreign governments.<sup about="#mwt2267" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_04292025_634-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Lipton 04292025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_04292025-634"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_04292025-634" id="mwD9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD9E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9I">[</span>632<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9M">]</span></span></a></sup> As of his July 2026 financial report, Trump made over $2.2B in 2025 compared to $622M in 2024, of which $1.4B came from his family's cryptocurrency business.<sup about="#mwt2272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Protess_06302026_635-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Protess 06302026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Protess_06302026-635"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Protess_06302026-635" id="mwD9Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD9U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9Y">[</span>633<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9c">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump has received an unusually large number of expensive gifts, such as a $400M <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing_VC-25B_Bridge" title="Boeing VC-25B Bridge">jet from Qatar</a> or gold bars, which some scholars view as a violation of the emoluments clause of the Constitution.<sup about="#mwt2277" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_npr.org_636-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency npr.org"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_npr.org-636"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_npr.org-636" id="mwD9g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD9k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9o">[</span>634<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD9s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2282" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_thetimes.com_637-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency thetimes.com"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_thetimes.com-637"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_thetimes.com-637" id="mwD9w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD90"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD94">[</span>635<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD98">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>Trump's second term has been described by political commentators as having fewer prohibitions on business activity and guardrails against potential conflicts of interest than his first, and for having more opportunities to directly influence Trump.<sup about="#mwt2287" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Yourish_2025_638-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Yourish 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Yourish_2025-638"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Yourish_2025-638" id="mwD-A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-I">[</span>636<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2292" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Schouten_2025_639-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Schouten 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Schouten_2025-639"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Schouten_2025-639" id="mwD-Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-Y">[</span>637<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-c">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump repealed and rolled back anti-corruption measures and ethical standards for himself and his allies, dropped corruption charges against political figures with ties to him, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_dismissals_of_U.S._inspectors_general" title="2025 dismissals of U.S. inspectors general">fired inspectors generals</a> investigating fraud and abuse. <i>The New York Times</i> described Trump as making up statistics "out of thin air", and for accusing government agencies and "anyone he disfavors of corruption and even criminality without proof".<sup about="#mwt2297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-640" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-640"}}'><a href="#cite_note-640" id="mwD-g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-o">[</span>638<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-s">]</span></span></a></sup> His second presidency was described as breaking with decades of ethical norms,<sup about="#mwt2302" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_02172025_641-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Lipton 02172025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_02172025-641"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_02172025-641" id="mwD-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD-0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-4">[</span>639<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD-8">]</span></span></a></sup> and raising substantial corruption concerns.<sup about="#mwt2307" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Savage_05122025_642-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Savage 05122025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Savage_05122025-642"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Savage_05122025-642" id="mwD_A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_E"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_I">[</span>640<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_M">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2310" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025_610-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Stringer 05182025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610" id="mwD_Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_U"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_Y">[</span>608<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_c">]</span></span></a></sup> Congressional Republicans have largely downplayed or ignored the concerns.<sup about="#mwt2314" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-643" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-643"}}'><a href="#cite_note-643" id="mwD_g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_o">[</span>641<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_s">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2317" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_02172025_641-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Lipton 02172025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lipton_02172025-641" id="mwD_w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwD_0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_4">[</span>639<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwD_8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>Federal judges found many of the administration's actions to be illegal and unconstitutional,<sup about="#mwt2349" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-650" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"group":""},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-650"}}'><a href="#cite_note-650" id="mwEAA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEAE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAI">[</span>648<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAM">]</span></span></a></sup> and by mid-July, a <i><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Washington_Post" title="Washington Post" class="mw-redirect">Washington Post</a></i> analysis found he defied judges and the courts in roughly one third of all cases against him, actions which were described by legal experts as unprecedented for any presidential administration.<sup about="#mwt2365" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025_651-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Jouvenal 07212025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025-651"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025-651" id="mwEAQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEAU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAY">[</span>649<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAc">]</span></span></a></sup> His defiance of court orders and a claimed right to disobey the courts raised fears among legal experts of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitutional_crisis" title="Constitutional crisis">constitutional crisis</a>.<sup about="#mwt2370" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-652" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-652"}}'><a href="#cite_note-652" id="mwEAg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEAk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAo">[</span>650<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEAs">]</span></span></a></sup> An August 2026 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters" title="Reuters">Reuters</a>/<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipsos" title="Ipsos">Ipsos</a> poll found a majority of Americans believe that Trump and his family "have inappropriately profited from cryptocurrency since his return to power and that his policy decisions are influenced by his private business dealings".<sup about="#mwt2375" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-653" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-653"}}'><a href="#cite_note-653" id="mwEAw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEA0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA4">[</span>651<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts"/>
</div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="89" id="mwEBA" aria-labelledby="Alleged_conflict_of_interest"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Alleged_conflict_of_interest">Alleged conflict of interest</h3></div>
<p id="mwEBE">In September 2026, a Powerus delegation met General <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asim_Munir" title="Asim Munir" id="mwEBI">Asim Munir</a> and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Memorandum_of_understanding" title="Memorandum of understanding" id="mwEBM">MoU</a> was signed between the Pakistan Army and the Trump-family backed drone maker while the company was due to merge with Aureus Greenway Holdings linked to Eric Trump and Donald Trump Jr. However, Andrew Fox, Powerus' founder, denied that "the company's growth was linked to the involvement of Trump's sons."<sup about="#mwt2380" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-654" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-654"}}'><a href="#cite_note-654" id="mwEBQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEBU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBY">[</span>652<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2383" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-655" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-655"}}'><a href="#cite_note-655" id="mwEBg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEBk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBo">[</span>653<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEBs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="90" id="mwEBw" aria-labelledby="Pardons_and_commutations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Pardons_and_commutations">Pardons and commutations</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2384" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEB0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Further","href":"./Template:Further"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"List of people granted executive clemency in the second Trump presidency"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2385" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2384" id="mwEB4">Further information: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_people_granted_executive_clemency_in_the_second_Trump_presidency" title="List of people granted executive clemency in the second Trump presidency">List of people granted executive clemency in the second Trump presidency</a></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt2386" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEB8" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:Excerpt","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"main"},"2":{"wt":"only=paragraphs"},"3":{"wt":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency#Pardons and commutations"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353838603" about="#mwt2387" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Excerpt/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2388" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency#Pardons_and_commutations" title="Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency">Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency § Pardons and commutations</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p>As of November<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>2025<sup class="plainlinks noexcerpt noprint asof-tag update" style="display:none;"><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Second_presidency_of_Donald_Trump&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Second_presidency_of_Donald_Trump&amp;action=edit"><span typeof="mw:Entity">[</span>update<span typeof="mw:Entity">]</span></a></sup> Trump had issued nearly two thousand pardons and commutations<sup about="#mwt2391" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-656" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-656"}}'><a href="#cite_note-656" id="mwECA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwECE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECI">[</span>654<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECM">]</span></span></a></sup> including for some prosecuted during his first presidency.<sup about="#mwt2396" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-657" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-657"}}'><a href="#cite_note-657" id="mwECQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwECU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECY">[</span>655<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECc">]</span></span></a></sup> His grant of pardons outpaced those of prior presidents.<sup about="#mwt2399" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026_658-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Ava 08102026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026-658" id="mwECg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwECk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECo">[</span>656<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwECs">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump's pardons and grants of clemency favored political allies and loyalists.<sup about="#mwt2403" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_axios.com_631-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency axios.com"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_axios.com-631"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_axios.com-631" id="mwECw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEC0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEC4">[</span>629<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEC8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2408" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Thrush_May292025_632-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Thrush May292025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Thrush_May292025-632"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Thrush_May292025-632" id="mwEDA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEDE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDI">[</span>630<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDM">]</span></span></a></sup> Lobbyists have told the Wall Street Journal and other news outlets that fees of $1M are standard. Some would-be pardon recipients have offered success fees of $6M for a successful application.<sup about="#mwt2413" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-659" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-659"}}'><a href="#cite_note-659" id="mwEDQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEDU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDY">[</span>657<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2418" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-660" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-660"}}'><a href="#cite_note-660" id="mwEDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEDk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDo">[</span>658<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEDs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2423" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-661" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-661"}}'><a href="#cite_note-661" id="mwEDw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwED0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwED4">[</span>659<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwED8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>Trump frequently bypassed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_of_the_Pardon_Attorney" title="Office of the Pardon Attorney">Office of the Pardon Attorney</a>, and on March 7, 2025, fired its leader, Department of Justice career attorney Liz Oyer, and installed political loyalist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ed_Martin_(Missouri_politician)" title="Ed Martin (Missouri politician)">Ed Martin</a> in the role.<sup about="#mwt2428" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-662" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-662"}}'><a href="#cite_note-662" id="mwEEA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEEE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEI">[</span>660<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2433" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-663" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-663"}}'><a href="#cite_note-663" id="mwEEQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEEU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEY">[</span>661<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEc">]</span></span></a></sup> Ed Martin described the rationale for granting pardons as "No MAGA left behind".<sup about="#mwt2438" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-664" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-664"}}'><a href="#cite_note-664" id="mwEEg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEEk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEo">[</span>662<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEEs">]</span></span></a></sup> In April 2025, Oyer testified to the Senate and accused the Justice Department of "ongoing corruption" and that "the leadership of the Department of Justice appears to value political loyalty above the fair and responsible administration of justice".<sup about="#mwt2443" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-665" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-665"}}'><a href="#cite_note-665" id="mwEEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEE0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEE4">[</span>663<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEE8">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2025, Trump pardoned 42 people charged with white-collar crimes. As of late January 2026, he had pardoned an additional 10 white collar criminals.<sup about="#mwt2448" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-666" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-666"}}'><a href="#cite_note-666" id="mwEFA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEFE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFI">[</span>664<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFM">]</span></span></a></sup> In April 2026, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wall_Street_Journal" title="The Wall Street Journal">The Wall Street Journal</a> reported that Trump "repeatedly promised his top administration officials pardons before he leaves office".<sup about="#mwt2453" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-667" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-667"}}'><a href="#cite_note-667" id="mwEFQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEFU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFY">[</span>665<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFc">]</span></span></a></sup> In June 2026, a Reuters investigation found 96% of clemency grants failed to meet longstanding Department of Justice guidelines for such requests, that they were based on partisan and personal criteria, and that there was evidence of payments being used to solicit them.<sup about="#mwt2458" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-668" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-668"}}'><a href="#cite_note-668" id="mwEFg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEFk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFo">[</span>666<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEFs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>Trump was the first president in modern American history to issue pardons for businesses, and by July 2026 had issued nine and wiped out $200 million in penalties, some of which was destined for victims of wrongdoing.<sup about="#mwt2461" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026_658-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Ava 08102026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026-658" id="mwEFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEF0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEF4">[</span>656<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEF8">]</span></span></a></sup> Bloomberg highlighted the case of HDR Global Trading, which owned crypto platform <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BitMEX" title="BitMEX">BitMEX</a> and was the first company pardoned instead of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_person" title="Natural person">natural person</a>.<sup about="#mwt2465" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-669" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-669"}}'><a href="#cite_note-669" id="mwEGA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGI">[</span>667<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2468" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026_658-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Ava 08102026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026-658" id="mwEGQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGY">[</span>656<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGc">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 15, 2025, BitMEX was fined $100 million for violating anti-money laundering laws after pleading guilty in July 2024.<sup about="#mwt2472" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-670" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-670"}}'><a href="#cite_note-670" id="mwEGg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEGk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGo">[</span>668<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEGs">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2477" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-671" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-671"}}'><a href="#cite_note-671" id="mwEGw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEG0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEG4">[</span>669<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEG8">]</span></span></a></sup> That month, the exchange launched a swap listing tied to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/$TRUMP" title="$TRUMP" class="mw-redirect">$TRUMP</a> memecoin and its founder penned an essay which Bloomberg described as "framing the president's embrace of meme coins as a move toward bolstering political accountability". On March 27, 2025, Trump signed pardons for four BitMEX executives and pardoned the company the same week the $100 million fine was due.<sup about="#mwt2482" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026_658-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Ava 08102026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026-658"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Ava_08102026-658" id="mwEHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEHE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHI">[</span>656<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts"/>
</div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="91" id="mwEHQ" aria-labelledby="Branding_of_institutions"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Branding_of_institutions">Branding of institutions</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2485" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEHU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Branding of United States government programs and facilities after Donald Trump"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2486" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2485" id="mwEHY">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Branding_of_United_States_government_programs_and_facilities_after_Donald_Trump" title="Branding of United States government programs and facilities after Donald Trump">Branding of United States government programs and facilities after Donald Trump</a></div>
<p id="mwEHc">Trump, long known before he took elective office for labeling his companies' properties and merchandise with his name or image,<sup about="#mwt2489" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-672" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-672"}}'><a href="#cite_note-672" id="mwEHg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEHk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHo">[</span>670<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEHs">]</span></span></a></sup> has controversially continued the practice in public life in his second presidential term, in some cases by altering existing names or images.</p>

<p id="mwEHw">Soon after the term began, Trump's portrait appeared on large banners hung from three federal buildings in Washington, D.C.; U.S. Sen. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Schiff" title="Adam Schiff" id="mwEH0">Adam Schiff</a> (D.-Calif.) objected that the banners violated “a longstanding legal prohibition against the use of federal funds for propaganda and self-aggrandizement purposes.”<sup about="#mwt2492" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-673" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-673"}}'><a href="#cite_note-673" id="mwEH4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEH8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIA">[</span>671<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIE">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump also promptly dismissed the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_F._Kennedy_Center_for_the_Performing_Arts" title="John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEII">Kennedy Center</a>'s board of trustees, then selected a replacement board, which voted in December to rename the center the Donald J. Trump and the John F. Kennedy Memorial Center for the Performing Arts; its signage was altered to reflect the new name. The change drew criticism from politicians in Congress, some of them in Trump's own party; House <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minority_leader" title="Minority leader" id="mwEIM">minority leader</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hakeem_Jeffries" title="Hakeem Jeffries" id="mwEIQ">Hakeem Jeffries</a> (D-N.Y.) declared that the board had “no authority to actually rename the Kennedy Center in the absence of legislative action,”<sup about="#mwt2495" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-674" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-674"}}'><a href="#cite_note-674" id="mwEIU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEIY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIc">[</span>672<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIg">]</span></span></a></sup> and a federal judge later ordered that Trump's name be removed.<sup about="#mwt2498" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-675" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-675"}}'><a href="#cite_note-675" id="mwEIk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEIo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIs">[</span>673<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEIw">]</span></span></a></sup> The new board had appointed Trump himself to its chairmanship, a first for a president.<sup about="#mwt2501" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-676" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-676"}}'><a href="#cite_note-676" id="mwEI0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEI4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEI8">[</span>674<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJA">]</span></span></a></sup> That month, Trump also set his name on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Institute_of_Peace" title="United States Institute of Peace" id="mwEJE">U.S. Institute of Peace</a> (USIP), renaming it the Donald J. Trump Institute of Peace, and its signage, too, was so altered. Trump had recently fired not only the USIP's board but its every employee, turning control of its headquarters over to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Services_Administration" title="General Services Administration" id="mwEJI">General Services Administration</a>.<sup about="#mwt2504" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-677" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-677"}}'><a href="#cite_note-677" id="mwEJM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJU">[</span>675<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJY">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump further announced that month a plan for a new fleet of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Navy" title="United States Navy" id="mwEJc">naval</a> vessels, to be called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trump-class_battleship" title="Trump-class battleship" id="mwEJg">Trump-class battleships</a>, although battleships have long been obsolete in naval warfare<sup about="#mwt2507" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-678" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-678"}}'><a href="#cite_note-678" id="mwEJk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEJo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJs">[</span>676<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2510" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-679" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-679"}}'><a href="#cite_note-679" id="mwEJ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEJ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEJ8">[</span>677<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKA">]</span></span></a></sup> and the Navy's last one in service was decommissioned in 1992.<sup about="#mwt2513" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-680" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-680"}}'><a href="#cite_note-680" id="mwEKE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEKI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKM">[</span>678<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEKU">For many years, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Park_Service" title="National Park Service" id="mwEKY">National Park Service</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/America_the_Beautiful_Pass" title="America the Beautiful Pass" id="mwEKc">annual general pass</a> depicted natural landscapes, but the new 2026 pass design for U.S. residents has a photo of Donald Trump.<sup about="#mwt2516" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-681" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-681"}}'><a href="#cite_note-681" id="mwEKg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEKk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKo">[</span>679<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEKs">]</span></span></a></sup> The redesign triggered a popular backlash of passholders' covering his photo with stickers; the Park Service responded by updating its ban on defaced passes to include anything obscuring the front.<sup about="#mwt2519" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-682" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-682"}}'><a href="#cite_note-682" id="mwEKw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEK0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEK4">[</span>680<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEK8">]</span></span></a></sup> The year also marked the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_the_Treasury" title="United States Department of the Treasury" id="mwELA">Treasury</a>'s announcement that Trump's own signature would replace that of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treasurer_of_the_United_States" title="Treasurer of the United States" id="mwELE">treasurer</a> on paper currency, another first for a president;<sup about="#mwt2522" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-683" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-683"}}'><a href="#cite_note-683" id="mwELI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwELM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELQ">[</span>681<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELU">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_State" title="United States Department of State" id="mwELY">State Department</a>’s issuance of a new passport design with a portrait of Trump, the first living president to appear on a U.S. passport, offered as an option to in-person applicants at the Washington, D.C., Passport Agency;<sup about="#mwt2525" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-684" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-684"}}'><a href="#cite_note-684" id="mwELc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwELg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELk">[</span>682<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwELo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2528" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-685" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-685"}}'><a href="#cite_note-685" id="mwELs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwELw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEL0">[</span>683<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEL4">]</span></span></a></sup> and Florida Gov. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_DeSantis" title="Ron DeSantis" id="mwEL8">Ron DeSantis</a>'s consent to renaming <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palm_Beach_International_Airport" title="Palm Beach International Airport" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEMA">Palm Beach International Airport</a> after Trump,<sup about="#mwt2531" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-686" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-686"}}'><a href="#cite_note-686" id="mwEME"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEMI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMM">[</span>684<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMQ">]</span></span></a></sup> a change the president had reportedly sought in 2020.<sup about="#mwt2534" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-687" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-687"}}'><a href="#cite_note-687" id="mwEMU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEMY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMc">[</span>685<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEMg">]</span></span></a></sup> Other measures bearing Trump’s name are <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trump_account" title="Trump account" id="mwEMk">Trump accounts</a>, tax-advantaged investment accounts for American minors rolled out as part of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/One_Big_Beautiful_Bill_Act" title="One Big Beautiful Bill Act" id="mwEMo">One Big Beautiful Bill Act</a>; <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TrumpRx" title="TrumpRx" id="mwEMs">TrumpRx</a>, a prescription drug website run by the federal government; and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trump_Gold_Card" title="Trump Gold Card" id="mwEMw">Trump Gold Card</a>, a program offering foreign nationals expedited U.S. residency in exchange for donations of $1 million or more to the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_Commerce" title="United States Department of Commerce" id="mwEM0">Commerce Department</a> and denounced by U.S. Sen. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_Durbin" title="Dick Durbin" id="mwEM4">Dick Durbin</a> (D.-Ill.) as illegal.<sup about="#mwt2537" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-688" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-688"}}'><a href="#cite_note-688" id="mwEM8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENE">[</span>686<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwENI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="92" id="mwENM" aria-labelledby="Authoritarian_drift"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Authoritarian_drift">Authoritarian drift</h2></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2538" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwENQ" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Authoritarian drift during the second Trump administration sidebar","href":"./Template:Authoritarian_drift_during_the_second_Trump_administration_sidebar"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1374427404" about="#mwt2539" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Hlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1246091330" about="#mwt2540" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Sidebar/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><table class="sidebar sidebar-collapse nomobile nowraplinks hlist" role="navigation" about="#mwt2538" id="mwENU"><tbody><tr><td class="sidebar-pretitle">Part of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:Democratic_backsliding_in_the_United_States" title="Category:Democratic backsliding in the United States">a series</a> on</td></tr><tr><th class="sidebar-title-with-pretitle"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authoritarianism_during_the_Trump_presidencies" title="Authoritarianism during the Trump presidencies">Authoritarianism during<br/>the Trump presidencies</a></th></tr><tr><td class="sidebar-content" style="padding:0.2em 0.2em 0.2em 0.3em;">
<div class="sidebar-list mw-collapsible mw-collapsed"><div class="sidebar-list-title" style="background:#e7e1e1;padding:0;;color: var(--color-base)"><div class="sidebar-list-title-c">Concepts and strategy</div></div><div class="sidebar-list-content mw-collapsible-content">
