<ul><li><span class="nowrap"><span class="mw-image-border noviewer" typeof="mw:File"><span><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_United_States.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Flag_of_the_United_States.svg/40px-Flag_of_the_United_States.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a4/Flag_of_the_United_States.svg/120px-Flag_of_the_United_States.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="flag" data-file-width="1235" data-file-height="650" data-file-type="drawing" height="17" width="32" class="mw-file-element"/></span></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:United_States" title="Portal:United States">United States<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>portal</a></li>
<li><span class="nowrap"><span class="skin-invert-image noviewer" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Noun-smartphone-apps-432831.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Noun-smartphone-apps-432831.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Noun-smartphone-apps-432831.svg/20px-Noun-smartphone-apps-432831.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Noun-smartphone-apps-432831.svg/40px-Noun-smartphone-apps-432831.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="icon" data-file-width="512" data-file-height="960" data-file-type="drawing" height="28" width="15" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:2010s" title="Portal:2010s">2010s<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>portal</a></li>
<li><span class="nowrap"><span class="skin-invert-image noviewer" typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Noun-artificial-intelligence-6431591.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Noun-artificial-intelligence-6431591.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Noun-artificial-intelligence-6431591.svg/40px-Noun-artificial-intelligence-6431591.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Noun-artificial-intelligence-6431591.svg/60px-Noun-artificial-intelligence-6431591.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" alt="icon" data-file-width="1600" data-file-height="1600" data-file-type="drawing" height="28" width="28" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span> </span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portal:2020s" title="Portal:2020s">2020s<span typeof="mw:Entity"> </span>portal</a></li></ul></td></tr><tr><td class="sidebar-navbar"><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1374427404" about="#mwt2541" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Hlist/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1239400231" about="#mwt2542" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Navbar/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="navbar plainlinks hlist navbar-mini"><ul><li class="nv-view"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Authoritarianism_during_the_Trump_presidencies_sidebar" title="Template:Authoritarianism during the Trump presidencies sidebar"><abbr title="View this template">v</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-talk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Authoritarianism_during_the_Trump_presidencies_sidebar" title="Template talk:Authoritarianism during the Trump presidencies sidebar"><abbr title="Discuss this template">t</abbr></a></li><li class="nv-edit"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Template:Authoritarianism_during_the_Trump_presidencies_sidebar" title="Special:EditPage/Template:Authoritarianism during the Trump presidencies sidebar"><abbr title="Edit this template">e</abbr></a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwENY"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:1975-_Ideology_of_political_murders_-_US.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwENc"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:1975-_Ideology_of_political_murders_-_US.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/1975-_Ideology_of_political_murders_-_US.svg/250px-1975-_Ideology_of_political_murders_-_US.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/1975-_Ideology_of_political_murders_-_US.svg/500px-1975-_Ideology_of_political_murders_-_US.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="141" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwENg"/></a><figcaption id="mwENk">In September 2025, Trump announced a widespread crackdown on left-wing groups and donors, saying that "the radicals on the left are the problem" with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_violence_in_the_United_States" title="Political violence in the United States" id="mwENo">political violence</a>.<sup about="#mwt2545" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYTimes_20250912_689-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYTimes_20250912"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYTimes_20250912-689"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYTimes_20250912-689" id="mwENs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwENw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEN0">[</span>687<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEN4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2548" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-690" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-690"}}'><a href="#cite_note-690" id="mwEN8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEOA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEOE">[</span>688<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEOI">]</span></span></a></sup> However, cumulatively over decades, most extremist killings in the US have been caused by right-wing perpetrators.<sup about="#mwt2554" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Time_and_Cato_691-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Time_and_Cato"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Time_and_Cato-691"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Time_and_Cato-691" id="mwEOM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEOU">[</span>689<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEOY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2557" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-AP_20250914_692-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"AP_20250914"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AP_20250914-692"}}'><a href="#cite_note-AP_20250914-692" id="mwEOc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEOg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEOk">[</span>690<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEOo">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>

<section data-mw-section-id="93" id="mwEOs" aria-labelledby="Government_targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Government_targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society">Government targeting of political opponents and civil society</h3></div>
<div class="excerpt-block" about="#mwt2558" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEOw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:Excerpt","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"main"},"2":{"wt":"only=paragraphs"},"3":{"wt":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="mw-empty-elt"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1353838603" about="#mwt2559" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Excerpt/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2560" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration">Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration</a>.<span class="mw-editsection-like plainlinks"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a rel="mw:ExtLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration&amp;action=edit" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration&amp;action=edit">edit</a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div><div class="excerpt">
<p>During <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump" title="Donald Trump">Donald Trump</a>'s second presidency, the Trump administration took a series of actions using the government to target his political opponents and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_society" title="Civil society">civil society</a>. News outlets described his actions as part of his promised "retribution" and "revenge" campaign, within the context of a strongly personalist and leader-centered conception of politics.<sup about="#mwt2563" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-693" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-693"}}'><a href="#cite_note-693" id="mwEO0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEO4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEO8">[</span>691<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2568" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Collinson_1282025_694-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Collinson 1282025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Collinson_1282025-694"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Collinson_1282025-694" id="mwEPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPM">[</span>692<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2573" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Dreisbach_04282025_695-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Dreisbach 04282025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Dreisbach_04282025-695"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Dreisbach_04282025-695" id="mwEPU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEPY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPc">[</span>693<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2578" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Moynihan_696-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Moynihan"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Moynihan-696"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Moynihan-696" id="mwEPk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEPo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPs">[</span>694<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEPw">]</span></span></a></sup> During <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump_2024_presidential_campaign" title="Donald Trump 2024 presidential campaign">his 2024 presidential campaign</a>, Trump repeatedly stated that he had "every right" to go after his political opponents.<sup about="#mwt2583" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Byron_1222025_1_697-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Byron 1222025 1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Byron_1222025_1-697"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Byron_1222025_1-697" id="mwEP0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEP4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEP8">[</span>695<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>He undertook a massive expansion of presidential power under a maximalist interpretation of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unitary_executive_theory" title="Unitary executive theory">unitary executive theory</a>.<sup about="#mwt2588" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Economist_04242025_698-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Economist 04242025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Economist_04242025-698"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Economist_04242025-698" id="mwEQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQM">[</span>696<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Several of his actions ignored or violated federal laws, regulations, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constitution_of_the_United_States" title="Constitution of the United States">Constitution</a> according to American legal scholars,<sup about="#mwt2593" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-699" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-699"}}'><a href="#cite_note-699" id="mwEQU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEQY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQc">[</span>697<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2598" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-700" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-700"}}'><a href="#cite_note-700" id="mwEQk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEQo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQs">[</span>698<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2603" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-701" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-701"}}'><a href="#cite_note-701" id="mwEQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ8">[</span>699<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERA">]</span></span></a></sup> the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_Accountability_Office" title="Government Accountability Office" class="mw-redirect">Government Accountability Office</a>,<sup about="#mwt2608" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-702" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-702"}}'><a href="#cite_note-702" id="mwERE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwERI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERM">[</span>700<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERQ">]</span></span></a></sup> and federal judges.<sup about="#mwt2613" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-703" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-703"}}'><a href="#cite_note-703" id="mwERU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwERY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERc">[</span>701<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2618" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-704" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-704"}}'><a href="#cite_note-704" id="mwERk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwERo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERs">[</span>702<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwERw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2623" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-705" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-705"}}'><a href="#cite_note-705" id="mwER0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwER4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwER8">[</span>703<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESA">]</span></span></a></sup> He threatened, signed executive actions against, and ordered investigations into his political opponents, critics, and organizations aligned with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_Party_(United_States)" title="Democratic Party (United States)">Democratic Party</a>.<sup about="#mwt2628" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Vogel_&amp;_Goldmacher_2025_706-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Vogel &amp; Goldmacher 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Vogel_&amp;_Goldmacher_2025-706"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Vogel_&amp;_Goldmacher_2025-706" id="mwESE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwESI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESM">[</span>704<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESQ">]</span></span></a></sup> He politicized the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_federal_civil_service" title="United States federal civil service">civil service</a>,<sup about="#mwt2631" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Economist_04242025_698-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Economist 04242025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Economist_04242025-698" id="mwESU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwESY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESc">[</span>696<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESg">]</span></span></a></sup> undertaking <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States_federal_mass_layoffs" title="2025 United States federal mass layoffs">mass layoffs of government employees</a> to recruit workers more loyal to himself.<sup about="#mwt2635" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025_707-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Basu 01272025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025-707"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025-707" id="mwESk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwESo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESs">[</span>705<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwESw">]</span></span></a></sup> He ended the post-<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watergate_scandal" title="Watergate scandal">Watergate</a> norm of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_Justice" title="United States Department of Justice">Justice Department</a> independence, weaponizing it and ordering it to target his political enemies.<sup about="#mwt2638" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025_708-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Savage 04302025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025-708" id="mwES0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwES4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwES8">[</span>706<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETA">]</span></span></a></sup> He utilized several government agencies to retaliate against his political enemies and continued filing personal lawsuits against his political opponents, companies, and news organizations that angered him.<sup about="#mwt2640" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Dreisbach_04282025_695-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Dreisbach 04282025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Dreisbach_04282025-695" id="mwETE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwETI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETM">[</span>693<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2644" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025_709-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Cooper 09062025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025-709"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025-709" id="mwETU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwETY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETc">[</span>707<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>By July 2025, Trump had extracted more than $1.2 billion in settlements in a "cultural crackdown" against a variety of institutions that largely chose to settle rather than fight back.<sup about="#mwt2649" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025_710-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Basu 07302025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025-710"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025-710" id="mwETk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwETo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETs">[</span>708<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwETw">]</span></span></a></sup> He engaged in an unprecedented <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Targeting_of_law_firms_and_lawyers_under_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Targeting of law firms and lawyers under the second Trump administration">targeting of law firms and lawyers</a> that previously represented positions adverse to himself.<sup about="#mwt2654" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025_711-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Lucas 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025-711"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025-711" id="mwET0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwET4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwET8">[</span>709<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2659" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Scarcella,_Merken_&amp;_Sloan_2025_712-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Scarcella, Merken &amp; Sloan 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Scarcella,_Merken_&amp;_Sloan_2025-712"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Scarcella,_Merken_&amp;_Sloan_2025-712" id="mwEUE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEUI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUM">[</span>710<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Trump <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Education_policy_of_the_second_Donald_Trump_administration#Actions_against_universities" title="Education policy of the second Donald Trump administration" class="mw-redirect">targeted higher education</a> by demanding it give federal oversight of curriculum and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Visa_and_deportation_controversies_in_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Visa and deportation controversies in the second Trump administration">targeted activists</a>, legal immigrants, tourists, and students with visas who expressed criticism of his policies or engaged in pro-Palestinian advocacy.<sup about="#mwt2664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Kanno-Youngs-2025_713-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Kanno-Youngs-2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Kanno-Youngs-2025-713"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Kanno-Youngs-2025-713" id="mwEUU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEUY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUc">[</span>711<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUg">]</span></span></a></sup> He also <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deportation_and_detention_of_American_citizens_in_the_second_Trump_administration" title="Deportation and detention of American citizens in the second Trump administration" class="mw-redirect">detained and deported United States citizens</a>.<sup about="#mwt2669" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-714" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-714"}}'><a href="#cite_note-714" id="mwEUk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEUo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUs">[</span>712<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEUw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p>Trump's actions against <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_society" title="Civil society">civil society</a> have been described by legal experts and political scientists as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authoritarianism_during_the_Trump_presidencies" title="Authoritarianism during the Trump presidencies">authoritarian</a> and contributing to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Democratic_backsliding_in_the_United_States" title="Democratic backsliding in the United States">democratic backsliding</a>,<sup about="#mwt2674" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Riccardi_2025_715-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Riccardi 2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Riccardi_2025-715"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Riccardi_2025-715" id="mwEU0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEU4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEU8">[</span>713<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2679" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Leingang-2025_716-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Leingang-2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Leingang-2025-716"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Leingang-2025-716" id="mwEVE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEVI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVM">[</span>714<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2684" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Mascaro-2025_717-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Mascaro-2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Mascaro-2025-717"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Mascaro-2025-717" id="mwEVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVc">[</span>715<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVg">]</span></span></a></sup> as well as negatively impacting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_government_attacks_on_journalists_in_the_United_States#2025–present:_Donald_Trump's_second_presidency" title="Timeline of government attacks on journalists in the United States">freedom of the press</a>,<sup about="#mwt2689" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-718" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-718"}}'><a href="#cite_note-718" id="mwEVk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEVo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVs">[</span>716<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEVw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2694" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-719" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-719"}}'><a href="#cite_note-719" id="mwEV0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEV4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEV8">[</span>717<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2699" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-720" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-720"}}'><a href="#cite_note-720" id="mwEWE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEWI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWM">[</span>718<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_speech" title="Free speech" class="mw-redirect">free speech</a>, and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rule_of_law" title="Rule of law">rule of law</a>.<sup about="#mwt2704" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025_708-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Savage 04302025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025-708"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025-708" id="mwEWU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEWY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWc">[</span>706<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2709" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Abels_04292025_721-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Abels 04292025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Abels_04292025-721"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Abels_04292025-721" id="mwEWk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEWo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWs">[</span>719<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEWw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2714" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Hall_04242025_722-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Hall 04242025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Hall_04242025-722"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Hall_04242025-722" id="mwEW0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEW4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEW8">[</span>720<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2719" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Gilliand_04262025_723-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Targeting of political opponents and civil society under the second Trump administration Gilliand 04262025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Gilliand_04262025-723"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Gilliand_04262025-723" id="mwEXE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEXI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXM">[</span>721<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>
<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_excerpts"/>
</div></div>
<p id="mwEXU">In February 2026, during his State of the Union address to Congress, Trump was publicly criticized by Representatives <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ilhan_Omar" title="Ilhan Omar" id="mwEXY">Ilhan Omar</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rashida_Tlaib" title="Rashida Tlaib" id="mwEXc">Rashida Tlaib</a>, who challenged his immigration policies and accused his administration of harming U.S. citizens. In response, Trump posted on his social media platform Truth Social, suggesting that the lawmakers "should be sent back from where they came". Omar, a naturalized U.S. citizen born in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Somalia" title="Somalia" id="mwEXg">Somalia</a>, and Tlaib, a U.S.-born citizen of Palestinian descent, were both widely reported to have been the focus of these remarks. Media outlets and civil rights organizations described Trump's comments as xenophobic and controversial, drawing bipartisan criticism for targeting members of Congress based on their heritage.<sup about="#mwt2724" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-724" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-724"}}'><a href="#cite_note-724" id="mwEXk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEXo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXs">[</span>722<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEXw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2727" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-725" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-725"}}'><a href="#cite_note-725" id="mwEX0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEX4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEX8">[</span>723<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2730" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-726" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-726"}}'><a href="#cite_note-726" id="mwEYE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEYI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYM">[</span>724<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2733" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-727" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-727"}}'><a href="#cite_note-727" id="mwEYU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEYY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYc">[</span>725<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEYg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="94" id="mwEYk" aria-labelledby="Flood-the-zone_strategy"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Flood-the-zone_strategy">Flood-the-zone strategy</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2734" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEYo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Main","href":"./Template:Main"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"Flood the zone"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237" about="#mwt2735" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Hatnote/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div role="note" class="hatnote navigation-not-searchable" about="#mwt2734" id="mwEYs">Main article: <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flood_the_zone" title="Flood the zone">Flood the zone</a></div>

<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwEYw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_has_signed_the_most_first-day_executive_orders_of_recent_presidents._First-day_executive_orders_by_previous_ten_presidents,_1969–2025.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwEY0"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:President_Donald_Trump_has_signed_the_most_first-day_executive_orders_of_recent_presidents._First-day_executive_orders_by_previous_ten_presidents,_1969–2025.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/President_Donald_Trump_has_signed_the_most_first-day_executive_orders_of_recent_presidents._First-day_executive_orders_by_previous_ten_presidents%2C_1969%E2%80%932025.png/250px-thumbnail.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/President_Donald_Trump_has_signed_the_most_first-day_executive_orders_of_recent_presidents._First-day_executive_orders_by_previous_ten_presidents%2C_1969%E2%80%932025.png/500px-thumbnail.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1080" data-file-height="1456" data-file-type="bitmap" height="337" width="250" class="mw-file-element" id="mwEY4"/></a><figcaption id="mwEY8">Comparisons between numbers of first-day executive orders</figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwEZA">The beginning of Trump's second presidency is largely recognized as the one theorized by political strategist <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steve_Bannon" title="Steve Bannon" id="mwEZE">Steve Bannon</a> during Trump's first presidency, here deployed by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Miller" title="Stephen Miller" id="mwEZI">Stephen Miller</a>. The strategy consists of "flood[ing] the zone of shit", with an impressive number of claims and executive orders with the intent to tire journalists, political opponents and judicial institutions. As such the latter can't react rapidly and appropriately enough, and it nips controversies in the bud because of the flood of information. The administration had already prepared diverse executive orders to allow the signing of 55 executive orders in 20 days, a frequency never before seen.<sup about="#mwt2738" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-728" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-728"}}'><a href="#cite_note-728" id="mwEZM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEZU">[</span>726<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEZY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2741" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-729" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-729"}}'><a href="#cite_note-729" id="mwEZc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEZk">[</span>727<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEZo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2744" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-730" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-730"}}'><a href="#cite_note-730" id="mwEZs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEZw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEZ0">[</span>728<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEZ4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2747" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-731" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-731"}}'><a href="#cite_note-731" id="mwEZ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEaA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEaE">[</span>729<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEaI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2750" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-732" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-732"}}'><a href="#cite_note-732" id="mwEaM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEaQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEaU">[</span>730<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEaY">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2753" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-733" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-733"}}'><a href="#cite_note-733" id="mwEac"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEak">[</span>731<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEao">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="95" id="mwEas" aria-labelledby="Concentration_of_executive_power"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Concentration_of_executive_power">Concentration of executive power</h3></div>
<p id="mwEaw">A month after the beginning of the presidency, the government had been sued 200 times for "executive overreach", which the administration lost for the most part.<sup about="#mwt2756" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ARTE_734-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ARTE"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ARTE-734"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ARTE-734" id="mwEa0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEa4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEa8">[</span>732<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbA">]</span></span></a></sup> On <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twitter" title="Twitter" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEbE">Twitter</a>, Trump justified his policies by quoting <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Napoleon" title="Napoleon" id="mwEbI">Napoleon</a>: "He who saves his Country does not violate any Law".<sup about="#mwt2759" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GroundNews2025_735-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GroundNews2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-GroundNews2025-735"}}'><a href="#cite_note-GroundNews2025-735" id="mwEbM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEbQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbU">[</span>733<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbY">]</span></span></a></sup> In reaction, the American left accused him of acting as a dictator.<sup about="#mwt2762" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reinstein2025_736-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reinstein2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Reinstein2025-736"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reinstein2025-736" id="mwEbc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbk">[</span>734<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEbo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2765" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Chiacu2025_737-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Chiacu2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Chiacu2025-737"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Chiacu2025-737" id="mwEbs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEbw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEb0">[</span>735<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEb4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2768" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-738" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-738"}}'><a href="#cite_note-738" id="mwEb8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcE">[</span>736<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEcM">The right-wing and left-wing media both claim that their policies allowed a hitherto concentration of executive power in US history. Experts and newspapers feared a constitutional crisis because of frequent <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Separation_of_powers" title="Separation of powers" id="mwEcQ">checks and balances</a> breaches.<sup about="#mwt2769" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GroundNews2025_735-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GroundNews2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-GroundNews2025-735" id="mwEcU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEcY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcc">[</span>733<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcg">]</span></span></a></sup> The Trump administration often questioned the legitimacy of judges blocking his executive orders.<sup about="#mwt2770" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Reinstein2025_736-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Reinstein2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Reinstein2025-736" id="mwEck"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEco"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcs">[</span>734<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEcw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2771" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Chiacu2025_737-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Chiacu2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Chiacu2025-737" id="mwEc0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEc4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEc8">[</span>735<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2774" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-739" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-739"}}'><a href="#cite_note-739" id="mwEdE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEdI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdM">[</span>737<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEdU">According to <i id="mwEdY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_Yorker" title="The New Yorker" id="mwEdc">The New Yorker</a></i>, Trump's new governance based itself on unconditional loyalty towards himself. Trump allegedly implemented a climate where any criticism even among the Republicans is sanctioned. Figures like <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jack_Posobiec" title="Jack Posobiec" id="mwEdg">Jack Posobiec</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laura_Loomer" title="Laura Loomer" id="mwEdk">Laura Loomer</a> acted as ideological safeguards by listing potential dissidents among the party.<sup about="#mwt2777" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-740" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-740"}}'><a href="#cite_note-740" id="mwEdo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEds"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEdw">[</span>738<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEd0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEd4">The administrations openly wanted to concentrate political powers within Trump's hands. They justify it with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unitary_executive_theory" title="Unitary executive theory" id="mwEd8">unitary executive theory</a>, alleging that by having been elected and with the approval of the Constitution, Trump is warranted in having unchecked and absolute power on the judicial branch, and on politics in general.<sup about="#mwt2778" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ARTE_734-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ARTE"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ARTE-734" id="mwEeA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEeE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEeI">[</span>732<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEeM">]</span></span></a></sup> Legal expert Julien Jeanneney argued that the "unconstitutional" policies of Trump are backed by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Court_of_the_United_States" title="Supreme Court of the United States" id="mwEeQ">Supreme Court</a>, of which a third of the judges had been appointed by Trump during his first presidency, hence making Republican judges the majority. According to Jeanneney most of the judges "seem clearly on Trump's side concerning most of his policies, even when they violate the Court's long-lived principles".<sup about="#mwt2781" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-741" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-741"}}'><a href="#cite_note-741" id="mwEeU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEeY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEec">[</span>739<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEeg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwEek">Numerous experts of fascism and historians (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jason_Stanley" title="Jason Stanley" id="mwEeo">Jason Stanley</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marci_Shore" title="Marci Shore" id="mwEes">Marci Shore</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timothy_Snyder" title="Timothy Snyder" id="mwEew">Timothy Snyder</a>,<sup about="#mwt2784" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-742" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-742"}}'><a href="#cite_note-742" id="mwEe0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEe4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEe8">[</span>740<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Chapoutot" title="Johann Chapoutot" id="mwEfE">Johann Chapoutot</a>,<sup about="#mwt2787" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-743" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-743"}}'><a href="#cite_note-743" id="mwEfI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEfM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfQ">[</span>741<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfU">]</span></span></a></sup> Paul Lerner, Anne Berg,<sup about="#mwt2790" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Trouillard2025_744-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Trouillard2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Trouillard2025-744"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Trouillard2025-744" id="mwEfY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEfc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfg">[</span>742<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfk">]</span></span></a></sup> Diana Garvin, Tiffany Florvil, Claudia Koonz,<sup about="#mwt2793" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-745" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-745"}}'><a href="#cite_note-745" id="mwEfo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEfs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEfw">[</span>743<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEf0">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asma_Mhalla" title="Asma Mhalla" id="mwEf4">Asma Mhalla</a>,<sup about="#mwt2796" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-746" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-746"}}'><a href="#cite_note-746" id="mwEf8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgE">[</span>744<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgI">]</span></span></a></sup> and Ben Worthy<sup about="#mwt2799" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-747" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-747"}}'><a href="#cite_note-747" id="mwEgM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEgQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgU">[</span>745<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgY">]</span></span></a></sup>) denounced the authoritarianism of the presidency, which they explicitly <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump_and_fascism" title="Donald Trump and fascism" id="mwEgc">linked to fascism</a>. However experts <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christopher_R._Browning" title="Christopher R. Browning" id="mwEgg">Christopher R. Browning</a>,<sup about="#mwt2800" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Trouillard2025_744-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Trouillard2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Trouillard2025-744" id="mwEgk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEgo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgs">[</span>742<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEgw">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Griffin" title="Roger Griffin" id="mwEg0">Roger Griffin</a>,<sup about="#mwt2803" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-748" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-748"}}'><a href="#cite_note-748" id="mwEg4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEg8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhA">[</span>746<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhE">]</span></span></a></sup> Janos Bourgeois,<sup about="#mwt2806" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-749" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-749"}}'><a href="#cite_note-749" id="mwEhI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEhM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhQ">[</span>747<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhU">]</span></span></a></sup> Lloyd Cox and Brendon O'Connor<sup about="#mwt2809" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Cox2025_750-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Cox2025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Cox2025-750"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Cox2025-750" id="mwEhY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEhc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhg">[</span>748<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhk">]</span></span></a></sup> contested this comparison, although Browning noted "uncanny resemblances" between Trump and Hitler,<sup about="#mwt2810" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Trouillard2025_744-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Trouillard2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Trouillard2025-744" id="mwEho"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEhs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEhw">[</span>742<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEh0">]</span></span></a></sup> and Cox and O'Connor talked about "proto-fascist phenomenon".<sup about="#mwt2811" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Cox2025_750-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Cox2025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Cox2025-750" id="mwEh4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEh8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEiA">[</span>748<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEiE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="96" id="mwEiI" aria-labelledby="Academic_evaluations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Academic_evaluations">Academic evaluations</h3></div>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2812" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEiM" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"multiple image ","href":"./Template:Multiple_image"},"params":{"total_width":{"wt":"450"},"image1":{"wt":"V-Dem Electoral and Liberal Democracy Indices for the United States since 1900.svg"},"caption1":{"wt":"The [[V-Dem Institute]] said in 2026 regarding Trump&apos;s presidency that \"the speed with which American democracy is currently dismantled is unprecedented in modern history\".&lt;ref name=VDEM_Report_2026/> The institute noted executive overreach undermining the [[rule of law]], suppression and intimidation of media and dissenting voices, loss of legislative constraints, and declining [[civil rights]], equality, and [[freedom of expression]].&lt;ref name=VDEM_Report_2026>{{#invoke:cite | web |title=Democracy Report 2026 / Unraveling The Democratic Era? |url=https://www.v-dem.net/documents/75/V-Dem_Institute_Democracy_Report_2026_lowres.pdf |publisher=[[V-Dem Institute]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260320121434/https://www.v-dem.net/documents/75/V-Dem_Institute_Democracy_Report_2026_lowres.pdf |archive-date=March 20, 2026 |page=33 In Focus: Autocratization in the USA |date=March 2026 |url-status=live}}&lt;br>●{{nbsp}}Raw data presented at: {{#invoke:cite | web |title=Country Graph |url=https://www.v-dem.net/data_analysis/CountryGraph/ |publisher=V-Dem Institute |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260301172546/https://www.v-dem.net/data_analysis/CountryGraph/ |archive-date=March 1, 2026 |date=March 2026 |url-status=live}} (Choose \"United States of America\" and select \"Election Democracy Index\" and \"Liberal Democracy Index\".)&lt;/ref>"},"image2":{"wt":"20260513 Autocracy index - markers of democratic erosion.svg"},"caption2":{"wt":"Beginning in October 2025, &apos;&apos;The New York Times&apos;&apos; editorial board published an Autocracy Index showing erosion of US democracy using various benchmarks, offering \"a way to understand how much Mr. Trump is eroding American democracy\" since his January 2025 inauguration.&lt;ref name=NYTimes_20260513>{{cite news |author1=The Editorial Board |title=Trump&apos;s Election Meddling Erodes Our Democracy |url=https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/08/20/opinion/trump-election-interference-democracy.html |date=August 20, 2026 |work=The New York Times}} The editorial board wrote that \"clearest sign that a democracy has died is that a leader and his party make it impossible for their opponents to win an election and hold power\".&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1349637415/mw-parser-output/.tmulti" about="#mwt2813" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Multiple image/styles.css","wrapper":".tmulti"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/></span><div class="thumb tmulti floatright" about="#mwt2812"><div class="thumbinner multiimageinner" style="width:442px;max-width:442px"><div class="trow"><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:122px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:V-Dem_Electoral_and_Liberal_Democracy_Indices_for_the_United_States_since_1900.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:V-Dem_Electoral_and_Liberal_Democracy_Indices_for_the_United_States_since_1900.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/V-Dem_Electoral_and_Liberal_Democracy_Indices_for_the_United_States_since_1900.svg/250px-V-Dem_Electoral_and_Liberal_Democracy_Indices_for_the_United_States_since_1900.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/V-Dem_Electoral_and_Liberal_Democracy_Indices_for_the_United_States_since_1900.svg/500px-V-Dem_Electoral_and_Liberal_Democracy_Indices_for_the_United_States_since_1900.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="122" width="217" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V-Dem_Institute" title="V-Dem Institute">V-Dem Institute</a> said in 2026 regarding Trump's presidency that "the speed with which American democracy is currently dismantled is unprecedented in modern history".<sup about="#mwt2814" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-VDEM_Report_2026_751-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"VDEM_Report_2026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-VDEM_Report_2026-751" id="mwEiQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEiU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEiY">[</span>749<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEic">]</span></span></a></sup> The institute noted executive overreach undermining the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rule_of_law" title="Rule of law">rule of law</a>, suppression and intimidation of media and dissenting voices, loss of legislative constraints, and declining <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_rights" title="Civil rights" class="mw-redirect">civil rights</a>, equality, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Freedom_of_expression" title="Freedom of expression" class="mw-redirect">freedom of expression</a>.<sup about="#mwt2821" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-VDEM_Report_2026_751-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"VDEM_Report_2026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-VDEM_Report_2026-751"}}'><a href="#cite_note-VDEM_Report_2026-751" id="mwEig"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEik"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEio">[</span>749<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEis">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div><div class="tsingle" style="width:219px;max-width:219px"><div class="thumbimage" style="height:122px;overflow:hidden"><span typeof="mw:File"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20260513_Autocracy_index_-_markers_of_democratic_erosion.svg" class="mw-file-description"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20260513_Autocracy_index_-_markers_of_democratic_erosion.svg" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/20260513_Autocracy_index_-_markers_of_democratic_erosion.svg/250px-20260513_Autocracy_index_-_markers_of_democratic_erosion.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/20260513_Autocracy_index_-_markers_of_democratic_erosion.svg/500px-20260513_Autocracy_index_-_markers_of_democratic_erosion.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1200" data-file-height="675" data-file-type="drawing" height="122" width="217" class="mw-file-element"/></a></span></div><div class="thumbcaption">Beginning in October 2025, <i>The New York Times</i> editorial board published an Autocracy Index showing erosion of US democracy using various benchmarks, offering "a way to understand how much Mr. Trump is eroding American democracy" since his January 2025 inauguration.<sup about="#mwt2827" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NYTimes_20260513_752-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NYTimes_20260513"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYTimes_20260513-752"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NYTimes_20260513-752" id="mwEiw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEi0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEi4">[</span>750<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEi8">]</span></span></a></sup></div></div></div></div></div><span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2812"><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Pages_using_multiple_image_with_auto_scaled_images"/></span>
<p id="mwEjA">Professor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christina_Pagel" title="Christina Pagel" id="mwEjE">Christina Pagel</a> mapped the first actions of the Trump administration in a Venn diagram that identifies "five broad domains that correspond to features of proto-authoritarian states". These five domains are: undermining democratic institutions and the rule of law, dismantling federal government; dismantling social protections and rights, enrichment and corruption; suppressing dissent and controlling information; attacking science, environment, health, arts and education, particularly universities; aggressive foreign policy and global destabilization.<sup about="#mwt2832" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-kottke-pagel_753-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"kottke-pagel"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-kottke-pagel-753"}}'><a href="#cite_note-kottke-pagel-753" id="mwEjI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEjM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEjQ">[</span>751<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEjU">]</span></span></a></sup>
The journalist Martin Sandu and the authoritarian politics researcher Alex Norris described the maximalist interpretation of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Federal_government_and_executive_power" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwEjY">executive power</a> in Trump's second term as president, including sweeping <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_executive_orders_in_the_second_Trump_presidency" title="List of executive orders in the second Trump presidency" id="mwEjc">executive orders</a>, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_United_States_federal_government_grant_pause" title="2025 United States federal government grant pause" id="mwEjg">federal funding freeze</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="#Actions_against_political_opponents_and_the_media" class="mw-selflink-fragment" id="mwEjk">actions against political opponents and the media</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pardon_of_January_6_United_States_Capitol_attack_defendants" title="Pardon of January 6 United States Capitol attack defendants" id="mwEjo">pardons of those involved in the January 6th Capitol attack</a>, the actions of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elon_Musk" title="Elon Musk" id="mwEjs">Elon Musk</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Department_of_Government_Efficiency" title="Department of Government Efficiency" id="mwEjw">Department of Government Efficiency</a>, and the like as an attempted <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-coup" title="Self-coup" id="mwEj0">self-coup</a>.<sup about="#mwt2835" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-754" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-754"}}'><a href="#cite_note-754" id="mwEj4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEj8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkA">[</span>752<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2838" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-755" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-755"}}'><a href="#cite_note-755" id="mwEkI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEkM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkQ">[</span>753<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkU">]</span></span></a></sup> The political scientist Lee Morgenbesser argued the actions of DOGE are a form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_capture" title="State capture" id="mwEkY">state capture</a>.<sup about="#mwt2841" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-756" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-756"}}'><a href="#cite_note-756" id="mwEkc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEkg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEkk">[</span>754<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEko">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="97" id="mwEks" aria-labelledby="Elections_during_the_second_Trump_presidency"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Elections_during_the_second_Trump_presidency">Elections during the second Trump presidency</h2></div>
