<li about="#cite_note-Collinson_1282025-266" id="cite_note-Collinson_1282025-266" data-mw-footnote-number="265"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHq4"><a href="#cite_ref-Collinson_1282025_266-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHq8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHrA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Collinson_1282025-266" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt933" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwHrE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Collinson "},"3":{"wt":"first=Stephen "},"4":{"wt":"date=January 28, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump sets about his retribution agenda with relish "},"6":{"wt":"url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/28/politics/trump-retribution-agenda-analysis/index.html "},"7":{"wt":"access-date=January 28, 2025 "},"8":{"wt":"work=[[CNN]] "},"9":{"wt":"quote=The president is wasting no time in following through on his frequent campaign trail vows for retribution – with a torrent of purges and pardons. "},"10":{"wt":"archive-date=January 28, 2025 "},"11":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128111941/https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/28/politics/trump-retribution-agenda-analysis/index.html "},"12":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCollinson2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt933">Collinson, Stephen (January 28, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/28/politics/trump-retribution-agenda-analysis/index.html" class="external text" id="mwHrI">"Trump sets about his retribution agenda with relish"</a>. <i id="mwHrM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN" title="CNN" id="mwHrQ">CNN</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250128111941/https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/28/politics/trump-retribution-agenda-analysis/index.html" class="external text" id="mwHrU">Archived</a> from the original on January 28, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwHrY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwHrc">January 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwHrg">The president is wasting no time in following through on his frequent campaign trail vows for retribution – with a torrent of purges and pardons.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNN&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+sets+about+his+retribution+agenda+with+relish&amp;rft.date=2025-01-28&amp;rft.aulast=Collinson&amp;rft.aufirst=Stephen&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnn.com%2F2025%2F01%2F28%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-retribution-agenda-analysis%2Findex.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt933" id="mwHrk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Savage_1282025-267" id="cite_note-Savage_1282025-267" data-mw-footnote-number="266"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHro"><a href="#cite_ref-Savage_1282025_267-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHrs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHrw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Savage_1282025-267" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt936" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwHr0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Savage "},"3":{"wt":"first=Charlie "},"4":{"wt":"date=January 27, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Fired Inspectors General Raise Alarms as Trump Administration Moves to Finalize Purge "},"6":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/27/us/politics/trump-inspectors-general-fired.html "},"7":{"wt":"url-access=subscription "},"8":{"wt":"access-date=January 28, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"work=The New York Times "},"10":{"wt":"quote=Some advisers to Mr. Trump have been interested in advancing the so-called unitary executive theory, an expansive view of presidential power. According to the theory, the president must have complete control of the executive branch, so Congress may not give other officials independent decision-making authority or restrict the president&apos;s ability to fire them. "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=January 28, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128005655/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/27/us/politics/trump-inspectors-general-fired.html "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwHr4" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt936" data-x-id="CITEREFSavage2025">Savage, Charlie (January 27, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwHr8"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/27/us/politics/trump-inspectors-general-fired.html" class="external text" id="mwHsA">"Fired Inspectors General Raise Alarms as Trump Administration Moves to Finalize Purge"</a></span>. <i id="mwHsE">The New York Times</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250128005655/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/27/us/politics/trump-inspectors-general-fired.html" class="external text" id="mwHsI">Archived</a> from the original on January 28, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwHsM">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwHsQ">January 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwHsU">Some advisers to Mr. Trump have been interested in advancing the so-called unitary executive theory, an expansive view of presidential power. According to the theory, the president must have complete control of the executive branch, so Congress may not give other officials independent decision-making authority or restrict the president's ability to fire them.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Fired+Inspectors+General+Raise+Alarms+as+Trump+Administration+Moves+to+Finalize+Purge&amp;rft.date=2025-01-27&amp;rft.aulast=Savage&amp;rft.aufirst=Charlie&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F01%2F27%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-inspectors-general-fired.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt936" id="mwHsY"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-268" id="cite_note-268" data-mw-footnote-number="267"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHsc"><a href="#cite_ref-268" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHsg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHsk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-268" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt939" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwHso" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last1=Basu "},"3":{"wt":"first1=Zachary "},"4":{"wt":"last2=Lawler "},"5":{"wt":"first2=Dave "},"6":{"wt":"date=January 27, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"title=Trump&apos;s bureaucracy goes to war "},"8":{"wt":"url=https://www.axios.com/2025/01/27/trump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general "},"9":{"wt":"access-date=January 28, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"work=[[Axios (website)|Axios]] "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=January 28, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128213153/https://www.axios.com/2025/01/27/trump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBasuLawler2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt939">Basu, Zachary; Lawler, Dave (January 27, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.axios.com/2025/01/27/trump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general" class="external text" id="mwHss">"Trump's bureaucracy goes to war"</a>. <i id="mwHsw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axios_(website)" title="Axios (website)" id="mwHs0">Axios</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250128213153/https://www.axios.com/2025/01/27/trump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general" class="external text" id="mwHs4">Archived</a> from the original on January 28, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwHs8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwHtA">January 28,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+bureaucracy+goes+to+war&amp;rft.date=2025-01-27&amp;rft.aulast=Basu&amp;rft.aufirst=Zachary&amp;rft.au=Lawler%2C+Dave&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2025%2F01%2F27%2Ftrump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt939" id="mwHtE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-269" id="cite_note-269" data-mw-footnote-number="268"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHtI"><a href="#cite_ref-269" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHtM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHtQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-269" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt942" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwHtU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last1=Bose "},"3":{"wt":"first1=Nandita "},"4":{"wt":"last2=Shah "},"5":{"wt":"first2=Chandni "},"6":{"wt":"date=January 25, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"title=Trump fires 17 independent inspectors general at federal agencies, source says "},"8":{"wt":"url=https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-fires-least-12-independent-inspectors-general-washington-post-reports-2025-01-25/ "},"9":{"wt":"access-date=January 25, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"work=[[Reuters]] "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=March 13, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250313142535/https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-fires-least-12-independent-inspectors-general-washington-post-reports-2025-01-25/ "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBoseShah2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt942">Bose, Nandita; Shah, Chandni (January 25, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-fires-least-12-independent-inspectors-general-washington-post-reports-2025-01-25/" class="external text" id="mwHtY">"Trump fires 17 independent inspectors general at federal agencies, source says"</a>. <i id="mwHtc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters" title="Reuters" id="mwHtg">Reuters</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250313142535/https://www.reuters.com/world/us/trump-fires-least-12-independent-inspectors-general-washington-post-reports-2025-01-25/" class="external text" id="mwHtk">Archived</a> from the original on March 13, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwHto">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwHts">January 25,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Reuters&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+fires+17+independent+inspectors+general+at+federal+agencies%2C+source+says&amp;rft.date=2025-01-25&amp;rft.aulast=Bose&amp;rft.aufirst=Nandita&amp;rft.au=Shah%2C+Chandni&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.reuters.com%2Fworld%2Fus%2Ftrump-fires-least-12-independent-inspectors-general-washington-post-reports-2025-01-25%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt942" id="mwHtw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Savage_1252025-270" id="cite_note-Savage_1252025-270" data-mw-footnote-number="269"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHt0"><a href="#cite_ref-Savage_1252025_270-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHt4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHt8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Savage_1252025-270" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt945" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwHuA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Savage "},"3":{"wt":"first=Charlie "},"4":{"wt":"date=January 22, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump Seeks to Paralyze Independent Privacy and Civil Liberties Watchdog "},"6":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/22/us/trump-privacy-civil-liberties-oversight-board.html "},"7":{"wt":"url-access=subscription "},"8":{"wt":"access-date=January 25, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"work=[[The New York Times]] "},"10":{"wt":"quote=Advisers to Mr. Trump subscribe to a strong view of presidential power called the unitary executive theory, under which the Constitution should be interpreted as giving presidents exclusive control of the executive branch and independent agencies are considered illegitimate. During the campaign, Trump allies vowed to stomp out pockets of independence in the executive branch if he won the election. "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=January 25, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250125134617/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/22/us/trump-privacy-civil-liberties-oversight-board.html "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwHuE" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt945" data-x-id="CITEREFSavage2025">Savage, Charlie (January 22, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwHuI"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/22/us/trump-privacy-civil-liberties-oversight-board.html" class="external text" id="mwHuM">"Trump Seeks to Paralyze Independent Privacy and Civil Liberties Watchdog"</a></span>. <i id="mwHuQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwHuU">The New York Times</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250125134617/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/22/us/trump-privacy-civil-liberties-oversight-board.html" class="external text" id="mwHuY">Archived</a> from the original on January 25, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwHuc">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwHug">January 25,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwHuk">Advisers to Mr. Trump subscribe to a strong view of presidential power called the unitary executive theory, under which the Constitution should be interpreted as giving presidents exclusive control of the executive branch and independent agencies are considered illegitimate. During the campaign, Trump allies vowed to stomp out pockets of independence in the executive branch if he won the election.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+Seeks+to+Paralyze+Independent+Privacy+and+Civil+Liberties+Watchdog&amp;rft.date=2025-01-22&amp;rft.aulast=Savage&amp;rft.aufirst=Charlie&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F01%2F22%2Fus%2Ftrump-privacy-civil-liberties-oversight-board.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt945" id="mwHuo"></span></span></li>
