ew Research Center. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260624052238/https://www.pewresearch.org/global/2026/06/23/european-views-of-trump-and-the-u-s-are-especially-negative/" class="external text" id="mwH_A">Archived</a> from the original on June 24, 2026.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=PewResearch.org&amp;rft.atitle=European+views+of+Trump+and+the+U.S.+are+especially+negative&amp;rft.date=2026-06-23&amp;rft.aulast=Wike&amp;rft.aufirst=Richart&amp;rft.au=Silver%2C+Laura&amp;rft.au=Fagan%2C+Moira&amp;rft.au=Schulman%2C+Jonathan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pewresearch.org%2Fglobal%2F2026%2F06%2F23%2Feuropean-views-of-trump-and-the-u-s-are-especially-negative%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1044" id="mwH_E"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-296" id="cite_note-296" data-mw-footnote-number="295"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwH_I"><a href="#cite_ref-296" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwH_M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwH_Q">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-296" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1047" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwH_U" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last1=Colvin "},"3":{"wt":"first1=Jill "},"4":{"wt":"last2=Gillies "},"5":{"wt":"first2=Rob "},"6":{"wt":"date=January 9, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"title=Trump, the &apos;America First&apos; candidate, has a new preoccupation: Imperialism "},"8":{"wt":"work=The Associated Press "},"9":{"wt":"url=https://apnews.com/article/trump-imperialism-canada-panama-greenland-b4b53445dee97398b498b79eab54d49b "},"10":{"wt":"access-date=January 28, 2025 "},"11":{"wt":"quote=But since winning a second term, the president-elect has been embracing a new imperialist agenda, threatening to seize the Panama Canal and Greenland — perhaps by military force — and saying he will use economic coercion to pressure Canada to become the nation&apos;s 51st state. "},"12":{"wt":"archive-date=February 5, 2025 "},"13":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250205180523/https://apnews.com/article/trump-imperialism-canada-panama-greenland-b4b53445dee97398b498b79eab54d49b "},"14":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFColvinGillies2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1047">Colvin, Jill; Gillies, Rob (January 9, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://apnews.com/article/trump-imperialism-canada-panama-greenland-b4b53445dee97398b498b79eab54d49b" class="external text" id="mwH_Y">"Trump, the 'America First' candidate, has a new preoccupation: Imperialism"</a>. <i id="mwH_c">The Associated Press</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250205180523/https://apnews.com/article/trump-imperialism-canada-panama-greenland-b4b53445dee97398b498b79eab54d49b" class="external text" id="mwH_g">Archived</a> from the original on February 5, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwH_k">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwH_o">January 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwH_s">But since winning a second term, the president-elect has been embracing a new imperialist agenda, threatening to seize the Panama Canal and Greenland — perhaps by military force — and saying he will use economic coercion to pressure Canada to become the nation's 51st state.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Associated+Press&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%2C+the+%27America+First%27+candidate%2C+has+a+new+preoccupation%3A+Imperialism&amp;rft.date=2025-01-09&amp;rft.aulast=Colvin&amp;rft.aufirst=Jill&amp;rft.au=Gillies%2C+Rob&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Ftrump-imperialism-canada-panama-greenland-b4b53445dee97398b498b79eab54d49b&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1047" id="mwH_w"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-297" id="cite_note-297" data-mw-footnote-number="296"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwH_0"><a href="#cite_ref-297" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwH_4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwH_8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-297" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1050" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIAA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Collinson "},"3":{"wt":"first=Stephen "},"4":{"wt":"date=January 8, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump&apos;s threats to Greenland, Canada and Panama explain everything about America First "},"6":{"wt":"work=CNN "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://edition.cnn.com/2025/01/08/politics/trump-greenland-canada-panama-analysis/index.html "},"8":{"wt":"access-date=January 28, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"quote=Donald Trump&apos;s imperialist designs on Greenland, Canada and Panama often sound like the ramblings of a real estate shark who equates foreign and trade policy to a hunt for new deals. But there&apos;s method in his expansionist mindset. "},"10":{"wt":"archive-date=January 28, 2025 "},"11":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250128192631/https://edition.cnn.com/2025/01/08/politics/trump-greenland-canada-panama-analysis/index.html "},"12":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwIAE" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1050" data-x-id="CITEREFCollinson2025">Collinson, Stephen (January 8, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://edition.cnn.com/2025/01/08/politics/trump-greenland-canada-panama-analysis/index.html" class="external text" id="mwIAI">"Trump's threats to Greenland, Canada and Panama explain everything about America First"</a>. <i id="mwIAM">CNN</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250128192631/https://edition.cnn.com/2025/01/08/politics/trump-greenland-canada-panama-analysis/index.html" class="external text" id="mwIAQ">Archived</a> from the original on January 28, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIAU">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIAY">January 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIAc">Donald Trump's imperialist designs on Greenland, Canada and Panama often sound like the ramblings of a real estate shark who equates foreign and trade policy to a hunt for new deals. But there's method in his expansionist mindset.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNN&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+threats+to+Greenland%2C+Canada+and+Panama+explain+everything+about+America+First&amp;rft.date=2025-01-08&amp;rft.aulast=Collinson&amp;rft.aufirst=Stephen&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fedition.cnn.com%2F2025%2F01%2F08%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-greenland-canada-panama-analysis%2Findex.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1050" id="mwIAg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-298" id="cite_note-298" data-mw-footnote-number="297"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIAk"><a href="#cite_ref-298" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIAo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIAs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-298" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1053" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIAw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Smolar "},"3":{"wt":"first=Piotr "},"4":{"wt":"date=January 8, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Donald Trump&apos;s rhetoric of a new American imperialism "},"6":{"wt":"work=[[Le Monde]] "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2025/01/08/donald-trump-s-rhetoric-of-a-new-american-imperialism_6736821_4.html "},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription "},"9":{"wt":"access-date=January 28, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"quote=At a press conference in West Palm Beach, Florida, on Tuesday, January 7, Trump reiterated the idea of American expansion, which he believes would validate the promise of a &apos;golden age&apos; made to voters. "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=February 4, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250204133618/https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2025/01/08/donald-trump-s-rhetoric-of-a-new-american-imperialism_6736821_4.html "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSmolar2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1053">Smolar, Piotr (January 8, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIA0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2025/01/08/donald-trump-s-rhetoric-of-a-new-american-imperialism_6736821_4.html" class="external text" id="mwIA4">"Donald Trump's rhetoric of a new American imperialism"</a></span>. <i id="mwIA8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Monde" title="Le Monde" id="mwIBA">Le Monde</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250204133618/https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2025/01/08/donald-trump-s-rhetoric-of-a-new-american-imperialism_6736821_4.html" class="external text" id="mwIBE">Archived</a> from the original on February 4, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIBI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIBM">January 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIBQ">At a press conference in West Palm Beach, Florida, on Tuesday, January 7, Trump reiterated the idea of American expansion, which he believes would validate the promise of a 'golden age' made to voters.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Le+Monde&amp;rft.atitle=Donald+Trump%27s+rhetoric+of+a+new+American+imperialism&amp;rft.date=2025-01-08&amp;rft.aulast=Smolar&amp;rft.aufirst=Piotr&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lemonde.fr%2Fen%2Finternational%2Farticle%2F2025%2F01%2F08%2Fdonald-trump-s-rhetoric-of-a-new-american-imperialism_6736821_4.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1053" id="mwIBU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-299" id="cite_note-299" data-mw-footnote-number="298"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIBY"><a href="#cite_ref-299" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIBc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIBg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-299" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1056" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIBk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Mittelstadt "},"3":{"wt":"first=Jennifer "},"4":{"wt":"date=February 2, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Opinion {{!}} Why Does Trump Threaten America&apos;s Allies? Hint: It Starts in 1919. "},"6":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/02/opinion/trump-panama-greenland-foreign-policy.html "},"7":{"wt":"access-date=February 5, 2025 "},"8":{"wt":"work=The New York Times "},"9":{"wt":"archive-date=February 4, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250204021504/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/02/opinion/trump-panama-greenland-foreign-policy.html "},"11":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFMittelstadt2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1056">Mittelstadt, Jennifer (February 2, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/02/opinion/trump-panama-greenland-foreign-policy.html" class="external text" id="mwIBo">"Opinion | Why Does Trump Threaten America's Allies? Hint: It Starts in 1919"</a>. <i id="mwIBs">The New York Times</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250204021504/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/02/opinion/trump-panama-greenland-foreign-policy.html" class="external text" id="mwIBw">Archived</a> from the original on February 4, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIB0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIB4">February 5,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Opinion+%7C+Why+Does+Trump+Threaten+America%27s+Allies%3F+Hint%3A+It+Starts+in+1919.&amp;rft.date=2025-02-02&amp;rft.aulast=Mittelstadt&amp;rft.aufirst=Jennifer&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F02%2F02%2Fopinion%2Ftrump-panama-greenland-foreign-policy.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1056" id="mwIB8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Basu_2282025-300" id="cite_note-Basu_2282025-300" data-mw-footnote-number="299"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwICA"><a href="#cite_ref-Basu_2282025_300-0" id="mwICE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwICI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Basu_2282025_300-1" id="mwICM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwICQ">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Basu_2282025-300" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1059" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwICU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Basu "},"3":{"wt":"first=Zachary "},"4":{"wt":"date=February 28, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump&apos;s new world order: Strongmen make the rules "},"6":{"wt":"work=Axios "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.axios.com/2025/02/28/trump-new-world-order-russia-china-europe "},"8":{"wt":"access-date=February 28, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"quote=The international order forged after World War II is imploding, squeezed on all sides by the return of strongmen, nationalism and spheres of influence — with President Trump leading the charge.{{nbsp}}... Trump&apos;s approach is based, according to U.S. officials, in &apos;realism&apos;. "},"10":{"wt":"archive-date=March 1, 2025 "},"11":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250301053840/https://www.axios.com/2025/02/28/trump-new-world-order-russia-china-europe "},"12":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwICY" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1059" data-x-id="CITEREFBasu2025">Basu, Zachary (February 28, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.axios.com/2025/02/28/trump-new-world-order-russia-china-europe" class="external text" id="mwICc">"Trump's new world order: Strongmen make the rules"</a>. <i id="mwICg">Axios</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250301053840/https://www.axios.com/2025/02/28/trump-new-world-order-russia-china-europe" class="external text" id="mwICk">Archived</a> from the original on March 1, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwICo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwICs">February 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwICw">The international order forged after World War II is imploding, squeezed on all sides by the return of strongmen, nationalism and spheres of influence — with President Trump leading the charge.<span class="nowrap" id="mwIC0"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwIC4"> </span></span>... Trump's approach is based, according to U.S. officials, in 'realism'.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+new+world+order%3A+Strongmen+make+the+rules&amp;rft.date=2025-02-28&amp;rft.aulast=Basu&amp;rft.aufirst=Zachary&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2025%2F02%2F28%2Ftrump-new-world-order-russia-china-europe&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1059" id="mwIC8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Blaxland_2182025-301" id="cite_note-Blaxland_2182025-301" data-mw-footnote-number="300"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIDA"><a href="#cite_ref-Blaxland_2182025_301-0" id="mwIDE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIDI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Blaxland_2182025_301-1" id="mwIDM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIDQ">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Blaxland_2182025-301" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1090" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIDU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" web "},"2":{"wt":"last=Blaxland "},"3":{"wt":"first=John "},"4":{"wt":"date=February 18, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump&apos;s view of the world is becoming clear: America&apos;s allies come second to its own interests "},"6":{"wt":"work=The Conversation "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://theconversation.com/trumps-view-of-the-world-is-becoming-clear-americas-allies-come-second-to-its-own-interests-250144 "},"8":{"wt":"access-date=February 28, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"archive-date=February 26, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250226161634/https://theconversation.com/trumps-view-of-the-world-is-becoming-clear-americas-allies-come-second-to-its-own-interests-250144 "},"11":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBlaxland2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt1090">Blaxland, John (February 18, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://theconversation.com/trumps-view-of-the-world-is-becoming-clear-americas-allies-come-second-to-its-own-interests-250144" class="external text" id="mwIDY">"Trump's view of the world is becoming clear: America's allies come second to its own interests"</a>. <i id="mwIDc">The Conversation</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250226161634/https://theconversation.com/trumps-view-of-the-world-is-becoming-clear-americas-allies-come-second-to-its-own-interests-250144" class="external text" id="mwIDg">Archived</a> from the original on February 26, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIDk">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIDo">February 28,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Conversation&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+view+of+the+world+is+becoming+clear%3A+America%27s+allies+come+second+to+its+own+interests&amp;rft.date=2025-02-18&amp;rft.aulast=Blaxland&amp;rft.aufirst=John&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Ftheconversation.com%2Ftrumps-view-of-the-world-is-becoming-clear-americas-allies-come-second-to-its-own-interests-250144&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1090" id="mwIDs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Baker_02022025-302" id="cite_note-Baker_02022025-302" data-mw-footnote-number="301"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIDw"><a href="#cite_ref-Baker_02022025_302-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwID0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwID4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Baker_02022025-302" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1063" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwID8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"news"},"2":{"wt":"last=Baker"},"3":{"wt":"first=Peter"},"4":{"wt":"date=February 2, 2025"},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump Favors Blunt Force in Dealing With Foreign Allies and Enemies Alike"},"6":{"wt":"work=The New York Times"},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/02/us/politics/trump-tariffs-migrants-power.html"},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription"},"9":{"wt":"access-date=September 7, 2025"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFBaker2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1063">Baker, Peter (February 2, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIEA"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/02/us/politics/trump-tariffs-migrants-power.html" class="external text" id="mwIEE">"Trump Favors Blunt Force in Dealing With Foreign Allies and Enemies Alike"</a></span>. <i id="mwIEI">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIEM">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIEQ">September 7,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+Favors+Blunt+Force+in+Dealing+With+Foreign+Allies+and+Enemies+Alike&amp;rft.date=2025-02-02&amp;rft.aulast=Baker&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F02%2F02%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-tariffs-migrants-power.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1063" id="mwIEU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Hvistendahl_07232025-303" id="cite_note-Hvistendahl_07232025-303" data-mw-footnote-number="302"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIEY"><a href="#cite_ref-Hvistendahl_07232025_303-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIEc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIEg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hvistendahl_07232025-303" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1066" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIEk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"news"},"2":{"wt":"last=Hvistendahl"},"3":{"wt":"first=Mara"},"4":{"wt":"date=July 23, 2025"},"5":{"wt":"title=China Flexes Muscles at U.N. Cultural Agency, Just as Trump Walks Away"},"6":{"wt":"work=The New York Times"},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/23/world/asia/unesco-china-us.html"},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription"},"9":{"wt":"access-date=September 7, 2025"},"10":{"wt":"quote=The pullback reflects a broader American retreat from international bodies and Mr. Trump&apos;s dim view of soft power, the longstanding idea that America&apos;s cultural and economic influence abroad strengthens its hand in foreign affairs."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFHvistendahl2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1066">Hvistendahl, Mara (July 23, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIEo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/07/23/world/asia/unesco-china-us.html" class="external text" id="mwIEs">"China Flexes Muscles at U.N. Cultural Agency, Just as Trump Walks Away"</a></span>. <i id="mwIEw">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIE0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIE4">September 7,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIE8">The pullback reflects a broader American retreat from international bodies and Mr. Trump's dim view of soft power, the longstanding idea that America's cultural and economic influence abroad strengthens its hand in foreign affairs.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=China+Flexes+Muscles+at+U.N.+Cultural+Agency%2C+Just+as+Trump+Walks+Away&amp;rft.date=2025-07-23&amp;rft.aulast=Hvistendahl&amp;rft.aufirst=Mara&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F07%2F23%2Fworld%2Fasia%2Funesco-china-us.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1066" id="mwIFA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-304" id="cite_note-304" data-mw-footnote-number="303"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIFE"><a href="#cite_ref-304" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIFI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIFM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-304" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1069" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIFQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"news"},"2":{"wt":"last1=Basu"},"3":{"wt":"first1=Zachary"},"4":{"wt":"last2=Lawler"},"5":{"wt":"first2=Dave"},"6":{"wt":"date=July 17, 2025"},"7":{"wt":"title=Trump&apos;s soft-power retreat scrambles U.S.-China race"},"8":{"wt":"work=Axios"},"9":{"wt":"url=https://www.axios.com/2025/07/17/trump-china-retreat-soft-power"},"10":{"wt":"url-access=subscription"},"11":{"wt":"access-date=September 7, 2025"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwIFU" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1069" data-x-id="CITEREFBasuLawler2025">Basu, Zachary; Lawler, Dave (July 17, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIFY"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.axios.com/2025/07/17/trump-china-retreat-soft-power" class="external text" id="mwIFc">"Trump's soft-power retreat scrambles U.S.-China race"</a></span>. <i id="mwIFg">Axios</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIFk">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIFo">September 7,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+soft-power+retreat+scrambles+U.S.-China+race&amp;rft.date=2025-07-17&amp;rft.aulast=Basu&amp;rft.aufirst=Zachary&amp;rft.au=Lawler%2C+Dave&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2025%2F07%2F17%2Ftrump-china-retreat-soft-power&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1069" id="mwIFs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Hsu_06242025-305" id="cite_note-Hsu_06242025-305" data-mw-footnote-number="304"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIFw"><a href="#cite_ref-Hsu_06242025_305-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIF0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIF4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Hsu_06242025-305" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1072" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIF8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"news"},"2":{"wt":"last=Hsu"},"3":{"wt":"first=Tiffany"},"4":{"wt":"date=June 24, 2025"},"5":{"wt":"title=As U.S. Dismantles Voice of America, Rival Powers Hope to Fill the Void"},"6":{"wt":"work=The New York Times"},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/24/business/media/us-china-russia-global-communications.html"},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription"},"9":{"wt":"access-date=September 7, 2025"},"10":{"wt":"archive-date=September 10, 2025"},"11":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250910154648/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/24/business/media/us-china-russia-global-communications.html"},"12":{"wt":"url-status=live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwIGA" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1072" data-x-id="CITEREFHsu2025">Hsu, Tiffany (June 24, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIGE"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/24/business/media/us-china-russia-global-communications.html" class="external text" id="mwIGI">"As U.S. Dismantles Voice of America, Rival Powers Hope to Fill the Void"</a></span>. <i id="mwIGM">The New York Times</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250910154648/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/06/24/business/media/us-china-russia-global-communications.html" class="external text" id="mwIGQ">Archived</a> from the original on September 10, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIGU">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIGY">September 7,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=As+U.S.+Dismantles+Voice+of+America%2C+Rival+Powers+Hope+to+Fill+the+Void&amp;rft.date=2025-06-24&amp;rft.aulast=Hsu&amp;rft.aufirst=Tiffany&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F06%2F24%2Fbusiness%2Fmedia%2Fus-china-russia-global-communications.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1072" id="mwIGc"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Erlanger_2272025-306" id="cite_note-Erlanger_2272025-306" data-mw-footnote-number="305"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIGg"><a href="#cite_ref-Erlanger_2272025_306-0" id="mwIGk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIGo">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Erlanger_2272025_306-1" id="mwIGs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIGw">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Erlanger_2272025-306" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1077" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIG0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Erlanger "},"3":{"wt":"first=Steven "},"4":{"wt":"date=February 27, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Indifference or Hostility? Trump&apos;s View of European Allies Raises Alarm "},"6":{"wt":"work=The New York Times "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/world/europe/trump-eu-allies.html "},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription "},"9":{"wt":"access-date=February 28, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"quote=Mr. Trump has rebuffed NATO and aligned himself with the longstanding, principal threat to the alliance: Russia. "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=February 28, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250228010209/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/world/europe/trump-eu-allies.html/ "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFErlanger2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1077">Erlanger, Steven (February 27, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIG4"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/world/europe/trump-eu-allies.html" class="external text" id="mwIG8">"Indifference or Hostility? Trump's View of European Allies Raises Alarm"</a></span>. <i id="mwIHA">The New York Times</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250228010209/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/world/europe/trump-eu-allies.html/" class="external text" id="mwIHE">Archived</a> from the original on February 28, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIHI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIHM">February 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIHQ">Mr. Trump has rebuffed NATO and aligned himself with the longstanding, principal threat to the alliance: Russia.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Indifference+or+Hostility%3F+Trump%27s+View+of+European+Allies+Raises+Alarm&amp;rft.date=2025-02-27&amp;rft.aulast=Erlanger&amp;rft.aufirst=Steven&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F02%2F27%2Fworld%2Feurope%2Ftrump-eu-allies.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1077" id="mwIHU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Broadwater_2272025-307" id="cite_note-Broadwater_2272025-307" data-mw-footnote-number="306"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIHY"><a href="#cite_ref-Broadwater_2272025_307-0" id="mwIHc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIHg">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Broadwater_2272025_307-1" id="mwIHk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIHo">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Broadwater_2272025-307" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1080" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIHs" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Broadwater "},"3":{"wt":"first=Luke "},"4":{"wt":"date=February 27, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=With Trump, Alliances Come With Strings Attached "},"6":{"wt":"work=The New York Times "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/us/politics/trump-alliances-ukraine-russia.html "},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription "},"9":{"wt":"access-date=February 28, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"quote=But it underscores Mr. Trump&apos;s impulse to squeeze even America&apos;s traditional allies as he applies his transactional approach to foreign policy. "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=March 1, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250301023027/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/us/politics/trump-alliances-ukraine-russia.html "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwIHw" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1080" data-x-id="CITEREFBroadwater2025">Broadwater, Luke (February 27, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIH0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/us/politics/trump-alliances-ukraine-russia.html" class="external text" id="mwIH4">"With Trump, Alliances Come With Strings Attached"</a></span>. <i id="mwIH8">The New York Times</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250301023027/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/27/us/politics/trump-alliances-ukraine-russia.html" class="external text" id="mwIIA">Archived</a> from the original on March 1, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIIE">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIII">February 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIIM">But it underscores Mr. Trump's impulse to squeeze even America's traditional allies as he applies his transactional approach to foreign policy.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=With+Trump%2C+Alliances+Come+With+Strings+Attached&amp;rft.date=2025-02-27&amp;rft.aulast=Broadwater&amp;rft.aufirst=Luke&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F02%2F27%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-alliances-ukraine-russia.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1080" id="mwIIQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-308" id="cite_note-308" data-mw-footnote-number="307"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIIU"><a href="#cite_ref-308" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIIY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIIc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-308" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1083" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIIg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last=Baker "},"3":{"wt":"first=Peter "},"4":{"wt":"date=February 25, 2025 "},"5":{"wt":"title=Under Trump, America&apos;s New Friends: Russia, North Korea and Belarus "},"6":{"wt":"work=The New York Times "},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/25/us/politics/trump-diplomacy.html "},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription "},"9":{"wt":"access-date=March 2, 2025 "},"10":{"wt":"quote=It would be hard to think of a starker demonstration of how radically Mr. Trump is recalibrating America&apos;s place in the world after barely a month back in office. He is positioning the United States in the camp of the globe&apos;s chief rogue states in opposition to the countries that have been America&apos;s best friends since World War II or before. "},"11":{"wt":"archive-date=March 1, 2025 "},"12":{"wt":"archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250301105743/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/25/us/politics/trump-diplomacy.html "},"13":{"wt":"url-status=live "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwIIk" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1083" data-x-id="CITEREFBaker2025">Baker, Peter (February 25, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIIo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/25/us/politics/trump-diplomacy.html" class="external text" id="mwIIs">"Under Trump, America's New Friends: Russia, North Korea and Belarus"</a></span>. <i id="mwIIw">The New York Times</i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250301105743/https://www.nytimes.com/2025/02/25/us/politics/trump-diplomacy.html" class="external text" id="mwII0">Archived</a> from the original on March 1, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwII4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwII8">March 2,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIJA">It would be hard to think of a starker demonstration of how radically Mr. Trump is recalibrating America's place in the world after barely a month back in office. He is positioning the United States in the camp of the globe's chief rogue states in opposition to the countries that have been America's best friends since World War II or before.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Under+Trump%2C+America%27s+New+Friends%3A+Russia%2C+North+Korea+and+Belarus&amp;rft.date=2025-02-25&amp;rft.aulast=Baker&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F02%2F25%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-diplomacy.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1083" id="mwIJE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-309" id="cite_note-309" data-mw-footnote-number="308"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIJI"><a href="#cite_ref-309" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIJM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIJQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-309" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1086" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwIJU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite magazine ","href":"./Template:Cite_magazine"},"params":{"date":{"wt":"February 27, 2025"},"title":{"wt":"Donald Trump has begun a mafia-like struggle for global power"},"magazine":{"wt":"The Economist"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.economist.com/leaders/2025/02/27/donald-trump-has-begun-a-mafia-like-struggle-for-global-power?itm_source=parsely-api"},"url-access":{"wt":"subscription"},"access-date":{"wt":"February 28, 2025"},"quote":{"wt":"The rupture of the post-1945 order is gaining pace. In extraordinary scenes at the UN this week, America sided with Russia and North Korea against Ukraine and Europe. Germany&apos;s probable new chancellor, Friedrich Merz, warns that by June NATO may be dead. Fast approaching is a might-is-right world in which big powers cut deals and bully small ones."},"archive-date":{"wt":"March 2, 2025"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250302140202/https://www.economist.com/leaders/2025/02/27/donald-trump-has-begun-a-mafia-like-struggle-for-global-power?itm_source=parsely-api"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation magazine cs1" about="#mwt1086" id="mwIJY"><span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwIJc"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.economist.com/leaders/2025/02/27/donald-trump-has-begun-a-mafia-like-struggle-for-global-power?itm_source=parsely-api" class="external text" id="mwIJg">"Donald Trump has begun a mafia-like struggle for global power"</a></span>. <i id="mwIJk">The Economist</i>. February 27, 2025. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20250302140202/https://www.economist.com/leaders/2025/02/27/donald-trump-has-begun-a-mafia-like-struggle-for-global-power?itm_source=parsely-api" class="external text" id="mwIJo">Archived</a> from the original on March 2, 2025<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIJs">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIJw">February 28,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwIJ0">The rupture of the post-1945 order is gaining pace. In extraordinary scenes at the UN this week, America sided with Russia and North Korea against Ukraine and Europe. Germany's probable new chancellor, Friedrich Merz, warns that by June NATO may be dead. Fast approaching is a might-is-right world in which big powers cut deals and bully small ones.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Economist&amp;rft.atitle=Donald+Trump+has+begun+a+mafia-like+struggle+for+global+power&amp;rft.date=2025-02-27&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.economist.com%2Fleaders%2F2025%2F02%2F27%2Fdonald-trump-has-begun-a-mafia-like-struggle-for-global-power%3Fitm_source%3Dparsely-api&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1086" id="mwIJ4"></span></span></li>
