%2F04%2F08%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-admin-aid-yemen-afghanistan%2Findex.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1838" id="mwKVY"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025-539" id="cite_note-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025-539" data-mw-footnote-number="537"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwKVc"><a href="#cite_ref-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025_539-0" id="mwKVg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwKVk">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025_539-1" id="mwKVo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwKVs">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-CBS,_Trump's_request_to_cancel_billions,_July_15,_2025-539" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt1842" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwKVw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"date=July 15, 2025 "},"3":{"wt":"title=Senate advances Trump&apos;s request to cancel billions in foreign aid, NPR and PBS funding "},"4":{"wt":"url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/senate-rescissions-package-foreign-aid-npr-pbs-funding/ "},"5":{"wt":"work=CBS "},"6":{"wt":"quote=The rescissions request would cut $8.3 billion for the United States Agency for International Development, or USAID, along with other international assistance programs — from peacekeeping efforts to refugee assistance and climate projects. "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt1842" id="mwKV0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cbsnews.com/news/senate-rescissions-package-foreign-aid-npr-pbs-funding/" class="external text" id="mwKV4">"Senate advances Trump's request to cancel billions in foreign aid, NPR and PBS funding"</a>. <i id="mwKV8">CBS</i>. July 15, 2025. <q id="mwKWA">The rescissions request would cut $8.3 billion for the United States Agency for International Development, or USAID, along with other international assistance programs — from peacekeeping efforts to refugee assistance and climate projects.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CBS&amp;rft.atitle=Senate+advances+Trump%27s+request+to+cancel+billions+in+foreign+aid%2C+NPR+and+PBS+funding&amp;rft.date=2025-07-15&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cbsnews.com%2Fnews%2Fsenate-rescissions-package-foreign-aid-npr-pbs-funding%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt1842" id="mwKWE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025-540" id="cite_note-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025-540" data-mw-footnote-number="538"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwKWI"><a href="#cite_ref-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025_540-0" id="mwKWM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwKWQ">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025_540-1" id="mwKWU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwKWY">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC,_Senate_to_vote_to_formalize,_July_14,_2025-540" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/senate-formalize-cuts-public-broadcast-usaid-weeks-end/story?id=123741614" class="external text" id="mwKWc">"Senate to vote to formalize DOGE cuts to public broadcasting, USAID"</a>, <i id="mwKWg">ABC News</i>, July 14, 2025. In a post on July 10, President Trump said, "It is very important that all Republicans adhere to my Recissions Bill and, in particular, DEFUND THE CORPORATION FOR PUBLIC BROADCASTING (PBS and NPR), which is worse than CNN &amp; MSDNC put together. Any Republican that votes to allow this monstrosity to continue broadcasting will not have my support or Endorsement. Thank you for your attention to this matter!"</span></li>
