<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026-606" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026-606" data-mw-footnote-number="604"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwK9k"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026_606-0" id="mwK9o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK9s">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026_606-1" id="mwK9w"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK90">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026-606" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2061" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwK94" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFHorowitz2026" class="citation news cs1">Horowitz, Jason (July 2, 2026). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwK98"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/07/02/world/europe/trump-world-leaders-corruption-wealth.html" class="external text" id="mwK-A">"Trump's Huge Windfall Has Few Known Global Precedents"</a></span>. <i id="mwK-E">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwK-I">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwK-M">August 10,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+Huge+Windfall+Has+Few+Known+Global+Precedents&amp;rft.date=2026-07-02&amp;rft.aulast=Horowitz&amp;rft.aufirst=Jason&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2026%2F07%2F02%2Fworld%2Feurope%2Ftrump-world-leaders-corruption-wealth.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwK-Q"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026-607" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026-607" data-mw-footnote-number="605"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwK-U"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026_607-0" id="mwK-Y"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK-c">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026_607-1" id="mwK-g"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK-k">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026-607" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2066" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwK-o" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFStone2026" class="citation news cs1">Stone, Peter (August 13, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/13/trump-presidency-revenue-wealth" class="external text" id="mwK-s">"Trump has amassed staggering wealth in 'most openly corrupt' presidency"</a>. <i id="mwK-w">The Guardian</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwK-0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwK-4">August 13,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwK-8">Former federal officials, historians and other experts have raised "corruption" concerns and other red flags as Trump has monetized his presidency for personal gain in ways that far exceed any other president's tenure. ... Former election officials concur that Trump is cashing in on his presidency to an unprecedented level.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+has+amassed+staggering+wealth+in+%E2%80%98most+openly+corrupt%E2%80%99+presidency&amp;rft.date=2026-08-13&amp;rft.aulast=Stone&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2026%2Faug%2F13%2Ftrump-presidency-revenue-wealth&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwK_A"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026-608" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026-608" data-mw-footnote-number="606"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwK_E"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026_608-0" id="mwK_I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK_M">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026_608-1" id="mwK_Q"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK_U">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026-608" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2071" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwK_Y" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFSonneLipton2026" class="citation news cs1">Sonne, Paul; Lipton, Eric (July 14, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/06/28/world/europe/trump-lutnick-sons-kazakhstan.html" class="external text" id="mwK_c">"Trump Cut a Billion-Dollar Mining Deal. His Sons Stand to Profit"</a>. <i id="mwK_g">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwK_k">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwK_o">August 10,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwK_s">Their sons were soon doing business with partners in a deal that their fathers were negotiating, continuing a pattern of self-enrichment in the second Trump administration that has few precedents in American history.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+Cut+a+Billion-Dollar+Mining+Deal.+His+Sons+Stand+to+Profit.&amp;rft.date=2026-07-14&amp;rft.aulast=Sonne&amp;rft.aufirst=Paul&amp;rft.au=Lipton%2C+Eric&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2026%2F06%2F28%2Fworld%2Feurope%2Ftrump-lutnick-sons-kazakhstan.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwK_w"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" data-mw-footnote-number="607"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwK_0"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-0" id="mwK_4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwK_8">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-1" id="mwLAA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLAE">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-2" id="mwLAI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLAM">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-3" id="mwLAQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLAU">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2076" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLAY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFDawseyMattioliLinskeyGlazer2026" class="citation news cs1">Dawsey, Josh; Mattioli, Dana; Linskey, Annie; Glazer, Emily (July 30, 2026). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwLAc"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trump-donations-company-fundraising-1e34a78f" class="external text" id="mwLAg">"<span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwLAk"></span>'The Boss Wants This Money': Inside Trump's Unprecedented Fundraising Operation"</a></span>. <i id="mwLAo">The Wall Street Journal</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLAs">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLAw">August 10,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLA0">Trump is shattering all fundraising paradigms in regards to hitting up corporate America for donations. The scope is mind-bogglingly large," said Douglas Brinkley, a presidential historian at Rice University. "We used to talk about the Lincoln bedroom being for sale, but this is just a wholesale money trough that's totally different.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Wall+Street+Journal&amp;rft.atitle=%27The+Boss+Wants+This+Money%27%3A+Inside+Trump%E2%80%99s+Unprecedented+Fundraising+Operation&amp;rft.date=2026-07-30&amp;rft.aulast=Dawsey&amp;rft.aufirst=Josh&amp;rft.au=Mattioli%2C+Dana&amp;rft.au=Linskey%2C+Annie&amp;rft.au=Glazer%2C+Emily&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.wsj.com%2Fpolitics%2Fpolicy%2Ftrump-donations-company-fundraising-1e34a78f&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLA4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610" data-mw-footnote-number="608"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLA8"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025_610-0" id="mwLBA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLBE">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025_610-1" id="mwLBI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLBM">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025_610-2" id="mwLBQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLBU">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2081" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLBY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFStringerLawford2025" class="citation news cs1">Stringer, Connor; Lawford, Melissa (May 18, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.telegraph.co.uk/business/2025/05/18/trump-turned-white-house-cash-machine/" class="external text" id="mwLBc">"<span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwLBg"></span>'It's open season for corruption': How Trump turned the White House into a cash cow"</a>. <i id="mwLBk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Daily_Telegraph" title="The Daily Telegraph" id="mwLBo">The Daily Telegraph</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLBs">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLBw">May 18,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLB0"><span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwLB4"></span>"We've never seen anything like this in American history," says Norm Eisen, a former White House ethics tsar.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Daily+Telegraph&amp;rft.atitle=%27It%27s+open+season+for+corruption%27%3A+How+Trump+turned+the+White+House+into+a+cash+cow&amp;rft.date=2025-05-18&amp;rft.aulast=Stringer&amp;rft.aufirst=Connor&amp;rft.au=Lawford%2C+Melissa&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.telegraph.co.uk%2Fbusiness%2F2025%2F05%2F18%2Ftrump-turned-white-house-cash-machine%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLB8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-611" id="cite_note-611" data-mw-footnote-number="609"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLCA"><a href="#cite_ref-611" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLCE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLCI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-611" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2086" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLCM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFTuckerRicher2026" class="citation news cs1">Tucker, Eric; Richer, Alanna Durkin (July 13, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://apnews.com/article/trump-irs-justice-department-61adebe5de8982eb214b30889ad4f251" class="external text" id="mwLCQ">"Judge says Trump IRS lawsuit was filed for 'improper purpose,' refers lawyer for possible discipline"</a>. <i id="mwLCU">AP News</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLCY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLCc">August 10,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLCg">President Donald Trump's lawsuit against the Internal Revenue Service over his leaked tax returns was filed for an "improper purpose," a judge said Monday as she referred one of his lawyers for potential disciplinary action and characterized the $10 billion complaint as an exercise in self-dealing. U.S. District Judge Kathleen Williams accused Trump and his lawyers in a scathing ruling of having manipulated the court system when he sued a federal agency under his control, bypassing a requirement that parties in a lawsuit must have adverse interests.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=AP+News&amp;rft.atitle=Judge+says+Trump+IRS+lawsuit+was+filed+for+%E2%80%98improper+purpose%2C%E2%80%99+refers+lawyer+for+possible+discipline&amp;rft.date=2026-07-13&amp;rft.aulast=Tucker&amp;rft.aufirst=Eric&amp;rft.au=Richer%2C+Alanna+Durkin&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Ftrump-irs-justice-department-61adebe5de8982eb214b30889ad4f251&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLCk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026-612" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026-612" data-mw-footnote-number="610"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLCo"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026_612-0" id="mwLCs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLCw">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026_612-1" id="mwLC0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLC4">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026-612" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2091" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLC8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFKirkpatrick2026" class="citation news cs1">Kirkpatrick, David (July 2, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.newyorker.com/news/the-lede/the-unprecedented-profiteering-revealed-by-donald-trumps-financial-disclosure" class="external text" id="mwLDA">"The Unprecedented Profiteering Revealed by Donald Trump's Financial Disclosure"</a>. <i id="mwLDE">The New Yorker</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLDI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLDM">August 24,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+Yorker&amp;rft.atitle=The+Unprecedented+Profiteering+Revealed+by+Donald+Trump%27s+Financial+Disclosure&amp;rft.date=2026-07-02&amp;rft.aulast=Kirkpatrick&amp;rft.aufirst=David&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.newyorker.com%2Fnews%2Fthe-lede%2Fthe-unprecedented-profiteering-revealed-by-donald-trumps-financial-disclosure&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLDQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-613" id="cite_note-613" data-mw-footnote-number="611"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLDU"><a href="#cite_ref-613" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLDY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLDc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-613" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2096" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLDg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwLDk" class="citation news cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFSavage2025">Savage, Charlie (May 12, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwLDo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/12/us/trump-qatar-jet-plane.html" class="external text" id="mwLDs">"Trump's Plan to Take Jet From Qatar Heightens Corruption Concerns"</a></span>. <i id="mwLDw">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLD0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLD4">May 18,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLD8">During President Trump's first term, the idea that special interests and governments were buying meals and booking rooms at his hotels set off legal and ethical alarms about the potential for corruption. Mr. Trump's second term is making those concerns look trivial.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+Plan+to+Take+Jet+From+Qatar+Heightens+Corruption+Concerns&amp;rft.date=2025-05-12&amp;rft.aulast=Savage&amp;rft.aufirst=Charlie&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F05%2F12%2Fus%2Ftrump-qatar-jet-plane.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLEA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-614" id="cite_note-614" data-mw-footnote-number="612"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLEE"><a href="#cite_ref-614" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLEI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLEM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-614" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2101" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLEQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFHulse2025" class="citation news cs1">Hulse, Carl (May 13, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwLEU"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/13/us/politics/congress-republican-reaction-trump-qatar-plane.html" class="external text" id="mwLEY">"As Trump Courts Gifts and Dangles Access, Congress Sits on the Sidelines"</a></span>. <i id="mwLEc">The New York Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLEg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLEk">May 18,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLEo">Nearly three decades later, President Trump has drawn accusations of corruption and self-dealing for publicly flirting with accepting a $400 million luxury jet from Qatar and promising an exclusive country club dinner and White House tour for the largest buyers of his crypto coin, one of many financial exploits enriching him and his family.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=As+Trump+Courts+Gifts+and+Dangles+Access%2C+Congress+Sits+on+the+Sidelines&amp;rft.date=2025-05-13&amp;rft.aulast=Hulse&amp;rft.aufirst=Carl&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F05%2F13%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Fcongress-republican-reaction-trump-qatar-plane.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLEs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-615" id="cite_note-615" data-mw-footnote-number="613"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLEw"><a href="#cite_ref-615" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLE0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLE4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-615" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2106" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLE8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFTuckerRicher2025" class="citation news cs1">Tucker, Eric; Richer, Alana Durkin (April 7, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://apnews.com/article/justice-department-mel-gibson-congress-667a79b368b215bb0cd7b0333f372fc7" class="external text" id="mwLFA">"Fired Justice Department pardon attorney accuses the agency of 'ongoing corruption,' abuse of power"</a>. <i id="mwLFE">The Associated Press</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLFI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLFM">May 31,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Associated+Press&amp;rft.atitle=Fired+Justice+Department+pardon+attorney+accuses+the+agency+of+%27ongoing+corruption%2C%27+abuse+of+power&amp;rft.date=2025-04-07&amp;rft.aulast=Tucker&amp;rft.aufirst=Eric&amp;rft.au=Richer%2C+Alana+Durkin&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Fjustice-department-mel-gibson-congress-667a79b368b215bb0cd7b0333f372fc7&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLFQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-616" id="cite_note-616" data-mw-footnote-number="614"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLFU"><a href="#cite_ref-616" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLFY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLFc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-616" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2111" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLFg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFWendling2025" class="citation news cs1">Wendling, Mike (May 14, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckg4zk22n9wo" class="external text" id="mwLFk">"Trump's critics and supporters unite against Qatar plane deal"</a>. <i id="mwLFo">BBC News</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLFs">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLFw">May 18,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLF0">Maga influencers have described the move as a "bribe", grift, or an example of the high-level corruption that Trump himself has consistently promised to root out.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=BBC+News&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+critics+and+supporters+unite+against+Qatar+plane+deal&amp;rft.date=2025-05-14&amp;rft.aulast=Wendling&amp;rft.aufirst=Mike&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2Fckg4zk22n9wo&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLF4"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-617" id="cite_note-617" data-mw-footnote-number="615"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLF8"><a href="#cite_ref-617" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLGA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLGE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-617" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2116" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLGI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwLGM" class="citation web cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFStone2025">Stone, Peter (May 25, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/may/25/trump-crypto-corruption-ethics" class="external text" id="mwLGQ">"<span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwLGU"></span>'Roadmap for corruption': Trump dive into cryptocurrency raises ethics alarm"</a>. <i id="mwLGY">The Guardian</i>. <q id="mwLGc">Fears of possible corruption have also focused on Chinese-born Justin Sun, the biggest investor in Trump's crypto ventures. ... "There is the appearance if not the reality of corruption in the upcoming dinner with Trump on the 22nd at his Virginia golf club for the 220 biggest Trump meme coin buyers and the private reception he's promised for the top 25 buyers, plus the separate $2bn deal between World Liberty Financial and the Abu Dhabi investment vehicle," said Richard Painter, a former White House ethics adviser to George W Bush who co-authored the Democracy Defenders Fund report. ... "Trump's dealings in crypto appear to present the greatest conflicts of interest and avenues for corruption any president has ever embraced," said Larry Noble, a former general counsel at the Federal Election Commission who now teaches law at American University. ... "Trump has taken corruption and self-dealing to a new level," said the ex-Republican congressman Dave Trott of Michigan.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=%27Roadmap+for+corruption%27%3A+Trump+dive+into+cryptocurrency+raises+ethics+alarm&amp;rft.date=2025-05-25&amp;rft.aulast=Stone&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2025%2Fmay%2F25%2Ftrump-crypto-corruption-ethics&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLGg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-618" id="cite_note-618" data-mw-footnote-number="616"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLGk"><a href="#cite_ref-618" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLGo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLGs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-618" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2121" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLGw" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFLandersAdams2026" class="citation news cs1">Landers, Liz; Adams, Doug (May 28, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/trump-stock-trades-fuel-accusations-of-corruption-and-profiting-off-presidency" class="external text" id="mwLG0">"Trump stock trades fuel accusations of corruption and profiting off presidency"</a>. <i id="mwLG4">PBS News</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLG8">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLHA">August 24,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=PBS+News&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+stock+trades+fuel+accusations+of+corruption+and+profiting+off+presidency&amp;rft.date=2026-05-28&amp;rft.aulast=Landers&amp;rft.aufirst=Liz&amp;rft.au=Adams%2C+Doug&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pbs.org%2Fnewshour%2Fshow%2Ftrump-stock-trades-fuel-accusations-of-corruption-and-profiting-off-presidency&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLHE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-619" id="cite_note-619" data-mw-footnote-number="617"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLHI"><a href="#cite_ref-619" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLHM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLHQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-619" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2126" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLHU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwLHY"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.npr.org/2026/05/25/nx-s1-5833813/warning-flags-about-the-trump-administration-and-alleged-corruption" class="external text" id="mwLHc">"Warning flags about the Trump administration and alleged corruption"</a>. <i id="mwLHg">NPR</i>. May 25, 2026<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLHk">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLHo">August 24,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=NPR&amp;rft.atitle=Warning+flags+about+the+Trump+administration+and+alleged+corruption&amp;rft.date=2026-05-25&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npr.org%2F2026%2F05%2F25%2Fnx-s1-5833813%2Fwarning-flags-about-the-trump-administration-and-alleged-corruption&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLHs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-620" id="cite_note-620" data-mw-footnote-number="618"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLHw"><a href="#cite_ref-620" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLH0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLH4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-620" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2131" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLH8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFJohnston2026" class="citation web cs1">Johnston, Michael (August 6, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.foreignaffairs.com/united-states/new-american-hustle" class="external text" id="mwLIA">"The New American Hustle: Trump Is Changing Corruption—and Making It More Dangerous"</a>. <i id="mwLIE">Foreign Affairs</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLII">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLIM">August 24,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLIQ">Whether he is launching cryptocurrency schemes or accepting a Qatari jumbo jet or issuing pardons for the relatives of major donors, Donald Trump has drawn frequent accusations of corruption in the early months of his second term as U.S. president. Each instance of corruption raises critical concerns about misused authority, undemocratic governance, or foreign influence. But larger trends in corruption are notoriously difficult to assess.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Foreign+Affairs&amp;rft.atitle=The+New+American+Hustle%3A+Trump+Is+Changing+Corruption%E2%80%94and+Making+It+More+Dangerous&amp;rft.date=2026-08-06&amp;rft.aulast=Johnston&amp;rft.aufirst=Michael&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.foreignaffairs.com%2Funited-states%2Fnew-american-hustle&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLIU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-621" id="cite_note-621" data-mw-footnote-number="619"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLIY"><a href="#cite_ref-621" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLIc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLIg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-621" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2146" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLIk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwLIo" class="citation news cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFStone2026">Stone, Peter (August 13, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/13/trump-presidency-revenue-wealth" class="external text" id="mwLIs">"Trump has amassed staggering wealth in 'most openly corrupt' presidency"</a>. <i id="mwLIw">The Guardian</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLI0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLI4">August 13,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLI8">Former federal officials, historians and other experts have raised "corruption" concerns and other red flags as Trump has monetized his presidency for personal gain in ways that far exceed any other president's tenure. ... Former election officials concur that Trump is cashing in on his presidency to an unprecedented level.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Guardian&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+has+amassed+staggering+wealth+in+%E2%80%98most+openly+corrupt%E2%80%99+presidency&amp;rft.date=2026-08-13&amp;rft.aulast=Stone&amp;rft.aufirst=Peter&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theguardian.com%2Fus-news%2F2026%2Faug%2F13%2Ftrump-presidency-revenue-wealth&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLJA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-622" id="cite_note-622" data-mw-footnote-number="620"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLJE"><a href="#cite_ref-622" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLJI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLJM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-622" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2155" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLJQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFBush2026" class="citation news cs1">Bush, Daniel (July 1, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c70yk07vq0po" class="external text" id="mwLJU">"From Truman's pension to Trump's billions - a White House windfall unmatched by any president"</a>. <i id="mwLJY">BBC News</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLJc">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLJg">August 24,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLJk">Donald Trump, in contrast, made at least $2.2bn (£1.7bn) in his first year back in office, according to a new financial disclosure report - a sum historians said was unprecedented and shattered the norm of US presidents avoiding financial conflicts of interest in the White House. "There's just no precedent for this," said Barbara Perry, a presidential historian at the University of Virginia's Miller Center. "It's beyond anything we've ever seen in the presidency."<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwLJo"></span></q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=BBC+News&amp;rft.atitle=From+Truman%27s+pension+to+Trump%27s+billions+-+a+White+House+windfall+unmatched+by+any+president&amp;rft.date=2026-07-01&amp;rft.aulast=Bush&amp;rft.aufirst=Daniel&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bbc.com%2Fnews%2Farticles%2Fc70yk07vq0po&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLJs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-623" id="cite_note-623" data-mw-footnote-number="621"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLJw"><a href="#cite_ref-623" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLJ0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLJ4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-623" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2160" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLJ8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFVandeHeiAllen2026" class="citation news cs1">VandeHei, Jim; Allen, Mike (May 22, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.axios.com/2026/05/22/trump-profit-presidency-stocks-crypto-irs-taxes" class="external text" id="mwLKA">"Behind the Curtain: Trump's unprecedented profit and protection"</a>. <i id="mwLKE">Axios</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLKI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLKM">August 24,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLKQ">Never in 250 years has America witnessed a sitting president shield himself and his family from tax scrutiny, after leveraging policies that benefit his own businesses and personal portfolios, as Donald J. Trump has done. Why it matters: This isn't a hidden scandal. Trump has done this publicly and proudly. Last year, we called it the "most unprecedented presidency in 250 years." In doing so, he has set a precedent — once so unfathomable as to be laughable — that it's OK for presidents and family members to make billions off deals affected by government decisions, then use the Justice Department to secure lifetime protection from scrutiny of their past tax returns.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=Behind+the+Curtain%3A+Trump%27s+unprecedented+profit+and+protection&amp;rft.date=2026-05-22&amp;rft.aulast=VandeHei&amp;rft.aufirst=Jim&amp;rft.au=Allen%2C+Mike&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2026%2F05%2F22%2Ftrump-profit-presidency-stocks-crypto-irs-taxes&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLKU"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-624" id="cite_note-624" data-mw-footnote-number="622"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLKY"><a href="#cite_ref-624" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLKc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLKg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-624" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2165" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLKk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFHarwwood2026" class="citation news cs1">Harwwood, John (July 1, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnbc.com/2018/06/28/trump-collects-on-business-and-presidency-is-boosting-brand.html" class="external text" id="mwLKo">"President Trump's money-making power is as unprecedented as his words"</a>. <i id="mwLKs">CNBC</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLKw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLK0">August 24,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLK4">What comes out of Donald Trump's mouth is, for a president of the United States, unprecedented. So is what goes into his wallet.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNBC&amp;rft.atitle=President+Trump%E2%80%99s+money-making+power+is+as+unprecedented+as+his+words&amp;rft.date=2026-07-01&amp;rft.aulast=Harwwood&amp;rft.aufirst=John&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2018%2F06%2F28%2Ftrump-collects-on-business-and-presidency-is-boosting-brand.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLK8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-625" id="cite_note-625" data-mw-footnote-number="623"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLLA"><a href="#cite_ref-625" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLLE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLLI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-625" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2172" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLLM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFCancrynHerbTolan2026" class="citation news cs1">Cancryn, Adam; Herb, Jeremy; Tolan, Casey (July 2, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/06/30/politics/trump-cryptocurrency-millions-disclosures" class="external text" id="mwLLQ">"Trump made more than a billion dollars from cryptocurrency ventures in first year back in office"</a>. <i id="mwLLU">CNN</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLLY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLLc">August 24,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLLg">The scope and scale of Trump's holdings continued an unprecedented streak of profit-making for a sitting president that has drawn sharp criticism from opponents and repeated accusations of conflicts of interest.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNN&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+made+more+than+a+billion+dollars+from+cryptocurrency+ventures+in+first+year+back+in+office&amp;rft.date=2026-07-02&amp;rft.aulast=Cancryn&amp;rft.aufirst=Adam&amp;rft.au=Herb%2C+Jeremy&amp;rft.au=Tolan%2C+Casey&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnn.com%2F2026%2F06%2F30%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-cryptocurrency-millions-disclosures&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLLk"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-626" id="cite_note-626" data-mw-footnote-number="624"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLLo"><a href="#cite_ref-626" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLLs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLLw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-626" class="mw-reference-text reference-text">Numerous sources and Trump's financial disclosures have attested to Trump's unprecedented self-enrichment and conflicts of interest,<sup about="#mwt2057" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_NYT_06302026_605-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency NYT 06302026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_NYT_06302026-605"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_NYT_06302026-605" id="mwLL0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLL4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLL8">[</span>603<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2062" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026_606-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Horowitz 07022026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026-606"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026-606" id="mwLME"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLMI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMM">[</span>604<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2067" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026_607-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Peter 08132026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026-607"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026-607" id="mwLMU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLMY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMc">[</span>605<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2072" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026_608-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Sonne 07142026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026-608"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026-608" id="mwLMk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLMo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMs">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLMw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2077" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Dawsey 08102026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" id="mwLM0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLM4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLM8">[</span>607<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2082" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025_610-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Stringer 05182025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610" id="mwLNE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLNI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNM">[</span>608<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2087" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-611" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-611"}}'><a href="#cite_note-611" id="mwLNU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLNY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNc">[</span>609<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2092" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026_612-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Kirkpatrick 07022026"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026-612"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Kirkpatrick_07022026-612" id="mwLNk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLNo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNs">[</span>610<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLNw">]</span></span></a></sup> referred to it as corruption,<sup about="#mwt2097" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-613" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-613"}}'><a href="#cite_note-613" id="mwLN0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLN4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLN8">[</span>611<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2102" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-614" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-614"}}'><a href="#cite_note-614" id="mwLOE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLOI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOM">[</span>612<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-615" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-615"}}'><a href="#cite_note-615" id="mwLOU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLOY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOc">[</span>613<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-616" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-616"}}'><a href="#cite_note-616" id="mwLOk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLOo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOs">[</span>614<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLOw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-617" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-617"}}'><a href="#cite_note-617" id="mwLO0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLO4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLO8">[</span>615<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-618" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-618"}}'><a href="#cite_note-618" id="mwLPE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLPI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPM">[</span>616<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-619" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-619"}}'><a href="#cite_note-619" id="mwLPU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLPY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPc">[</span>617<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-620" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-620"}}'><a href="#cite_note-620" id="mwLPk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLPo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPs">[</span>618<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLPw">]</span></span></a></sup> and described it as unprecedented in American history.<sup about="#mwt2135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_NYT_06302026_605-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency NYT 06302026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_NYT_06302026-605" id="mwLP0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLP4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLP8">[</span>603<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2137" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026_606-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Horowitz 07022026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Horowitz_07022026-606" id="mwLQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQM">[</span>604<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026_607-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Peter 08132026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Peter_08132026-607" id="mwLQU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQc">[</span>605<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2141" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026_608-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Sonne 07142026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sonne_07142026-608" id="mwLQk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQs">[</span>606<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Dawsey 08102026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" id="mwLQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLQ8">[</span>607<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2147" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-621" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-621"}}'><a href="#cite_note-621" id="mwLRE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLRI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRM">[</span>619<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2150" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026_609-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Dawsey 08102026"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Dawsey_08102026-609" id="mwLRU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLRY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRc">[</span>607<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2152" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025_610-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Stringer 05182025"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Stringer_05182025-610" id="mwLRk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLRo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRs">[</span>608<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLRw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2156" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-622" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-622"}}'><a href="#cite_note-622" id="mwLR0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLR4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLR8">[</span>620<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLSA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2161" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-623" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-623"}}'><a href="#cite_note-623" id="mwLSE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLSI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLSM">[</span>621<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLSQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2166" class="mw-ref