<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025-645" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025-645" data-mw-footnote-number="643"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLek"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025_645-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLeo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLes">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025-645" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2325" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLew" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFSneed2025" class="citation news cs1">Sneed, Tierney (January 23, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnn.com/2025/01/23/politics/birthright-citizenship-lawsuit-hearing-seattle/index.html" class="external text" id="mwLe0">"Judge blocks Trump's 'blatantly unconstitutional' executive order that aims to end birthright citizenship"</a>. <i id="mwLe4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN" title="CNN" id="mwLe8">CNN</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLfA">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLfE">January 23,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNN&amp;rft.atitle=Judge+blocks+Trump%27s+%27blatantly+unconstitutional%27+executive+order+that+aims+to+end+birthright+citizenship&amp;rft.date=2025-01-23&amp;rft.aulast=Sneed&amp;rft.aufirst=Tierney&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnn.com%2F2025%2F01%2F23%2Fpolitics%2Fbirthright-citizenship-lawsuit-hearing-seattle%2Findex.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLfI"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025-646" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025-646" data-mw-footnote-number="644"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLfM"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025_646-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLfQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLfU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025-646" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2330" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLfY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFLucas2025" class="citation news cs1">Lucas, Ryan (May 2, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwLfc"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.npr.org/2025/05/02/nx-s1-5385355/perkins-coie-trump-executive-order-law-firms" class="external text" id="mwLfg">"Federal judge strikes down Trump order targeting the law firm Perkins Coie"</a></span>. <i id="mwLfk">NPR News</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLfo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLfs">August 18,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLfw">A federal judge on Friday struck down President Trump's executive order targeting the prominent law firm of Perkins Coie, finding it unconstitutional and declaring it an attack on the foundational principles of the American legal system.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=NPR+News&amp;rft.atitle=Federal+judge+strikes+down+Trump+order+targeting+the+law+firm+Perkins+Coie&amp;rft.date=2025-05-02&amp;rft.aulast=Lucas&amp;rft.aufirst=Ryan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npr.org%2F2025%2F05%2F02%2Fnx-s1-5385355%2Fperkins-coie-trump-executive-order-law-firms&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLf0"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-647" id="cite_note-647" data-mw-footnote-number="645"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLf4"><a href="#cite_ref-647" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLf8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLgA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-647" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2335" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLgE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFWaldman2025" class="citation news cs1">Waldman, Annie (June 17, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.propublica.org/article/trump-nih-grant-terminations-illegal" class="external text" id="mwLgI">"Federal Judge Deems Trump Administration's Termination of NIH Grants Illegal"</a>. <i id="mwLgM">ProPublica</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLgQ">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLgU">August 16,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=ProPublica&amp;rft.atitle=Federal+Judge+Deems+Trump+Administration%27s+Termination+of+NIH+Grants+Illegal&amp;rft.date=2025-06-17&amp;rft.aulast=Waldman&amp;rft.aufirst=Annie&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.propublica.org%2Farticle%2Ftrump-nih-grant-terminations-illegal&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLgY"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-648" id="cite_note-648" data-mw-footnote-number="646"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLgc"><a href="#cite_ref-648" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLgg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLgk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-648" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2340" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLgo" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFTouchberry2025" class="citation news cs1">Touchberry, Ramsay (August 9, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/senate/3495365/trump-spending-freezes-quiet-pushback-senate-republicans/" class="external text" id="mwLgs">"Trump spending freezes spur quiet pushback from Senate Republicans"</a>. <i id="mwLgw">The Washington Examiner</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLg0">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLg4">August 16,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLg8">The Government Accountability Office, a congressional watchdog, has repeatedly ruled that canceled or delayed funding for biomedical research, K-12 education, and more is illegal and runs afoul of the Impoundment Control Act, a federal law regulating when presidents can withhold spending.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Washington+Examiner&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+spending+freezes+spur+quiet+pushback+from+Senate+Republicans&amp;rft.date=2025-08-09&amp;rft.aulast=Touchberry&amp;rft.aufirst=Ramsay&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonexaminer.com%2Fnews%2Fsenate%2F3495365%2Ftrump-spending-freezes-quiet-pushback-senate-republicans%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLhA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-649" id="cite_note-649" data-mw-footnote-number="647"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLhE"><a href="#cite_ref-649" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLhI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLhM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-649" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2345" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLhQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFStelter2026" class="citation news cs1"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Stelter" title="Brian Stelter" id="mwLhU">Stelter, Brian</a> (March 31, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/03/31/media/federal-judge-trump-order-npr-pbs-funding" class="external text" id="mwLhY">"Federal judge rules Trump order ending NPR and PBS funding was unconstitutional"</a>. <i id="mwLhc">CNN</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLhg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLhk">May 26,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=CNN&amp;rft.atitle=Federal+judge+rules+Trump+order+ending+NPR+and+PBS+funding+was+unconstitutional&amp;rft.date=2026-03-31&amp;rft.aulast=Stelter&amp;rft.aufirst=Brian&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnn.com%2F2026%2F03%2F31%2Fmedia%2Ffederal-judge-trump-order-npr-pbs-funding&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLho"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-650" id="cite_note-650" data-mw-footnote-number="648"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLhs"><a href="#cite_ref-650" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLhw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLh0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-650" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><sup about="#mwt2321" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Savage_05232025_644-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Savage 05232025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Savage_05232025-644"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Savage_05232025-644" id="mwLh4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLh8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLiA">[</span>642<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLiE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2326" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025_645-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Sneed 01232025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025-645"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Sneed_01232025-645" id="mwLiI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLiM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLiQ">[</span>643<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLiU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2331" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025_646-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Corruption allegations during the second Trump presidency Lucas 05022025"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025-646"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Lucas_05022025-646" id="mwLiY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLic"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLig">[</span>644<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLik">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2336" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-647" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-647"}}'><a href="#cite_note-647" id="mwLio"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLis"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLiw">[</span>645<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLi0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2341" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-648" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-648"}}'><a href="#cite_note-648" id="mwLi4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLi8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLjA">[</span>646<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLjE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt2346" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-649" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-649"}}'><a href="#cite_note-649" id="mwLjI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLjM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLjQ">[</span>647<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLjU">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025-651" id="cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025-651" data-mw-footnote-number="649"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLjY"><a href="#cite_ref-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025_651-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLjc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLjg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Corruption_allegations_during_the_second_Trump_presidency_Jouvenal_07212025-651" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2364" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLjk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFJouvenal2025" class="citation news cs1">Jouvenal, Justin (July 21, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwLjo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/2025/07/21/trump-court-orders-defy-noncompliance-marshals-judges/" class="external text" id="mwLjs">"Trump officials accused of defying 1 in 3 judges who ruled against him"</a></span>. <i id="mwLjw"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Washington_Post" title="The Washington Post" id="mwLj0">The Washington Post</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLj4">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLj8">August 1,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwLkA">A comprehensive analysis of hundreds of lawsuits against Trump policies shows dozens of examples of defiance, delay and dishonesty, which experts say pose an unprecedented threat to the U.S. legal system. [...] The Post examined 337 lawsuits filed against the administration since Trump returned to the White House and began a rapid-fire effort to reshape government programs and policy. As of mid-July, courts had ruled against the administration in 165 of the lawsuits. The Post found that the administration is accused of defying or frustrating court oversight in 57 of those cases — almost 35 percent. Legal experts said the pattern of conduct is unprecedented for any presidential administration and threatens to undermine the judiciary's role as a check on an executive branch asserting vast powers that test the boundaries of the law and Constitution.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Washington+Post&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+officials+accused+of+defying+1+in+3+judges+who+ruled+against+him&amp;rft.date=2025-07-21&amp;rft.aulast=Jouvenal&amp;rft.aufirst=Justin&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.washingtonpost.com%2Fpolitics%2F2025%2F07%2F21%2Ftrump-court-orders-defy-noncompliance-marshals-judges%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLkE"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-652" id="cite_note-652" data-mw-footnote-number="650"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLkI"><a href="#cite_ref-652" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLkM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLkQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-652" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2369" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLkU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFLiptak2025" class="citation news cs1"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adam_Liptak" title="Adam Liptak" id="mwLkY">Liptak, Adam</a> (March 19, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwLkc"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/19/us/politics/trump-deportations-constitutional-crisis-impeachment.html" class="external text" id="mwLkg">"Defiance and Threats in Deportation Case Renew Fear of Constitutional Crisis"</a></span>. <i id="mwLkk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwLko">The New York Times</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLks">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLkw">March 20,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Defiance+and+Threats+in+Deportation+Case+Renew+Fear+of+Constitutional+Crisis&amp;rft.date=2025-03-19&amp;rft.aulast=Liptak&amp;rft.aufirst=Adam&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F03%2F19%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-deportations-constitutional-crisis-impeachment.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLk0"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-653" id="cite_note-653" data-mw-footnote-number="651"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwLk4"><a href="#cite_ref-653" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwLk8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwLlA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-653" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2374" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwLlE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFLangeErickson2026" class="citation news cs1">Lange, Jason; Erickson, Bo (August 19, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.reuters.com/world/most-americans-believe-trump-has-inappropriately-profited-since-returning-power-2026-08-19/" class="external text" id="mwLlI">"Most Americans believe Trump has inappropriately profited since returning to power, Reuters/Ipsos poll finds"</a>. Reuters<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwLlM">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwLlQ">August 22,</span> 2026</span>. <q id="mwLlU">But experts on presidential ethics called the current confluence of business and politics in the White House unprecedented.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Most+Americans+believe+Trump+has+inappropriately+profited+since+returning+to+power%2C+Reuters%2FIpsos+poll+finds&amp;rft.date=2026-08-19&amp;rft.aulast=Lange&amp;rft.aufirst=Jason&amp;rft.au=Erickson%2C+Bo&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.reuters.com%2Fworld%2Fmost-americans-believe-trump-has-inappropriately-profited-since-returning-power-2026-08-19%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwLlY"></span></span></li>
