<li about="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025-707" id="cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025-707" data-mw-footnote-number="705"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMHI"><a href="#cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025_707-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMHM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMHQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_01272025-707" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2634" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMHU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwMHY" class="citation news cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFBasuLawler2025">Basu, Zachary; Lawler, Dave (January 27, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.axios.com/2025/01/27/trump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general" class="external text" id="mwMHc">"Trump's bureaucracy goes to war"</a>. <i id="mwMHg"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axios_(website)" title="Axios (website)" id="mwMHk">Axios</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMHo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMHs">January 28,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+bureaucracy+goes+to+war&amp;rft.date=2025-01-27&amp;rft.aulast=Basu&amp;rft.aufirst=Zachary&amp;rft.au=Lawler%2C+Dave&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2025%2F01%2F27%2Ftrump-federal-eorkers-inspectors-general&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMHw"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025-708" id="cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025-708" data-mw-footnote-number="706"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMH0"><a href="#cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025_708-0" id="mwMH4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMH8">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025_708-1" id="mwMIA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMIE">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Savage_04302025-708" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2703" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMII" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwMIM" class="citation news cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFSavage2025">Savage, Charlie (April 30, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwMIQ"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/30/us/politics/trump-100-days-president-power-law.html" class="external text" id="mwMIU">"Trump's Maximalist Assertion of Presidential Power Tests the Rule of Law"</a></span>. <i id="mwMIY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times" title="The New York Times" id="mwMIc">The New York Times</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMIg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMIk">May 4,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwMIo">The president, far more than in his first term, has cast aside a post-Watergate norm that the White House should stay out of law enforcement decisions. After years of baselessly accusing Barack Obama and Joseph R. Biden Jr. of directing investigations into him, he has made a reality the very weaponization of the Justice Department he once railed against.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+Maximalist+Assertion+of+Presidential+Power+Tests+the+Rule+of+Law&amp;rft.date=2025-04-30&amp;rft.aulast=Savage&amp;rft.aufirst=Charlie&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2F2025%2F04%2F30%2Fus%2Fpolitics%2Ftrump-100-days-president-power-law.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMIs"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025-709" id="cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025-709" data-mw-footnote-number="707"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMIw"><a href="#cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025_709-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMI0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMI4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Cooper_09062025-709" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2643" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMI8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFCooper2025" class="citation news cs1">Cooper, Jonathan J. (September 6, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://apnews.com/article/trump-weaponizing-government-second-term-54ab244ccb2328d116a498bbaeb680ef" class="external text" id="mwMJA">"How Donald Trump is weaponizing the government to settle personal scores and pursue his agenda"</a>. <i id="mwMJE">The Associated Press</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMJI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMJM">September 7,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Associated+Press&amp;rft.atitle=How+Donald+Trump+is+weaponizing+the+government+to+settle+personal+scores+and+pursue+his+agenda&amp;rft.date=2025-09-06&amp;rft.aulast=Cooper&amp;rft.aufirst=Jonathan+J.&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fapnews.com%2Farticle%2Ftrump-weaponizing-government-second-term-54ab244ccb2328d116a498bbaeb680ef&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMJQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025-710" id="cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025-710" data-mw-footnote-number="708"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMJU"><a href="#cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025_710-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMJY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMJc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Basu_07302025-710" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2648" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMJg" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwMJk" class="citation news cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFBasu2025">Basu, Zachary (July 30, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.axios.com/2025/07/30/trump-harvard-settlement-dei-lawsuit" class="external text" id="mwMJo">"Trump's billion-dollar settlement spree"</a>. <i id="mwMJs">Axios</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMJw">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMJ0">July 30,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwMJ4">America's most elite institutions have largely succumbed to the Trump administration's cultural crackdown, opting to pay up — often to the tune of tens or even hundreds of millions of dollars — rather than fight back.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Axios&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+billion-dollar+settlement+spree&amp;rft.date=2025-07-30&amp;rft.aulast=Basu&amp;rft.aufirst=Zachary&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2025%2F07%2F30%2Ftrump-harvard-settlement-dei-lawsuit&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMJ8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025-711" id="cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025-711" data-mw-footnote-number="709"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMKA"><a href="#cite_ref-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025_711-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMKE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMKI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Targeting_of_political_opponents_and_civil_society_under_the_second_Trump_administration_Lucas_2025-711" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2653" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMKM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="mwMKQ" class="citation episode cs1" data-x-id="CITEREFLucas2025">Lucas, Ryan (March 19, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.npr.org/2025/03/19/nx-s1-5323890/experts-say-trumps-targeting-of-law-firms-is-unprecedented" class="external text" id="mwMKU">"Experts say Trump's targeting of law firms is unprecedented"</a>. <i id="mwMKY"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/All_Things_Considered" title="All Things Considered" id="mwMKc">All Things Considered</a></i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMKg">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMKk">April 13,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=All+Things+Considered&amp;rft.date=2025-03-19&amp;rft.aulast=Lucas&amp;rft.aufirst=Ryan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.npr.org%2F2025%2F03%2F19%2Fnx-s1-5323890%2Fexperts-say-trumps-targeting-of-law-firms-is-unprecedented&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMKo"></span></span></li>
