:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1080%2F1600910X.2025.2481159" class="external text" id="mwMl8">10.1080/1600910X.2025.2481159</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN_(identifier)" title="ISSN (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwMmA">ISSN</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwMmE"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://search.worldcat.org/issn/1600-910X" class="external text" id="mwMmI">1600-910X</a>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Distinktion%3A+Journal+of+Social+Theory&amp;rft.atitle=Trumpism%2C+fascism+and+neoliberalism&amp;rft.volume=27&amp;rft.pages=29-46&amp;rft.date=2025-03-26&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1080%2F1600910X.2025.2481159&amp;rft.issn=1600-910X&amp;rft.aulast=Cox&amp;rft.aufirst=Lloyd&amp;rft.au=O%27Connor%2C+Brendon&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tandfonline.com%2Fdoi%2Ffull%2F10.1080%2F1600910X.2025.2481159&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2807" id="mwMmM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-VDEM_Report_2026-751" id="cite_note-VDEM_Report_2026-751" data-mw-footnote-number="749"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMmQ"><a href="#cite_ref-VDEM_Report_2026_751-0" id="mwMmU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMmY">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-VDEM_Report_2026_751-1" id="mwMmc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMmg">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-VDEM_Report_2026-751" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2817" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMmk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwMmo"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.v-dem.net/documents/75/V-Dem_Institute_Democracy_Report_2026_lowres.pdf" class="external text" id="mwMms">"Democracy Report 2026 / Unraveling The Democratic Era?"</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwMmw">(PDF)</span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/V-Dem_Institute" title="V-Dem Institute" id="mwMm0">V-Dem Institute</a>. March 2026. p.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwMm4"> </span>33 In Focus: Autocratization in the USA. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260320121434/https://www.v-dem.net/documents/75/V-Dem_Institute_Democracy_Report_2026_lowres.pdf" class="external text" id="mwMm8">Archived</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwMnA">(PDF)</span> from the original on March 20, 2026.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Democracy+Report+2026+%2F+Unraveling+The+Democratic+Era%3F&amp;rft.pages=33+In+Focus%3A+Autocratization+in+the+USA&amp;rft.pub=V-Dem+Institute&amp;rft.date=2026-03&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.v-dem.net%2Fdocuments%2F75%2FV-Dem_Institute_Democracy_Report_2026_lowres.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMnE"></span><br id="mwMnI"/>●<span class="nowrap" id="mwMnM"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwMnQ"> </span></span>Raw data presented at: <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2820" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMnU" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwMnY"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.v-dem.net/data_analysis/CountryGraph/" class="external text" id="mwMnc">"Country Graph"</a>. V-Dem Institute. March 2026. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260301172546/https://www.v-dem.net/data_analysis/CountryGraph/" class="external text" id="mwMng">Archived</a> from the original on March 1, 2026.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Country+Graph&amp;rft.pub=V-Dem+Institute&amp;rft.date=2026-03&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.v-dem.net%2Fdata_analysis%2FCountryGraph%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMnk"></span> (Choose "United States of America" and select "Election Democracy Index" and "Liberal Democracy Index".)</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-NYTimes_20260513-752" id="cite_note-NYTimes_20260513-752" data-mw-footnote-number="750"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMno"><a href="#cite_ref-NYTimes_20260513_752-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMns"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMnw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-NYTimes_20260513-752" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2826" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwMn0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFThe_Editorial_Board2026" class="citation news cs1">The Editorial Board (August 20, 2026). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/08/20/opinion/trump-election-interference-democracy.html" class="external text" id="mwMn4">"Trump's Election Meddling Erodes Our Democracy"</a>. <i id="mwMn8">The New York Times</i>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+New+York+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+Election+Meddling+Erodes+Our+Democracy&amp;rft.date=2026-08-20&amp;rft.au=The+Editorial+Board&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nytimes.com%2Finteractive%2F2026%2F08%2F20%2Fopinion%2Ftrump-election-interference-democracy.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" id="mwMoA"></span> The editorial board wrote that "clearest sign that a democracy has died is that a leader and his party make it impossible for their opponents to win an election and hold power".</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-kottke-pagel-753" id="cite_note-kottke-pagel-753" data-mw-footnote-number="751"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMoE"><a href="#cite_ref-kottke-pagel_753-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMoI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMoM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-kottke-pagel-753" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2830" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwMoQ" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" web "},"2":{"wt":"last=Kottke "},"3":{"wt":"first=Jason "},"4":{"wt":"title=The Venn Diagram of Trump&apos;s Authoritarian Actions "},"5":{"wt":"work=kottke.org "},"6":{"wt":"access-date=February 14, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"date=February 14, 2025 "},"8":{"wt":"url=https://kottke.org/25/02/the-venn-diagram-of-trumps-authoritarian-actions"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFKottke2025" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt2830">Kottke, Jason (February 14, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://kottke.org/25/02/the-venn-diagram-of-trumps-authoritarian-actions" class="external text" id="mwMoU">"The Venn Diagram of Trump's Authoritarian Actions"</a>. <i id="mwMoY">kottke.org</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMoc">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMog">February 14,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=kottke.org&amp;rft.atitle=The+Venn+Diagram+of+Trump%27s+Authoritarian+Actions&amp;rft.date=2025-02-14&amp;rft.aulast=Kottke&amp;rft.aufirst=Jason&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fkottke.org%2F25%2F02%2Fthe-venn-diagram-of-trumps-authoritarian-actions&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2830" id="mwMok"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-754" id="cite_note-754" data-mw-footnote-number="752"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMoo"><a href="#cite_ref-754" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMos"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMow">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-754" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2833" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwMo0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last1=Sandbu "},"3":{"wt":"first1=Martin "},"4":{"wt":"title=Donald Trump&apos;s administrative self-coup "},"5":{"wt":"url=https://www.ft.com/content/a221a10a-5ac2-47b6-ba8b-30e18553c181 "},"6":{"wt":"access-date=February 14, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"work=Financial Times "},"8":{"wt":"date=January 30, 2025"},"9":{"wt":"quote=This assault on both Congress&apos;s power of the purse and on the US&apos;s administrative state is as much of a self-coup as was the spurring of insurrectionists on January 6, 2021."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSandbu2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt2833">Sandbu, Martin (January 30, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ft.com/content/a221a10a-5ac2-47b6-ba8b-30e18553c181" class="external text" id="mwMo4">"Donald Trump's administrative self-coup"</a>. <i id="mwMo8">Financial Times</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMpA">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMpE">February 14,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwMpI">This assault on both Congress's power of the purse and on the US's administrative state is as much of a self-coup as was the spurring of insurrectionists on January 6, 2021.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Financial+Times&amp;rft.atitle=Donald+Trump%27s+administrative+self-coup&amp;rft.date=2025-01-30&amp;rft.aulast=Sandbu&amp;rft.aufirst=Martin&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.ft.com%2Fcontent%2Fa221a10a-5ac2-47b6-ba8b-30e18553c181&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2833" id="mwMpM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-755" id="cite_note-755" data-mw-footnote-number="753"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMpQ"><a href="#cite_ref-755" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMpU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMpY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-755" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2836" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwMpc" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last1=Norris "},"3":{"wt":"first1=Alex "},"4":{"wt":"title=Is It a Coup? "},"5":{"wt":"url=https://www.liberalcurrents.com/is-it-a-coup/ "},"6":{"wt":"access-date=February 14, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"work=Liberal Currents "},"8":{"wt":"date=February 13, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"quote=Verdict: Self coup, in-progress, success still unknown"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFNorris2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt2836">Norris, Alex (February 13, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.liberalcurrents.com/is-it-a-coup/" class="external text" id="mwMpg">"Is It a Coup?"</a>. <i id="mwMpk">Liberal Currents</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMpo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMps">February 14,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwMpw">Verdict: Self coup, in-progress, success still unknown</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Liberal+Currents&amp;rft.atitle=Is+It+a+Coup%3F&amp;rft.date=2025-02-13&amp;rft.aulast=Norris&amp;rft.aufirst=Alex&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.liberalcurrents.com%2Fis-it-a-coup%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2836" id="mwMp0"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-756" id="cite_note-756" data-mw-footnote-number="754"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMp4"><a href="#cite_ref-756" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMp8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMqA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-756" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2839" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwMqE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"last1=Morgebesser "},"3":{"wt":"first1=Lee "},"4":{"wt":"title=Why we should be worried about Elon Musk&apos;s siege of the US government "},"5":{"wt":"url=https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/elon-musk-donald-trump-government-state-capture-coup-b2697554.html "},"6":{"wt":"access-date=February 14, 2025 "},"7":{"wt":"work=The Independent "},"8":{"wt":"date=February 13, 2025 "},"9":{"wt":"quote=More accurately, Musk&apos;s siege amounts to a form of &apos;state capture&apos;. This refers to &apos;the appropriation of state resources by political actors for their own ends: either private or political.&apos;"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFMorgebesser2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt2839">Morgebesser, Lee (February 13, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/elon-musk-donald-trump-government-state-capture-coup-b2697554.html" class="external text" id="mwMqI">"Why we should be worried about Elon Musk's siege of the US government"</a>. <i id="mwMqM">The Independent</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwMqQ">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwMqU">February 14,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwMqY">More accurately, Musk's siege amounts to a form of 'state capture'. This refers to 'the appropriation of state resources by political actors for their own ends: either private or political.'<span class="cs1-kern-right" id="mwMqc"></span></q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Independent&amp;rft.atitle=Why+we+should+be+worried+about+Elon+Musk%27s+siege+of+the+US+government&amp;rft.date=2025-02-13&amp;rft.aulast=Morgebesser&amp;rft.aufirst=Lee&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.independent.co.uk%2Fnews%2Fworld%2Famericas%2Fus-politics%2Felon-musk-donald-trump-government-state-capture-coup-b2697554.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2839" id="mwMqg"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ABC,_Trump_supporters_angry,_July_7,_2025-758" id="cite_note-ABC,_Trump_supporters_angry,_July_7,_2025-758" data-mw-footnote-number="755"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMqk"><a href="#cite_ref-ABC,_Trump_supporters_angry,_July_7,_2025_758-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMqo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMqs">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC,_Trump_supporters_angry,_July_7,_2025-758" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/trump-supporters-angry-justice-departments-epstein-memo/story?id=123567461" class="external text" id="mwMqw">"Trump supporters angry over Justice Department's Epstein memo"</a>, <i id="mwMq0">ABC News</i>, July 7, 2025. President Trump said, "Are you still talking about Jeffrey Epstein? This guy's been talked about for years. You're asking. We have Texas, we have this. We have all of the things. And are people still talking about this guy, this creep? That is unbelievable. Do you want to waste the time? And do you feel like answering?"</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ABC_News,_Senate_Republicans,_July_24,_2025-759" id="cite_note-ABC_News,_Senate_Republicans,_July_24,_2025-759" data-mw-footnote-number="756"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMq4"><a href="#cite_ref-ABC_News,_Senate_Republicans,_July_24,_2025_759-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMq8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMrA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ABC_News,_Senate_Republicans,_July_24,_2025-759" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2862" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwMrE" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite ","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":" news "},"2":{"wt":"date=July 24, 2025 "},"3":{"wt":"title=&apos;Get it all out&apos;: Senate Republicans grapple with Epstein case amid reports on Trump ties "},"4":{"wt":"url=https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/senate-gop-grapple-epstein-case-amid-reports-trump/story?id=124040159 "},"5":{"wt":"work=ABC News "}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt2862" id="mwMrI"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://abcnews.go.com/Politics/senate-gop-grapple-epstein-case-amid-reports-trump/story?id=124040159" class="external text" id="mwMrM">"<span class="cs1-kern-left" id="mwMrQ"></span>'Get it all out': Senate Republicans grapple with Epstein case amid reports on Trump ties"</a>. <i id="mwMrU">ABC News</i>. July 24, 2025.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=ABC+News&amp;rft.atitle=%27Get+it+all+out%27%3A+Senate+Republicans+grapple+with+Epstein+case+amid+reports+on+Trump+ties&amp;rft.date=2025-07-24&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fabcnews.go.com%2FPolitics%2Fsenate-gop-grapple-epstein-case-amid-reports-trump%2Fstory%3Fid%3D1240