<li about="#cite_note-775" id="cite_note-775" data-mw-footnote-number="772"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwMz0"><a href="#cite_ref-775" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwMz4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwMz8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-775" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2919" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwM0A" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"news"},"2":{"wt":"last=Brenan"},"3":{"wt":"first=Megan"},"4":{"wt":"date=July 24, 2025"},"5":{"wt":"title=Independents Drive Trump&apos;s Approval to 37% Second-Term Low"},"6":{"wt":"work=Gallup"},"7":{"wt":"url=https://news.gallup.com/poll/692879/independents-drive-trump-approval-second-term-low.aspx"},"8":{"wt":"url-access=subscription"},"9":{"wt":"access-date=August 16, 2025"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwM0E" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt2919" data-x-id="CITEREFBrenan2025">Brenan, Megan (July 24, 2025). <span class="id-lock-subscription" title="Paid subscription required" id="mwM0I"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://news.gallup.com/poll/692879/independents-drive-trump-approval-second-term-low.aspx" class="external text" id="mwM0M">"Independents Drive Trump's Approval to 37% Second-Term Low"</a></span>. <i id="mwM0Q">Gallup</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwM0U">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwM0Y">August 16,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Gallup&amp;rft.atitle=Independents+Drive+Trump%27s+Approval+to+37%25+Second-Term+Low&amp;rft.date=2025-07-24&amp;rft.aulast=Brenan&amp;rft.aufirst=Megan&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fnews.gallup.com%2Fpoll%2F692879%2Findependents-drive-trump-approval-second-term-low.aspx&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2919" id="mwM0c"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-776" id="cite_note-776" data-mw-footnote-number="773"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwM0g"><a href="#cite_ref-776" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwM0k"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwM0o">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-776" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2922" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwM0s" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"news"},"2":{"wt":"last=Palmer"},"3":{"wt":"first=Kathryn"},"4":{"wt":"date=August 15, 2025"},"5":{"wt":"title=Trump approval rating round-up: Where does president stand in recent polls?"},"6":{"wt":"work=USA Today"},"7":{"wt":"url=https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2025/08/15/trump-approval-rating-polls/85663008007/"},"8":{"wt":"access-date=August 16, 2025"},"9":{"wt":"quote=It&apos;s the latest in a string of national surveys released in the past month giving Trump record-low numbers, following a 37% approval from a July 7–21 Gallup poll and a 40% approval rating from a Reuters/Ispos poll at the end of the month. A historical analysis by Gallup shows Trump&apos;s approval ratings in the first July of both of his terms are lower than those of any other modern president."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFPalmer2025" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt2922">Palmer, Kathryn (August 15, 2025). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/2025/08/15/trump-approval-rating-polls/85663008007/" class="external text" id="mwM0w">"Trump approval rating round-up: Where does president stand in recent polls?"</a>. <i id="mwM00">USA Today</i><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwM04">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwM08">August 16,</span> 2025</span>. <q id="mwM1A">It's the latest in a string of national surveys released in the past month giving Trump record-low numbers, following a 37% approval from a July 7–21 Gallup poll and a 40% approval rating from a Reuters/Ispos poll at the end of the month. A historical analysis by Gallup shows Trump's approval ratings in the first July of both of his terms are lower than those of any other modern president.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=USA+Today&amp;rft.atitle=Trump+approval+rating+round-up%3A+Where+does+president+stand+in+recent+polls%3F&amp;rft.date=2025-08-15&amp;rft.aulast=Palmer&amp;rft.aufirst=Kathryn&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.usatoday.com%2Fstory%2Fnews%2Fpolitics%2F2025%2F08%2F15%2Ftrump-approval-rating-polls%2F85663008007%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2922" id="mwM1E"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-777" id="cite_note-777" data-mw-footnote-number="774"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwM1I"><a href="#cite_ref-777" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwM1M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwM1Q">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-777" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt2925" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwM1U" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"#invoke:cite","function":"invoke"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"web"},"2":{"wt":"url= https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/trumps-approval-rating-is-incredibly-steady-is-that-weird-or-the-new-normal/"},"3":{"wt":"archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20190328153703/https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/trumps-approval-rating-is-incredibly-steady-is-that-weird-or-the-new-normal/"},"4":{"wt":"url-status= dead"},"5":{"wt":"archive-date= March 28, 2019"},"6":{"wt":"title=Trump&apos;s Approval Rating Is Incredibly Steady. Is That Weird Or The New Normal?"},"7":{"wt":"work=[[FiveThirtyEight]]"},"8":{"wt":"date=March 28, 2019"},"9":{"wt":"accessdate=February 3, 2026"},"10":{"wt":"last=Skelley"},"11":{"wt":"first=Geoffrey"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFSkelley2019" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt2925">Skelley, Geoffrey (March 28, 2019). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20190328153703/https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/trumps-approval-rating-is-incredibly-steady-is-that-weird-or-the-new-normal/" class="external text" id="mwM1Y">"Trump's Approval Rating Is Incredibly Steady. Is That Weird Or The New Normal?"</a>. <i id="mwM1c"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FiveThirtyEight" title="FiveThirtyEight" id="mwM1g">FiveThirtyEight</a></i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://fivethirtyeight.com/features/trumps-approval-rating-is-incredibly-steady-is-that-weird-or-the-new-normal/" class="external text" id="mwM1k">the original</a> on March 28, 2019<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwM1o">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwM1s">February 3,</span> 2026</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=FiveThirtyEight&amp;rft.atitle=Trump%27s+Approval+Rating+Is+Incredibly+Steady.+Is+That+Weird+Or+The+New+Normal%3F&amp;rft.date=2019-03-28&amp;rft.aulast=Skelley&amp;rft.aufirst=Geoffrey&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Ffivethirtyeight.com%2Ffeatures%2Ftrumps-approval-rating-is-incredibly-steady-is-that-weird-or-the-new-normal%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3ASecond+presidency+of+Donald+Trump" class="Z3988" about="#mwt2925" id="mwM1w"></span></span></li>
